613>>>>>>>>>>>>>// constants for RGB color schemes NOTE: these are for backwards compatibility - do not use them!
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>// The following symbols mirror the "System-Colors" of Windows and
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>// can be used wherever a RGB value is expected
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>// In VDF a rgb system color is recognized by setting the hi bit
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>// to true and passing the windows system color constant in the lower
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>// bytes. for example: ColorButtonFace in WinUser is $0F. In VDF you can
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>// set the color by setting the value $8000000F.
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>//     Set Color to $8000000F   or Set Color to clBtnFace
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>// VDF will do the system color conversion. It will also recognize that
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>// this is a system color and change the color if the system colors change.
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  If you were using any of these in the past you will now get different
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  values. You should be able to use them as before, but the actual value
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  is different. If you want to get the actual rgb color for this, use the
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  following: Move (GetSysColor(clName IAND $FFFFFF))
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  Note that these are better values for setting colors because they
613>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  will change if the system colors are changed.
