1180>>>>>>>>>//     This function shows the error message for the system error codes
1180>>>>>>>>>//     returned by GetLastError and returns the error code or NO_ERROR.
1180>>>>>>>>>Function ShowLastError Global Returns Integer
1182>>>>>>>>>    Integer iError iFlags iChars iResult
1182>>>>>>>>>    Pointer pAddress
1182>>>>>>>>>    WString sBuffer
1182>>>>>>>>>    
1182>>>>>>>>>    // Get the system error code
1182>>>>>>>>>    Move (GetLastError()) to iError
1183>>>>>>>>>    If (iError = NO_ERROR) ;        Function_Return NO_ERROR
1186>>>>>>>>>    
1186>>>>>>>>>    // Initialize pAddress, just to make sure AddressOf() works
1186>>>>>>>>>    Move 0 to pAddress
1187>>>>>>>>>    
1187>>>>>>>>>    // Set the flags...
1187>>>>>>>>>    Move (FORMAT_MESSAGE_ALLOCATE_BUFFER ior FORMAT_MESSAGE_FROM_SYSTEM ior FORMAT_MESSAGE_IGNORE_INSERTS) to iFlags
1188>>>>>>>>>    
1188>>>>>>>>>    // If FormatMessage fails iBytes will be 0, therefore no bytes will be copied and the error will only
1188>>>>>>>>>    // display the error code returned from GetLastError...
1188>>>>>>>>>    Move (FormatMessageW(iFlags,0,iError,0,AddressOf(pAddress),0,0)) to iChars
1189>>>>>>>>>    
1189>>>>>>>>>    // Allocate the buffer...
1189>>>>>>>>>    Move (Repeat(Character(0),iChars)) to sBuffer
1190>>>>>>>>>    If (iChars > 0) ;        Move (CopyMemory(AddressOf(sBuffer),pAddress,iChars * 2)) to iResult
1193>>>>>>>>>    
1193>>>>>>>>>    // Display the error code and message, if no message is available use 'No error text available'.
1193>>>>>>>>>    If (Trim(sBuffer) = "") ;        Move C_$NoErrorTextAvailable to sBuffer
1196>>>>>>>>>    Error DFERR_WINDOWS ("("+String(iError)+") "+sBuffer)
1197>>>>>>>>>>
1197>>>>>>>>>    
1197>>>>>>>>>    // Free memory used by the buffer...
1197>>>>>>>>>    Move (Free(pAddress)) to iResult
1198>>>>>>>>>    Function_Return iError
1199>>>>>>>>>End_Function
1200>>>>>>>>>
1200>>>>>>>>>//     global returns the size of the screen
1200>>>>>>>>>// If eMode is 0 or no argument is passed, return actual screen size
1200>>>>>>>>>// if eMode is 1, return workspace size. (adjusted for Taskbar)
1200>>>>>>>>>Function GUIScreen_Size Global Integer eMode Returns Integer
1202>>>>>>>>>    Integer iTop iLeft iRight iBottom bSuccess iHeight iWidth iSize
1202>>>>>>>>>    String  sRect
1202>>>>>>>>>    Pointer lpsRect
1202>>>>>>>>>    // if no arguments passed or it is 0, get full screen.
1202>>>>>>>>>    If (Num_arguments=0 or eMode=0) ;        Function_Return (GetSystemMetrics(SM_CYSCREEN)*65536 + ;        GetSystemMetrics(SM_CXSCREEN) )
1205>>>>>>>>>    
1205>>>>>>>>>    // This is a replacement for the GUIScreen_Size. The normal function uses the
1205>>>>>>>>>    // GetSystemMetrics to get the workable screensize. The systemmetric API call doesn't
1205>>>>>>>>>    // care about the size of your taskbar. The result of this is that panels that
1205>>>>>>>>>    // are auto_located on your screen suddenly run off the screen even with plenty of
1205>>>>>>>>>    // space around them.
1205>>>>>>>>>    // (Contributed by Wil van Antwerpen)
1205>>>>>>>>>    tWinRect Rect
1205>>>>>>>>>    tWinRect Rect
1205>>>>>>>>>    Move (SystemParametersInfo(SPI_GETWORKAREA, 0, AddressOf(Rect), 0)) to bSuccess
1206>>>>>>>>>    If bSuccess Begin
1208>>>>>>>>>        Move (rect.bottom - Rect.top) to iHeight
1209>>>>>>>>>        Move (Rect.right - Rect.left) to iWidth
1210>>>>>>>>>    End
1210>>>>>>>>>>
1210>>>>>>>>>    Function_Return  ((iHeight*65536) + iWidth)
1211>>>>>>>>>    
1211>>>>>>>>>End_Function
1212>>>>>>>>>
1212>>>>>>>>>// Convert String to Oem->Ansi or Ansi->Oem: Pass bToAnsi to determine convserion
1212>>>>>>>>>// This will convert both DF Strings and C Strings (zero terminated). If passed a
1212>>>>>>>>>// Cstring it will return a string with a terminating zero. If passed a DFstring
1212>>>>>>>>>// the terminating zero is not returned.
1212>>>>>>>>>// This function is used by ToAnsi and ToOEM. Developers are encouraged to use
1212>>>>>>>>>// these two functions
1212>>>>>>>>>
1212>>>>>>>>>Function gConvertChar Global Integer bToAnsi String sString Returns String
1214>>>>>>>>>    Pointer psString
1214>>>>>>>>>    Integer iVoid bIsCString
1214>>>>>>>>>    If (sString = "") ;        Function_Return sString
1217>>>>>>>>>    
1217>>>>>>>>>    Move (ascii(Right(sString,1))=0) to bIsCString
1218>>>>>>>>>    If not bISCString ;        Append sString (character(0))
