2686>>>>>// Redefine Exit-application behaviors so that:
2686>>>>>//
2686>>>>>// 1. Exit_Application is always delegated to the desktop
2686>>>>>// 2. From desktop it gets exit_system_confirmation
2686>>>>>// 3. Exit_system_confirmation Broadcasts verify_exit_application and
2686>>>>>//    if successful broadcasts Notify_Exit_application (these will be
2686>>>>>//    (received by main_panels to do with what they want).
2686>>>>>//
2686>>>>>Function Desktop_Verify_Exit_Application for cDesktop Returns Integer
2688>>>>>    Integer Fail
2688>>>>>    Broadcast Get Broadcast_Verify_Exit_Application to Fail
2690>>>>>    Function_Return Fail
2691>>>>>End_Function
2692>>>>>
2692>>>>>Procedure Desktop_Notify_Exit_Application for cDesktop
2694>>>>>    Broadcast Send Broadcast_Notify_Exit_Application
2696>>>>>End_Procedure
2697>>>>>
2697>>>>>Function Exit_System_Confirmation for cDesktop Returns Integer
2699>>>>>    Integer Fail
2699>>>>>    Get Desktop_Verify_Exit_Application of desktop to Fail
2700>>>>>    If not Fail ;        Send Desktop_Notify_Exit_Application to desktop
2703>>>>>    Function_Return (not(Fail))
2704>>>>>End_Function
2705>>>>>
2705>>>>>// We want this to delegate right up to Desktop object. So create for cObject that
2705>>>>>// simply delegates and a for cDesktop, that does that actual work
2705>>>>>
2705>>>>>Procedure Exit_Application for cObject
2707>>>>>    Delegate Send Exit_Application
2709>>>>>End_Procedure
2710>>>>>
2710>>>>>Procedure Exit_Application for cDesktop
2712>>>>>    If (Exit_System_Confirmation(Self)) ;        Abort
2715>>>>>End_Procedure
