2716>>>>>//  Take the last key processed by the Key message and return
2716>>>>>//  its ANSI value. Returns 0, if a non-printable character (e.g. F1).
2716>>>>>//  This should normally only get called within a Key message handler
2716>>>>>Function VKeyAscii for cUIObject Returns Integer
2718>>>>>    Integer vkCode
2718>>>>>    Integer iShift iCapsLock
2718>>>>>    Integer iCh
2718>>>>>    Get virtual_key to vkcode
2719>>>>>    Get shift_state to iShift // this has Key_Alt, Key_Shift and Key_Ctrl
2720>>>>>    Get_Key_State VK_CAPITAL to iCapslock  // is the capslock key currently depressed?
2721>>>>>    Move (To_Ascii( vkCode, (iShift iand KEY_SHIFT<>0), (iCapslock=1))) to iCh
2722>>>>>    Function_Return iCh
2723>>>>>End_Function
2724>>>>>
2724>>>>>Function AnsiKey for cUIObject Returns Integer
2726>>>>>    Function_Return (VKeyAscii(Self))
2727>>>>>End_Function
2728>>>>>
2728>>>>>Function OemKey for cUIObject Returns Integer
2730>>>>>    Function_Return (VKeyAscii(Self))
2731>>>>>End_Function
2732>>>>>
2732>>>>>//  Take the last key processed by the Key message and return
2732>>>>>//  its DF value. If a printable character it returns the unicode charcode value. If
2732>>>>>//  a special key (f1, Key_save, etc.) returns the DF name of this key.
2732>>>>>//
2732>>>>>Function DFKey  for cUIObject Integer iKey Returns Integer
2734>>>>>    Integer iCh
2734>>>>>    Get VKeyAscii to iCh
2735>>>>>    // if non-zero return OEM char value, If zero return the DF value (which is passed)
2735>>>>>    // first stripping off the shift bits. The passed key would be the key sent by the
2735>>>>>    // Key message.
2735>>>>>    Function_Return (If(ich, iCh, (iKey iand $F1FF))) // $F1FF= Not (Key_Shift+Key_Alt+Key_Ctrl)
2736>>>>>End_Function
