2763>>>>>
2763>>>>>//
2763>>>>>// This mixin is used by single item and no item objects for shadow
2763>>>>>// support.
2763>>>>>//
2763>>>>>// Note that an object supports three levels of shadowing. A single item
2763>>>>>// can be shadowed (if applicable), an object can be explicitly shadowed
2763>>>>>// or an object can be indirectly shadowed by a parent.
2763>>>>>//
2763>>>>>// Public Interface:
2763>>>>>//
2763>>>>>//  Get/Set Object_Shadow_State   Sets the object's explicit SS.
2763>>>>>//                                Gets object's explicit IOR Implicit SS
2763>>>>>//  Get/Set Item_Shadow_State     (if items are applicable)
2763>>>>>//  Get     Implicit_Shadow_State  if shadowed as group by ancestor
2763>>>>>//  Get     Explicit_Shadow_State  if shadowed by self
2763>>>>>//  Get     Implicit_Hidden_State  if hidden by an active parent (like a parent tab page)
2763>>>>>//  Send    Shadow_Display
2763>>>>>//
2763>>>>>//  Get/Set Shadow_State          (if item based, sets item, else object)
2763>>>>>// An object is shadowed if it is explicitly or implicitly shadowed. We now have two flavors of
2763>>>>>// implicit. Either shadowed by a parent or hidden by a parent (e.g. parent tab page). If shadowed under
2763>>>>>// any of these conditions the physical shadow_state must be true so that navigation skips it.
2763>>>>>
2763>>>>>Class Shadow_Mixin is a Mixin
2764>>>>>    
2764>>>>>    Procedure Define_Shadow_Mixin
2766>>>>>        // Should child objects receive shadow notification?
2766>>>>>        Property Integer Broadcast_Implicit_Shadow_State False
2767>>>>>        
2767>>>>>        Property Integer Private.Explicit_Shadow_State  False
2768>>>>>        
2768>>>>>        Property Integer Private.Implicit_Shadow_State  False
2769>>>>>        
2769>>>>>        Property Integer Private.Implicit_Hidden_State  False // PRIVATE
2770>>>>>        
2770>>>>>        // will be used by objects that have no runtime shadow_state
2770>>>>>        // item property (edits and containers)
2770>>>>>        //
2770>>>>>        Property Integer Private.Shadow_State           False
2771>>>>>    End_Procedure
2772>>>>>    
2772>>>>>    Register_Function Object_Shadow_State Returns Integer
2772>>>>>    
2772>>>>>    // Returns true if the object is shadowed as part of a group shadow.
2772>>>>>    //
2772>>>>>    Function Implicit_Shadow_State Returns Boolean
2774>>>>>        Function_Return (Private.Implicit_Shadow_State(Self))
2775>>>>>    End_Function
2776>>>>>    
2776>>>>>    // Returns true if the object is explicitly shadowed by self
2776>>>>>    //
2776>>>>>    Function Explicit_Shadow_State Returns Boolean
2778>>>>>        Function_Return (Private.Explicit_Shadow_State(Self))
2779>>>>>    End_Function
2780>>>>>    
2780>>>>>    // Returns true if the object is active but hidden (like a child of a tab page)
2780>>>>>    Function Implicit_Hidden_state Returns Integer
2782>>>>>        Function_Return (Active_State(Self) and Private.Implicit_Hidden_State(Self))
2783>>>>>    End_Function
2784>>>>>    
2784>>>>>    //  Private: Should only be sent by an ancestor object which is
2784>>>>>    //  notifying all descendants that they have been shadowed as part
2784>>>>>    //  of a group
2784>>>>>    //
2784>>>>>    Procedure Set Implicit_Shadow_State Integer iState
2786>>>>>        Set Private.Implicit_Shadow_State to iState // store group shadow status
2787>>>>>        // If the object is explicitly shadowed by the object we don't do anything
2787>>>>>        // because if state=T it is already shadowed (nothing to do) and if
2787>>>>>        // state=F we don't want to unshadow this one anyway
2787>>>>>        If not (Explicit_Shadow_State(Self)) Begin
2789>>>>>            Set Current_Shadow_State to iState
2790>>>>>            Send Shadow_display
2791>>>>>            If (Broadcast_Implicit_Shadow_State(Self)) ;                Broadcast Set Implicit_Shadow_State to iState
2795>>>>>        End
2795>>>>>>
2795>>>>>    End_Procedure
2796>>>>>    
2796>>>>>    // private. This sets implicit shadowing for child objects within a tab page. This is similar to
2796>>>>>    // Implicit_shadow_state except that it should not send shadow_display. Shadowing
2796>>>>>    // and unShadowing causes color side effects (unshadow ignores the old background color) so when shadowing
2796>>>>>    // for tab children (which you will never see) we just do nothing. Set the implicit shadowing is still needed
2796>>>>>    // to make the navigation work properly.
2796>>>>>    
2796>>>>>    Procedure DoImplicitTabHide Integer iState
2798>>>>>        Set Private.Implicit_Hidden_State to iState // = hidden by a parent
2799>>>>>        // broadcast so all private hidden states are correct
2799>>>>>        Broadcast Send DoImplicitTabHide iState // change here
2801>>>>>    End_Procedure
2802>>>>>    
2802>>>>>    Procedure Set Object_Shadow_State Integer iState
2804>>>>>        // If explictly shadowed, nothing to do. It's already shadowed
2804>>>>>        If (Explicit_Shadow_state(Self)=iState) ;            Procedure_Return
2807>>>>>        Set Private.Explicit_Shadow_State to iState
2808>>>>>        // If not implicitly shadowed skip....
2808>>>>>        If not (Implicit_Shadow_State(Self)) Begin
2810>>>>>            Set Current_Shadow_State to iState
2811>>>>>            Send Shadow_display
2812>>>>>            If (Broadcast_Implicit_Shadow_State(Self)) ;                Broadcast Set Implicit_Shadow_State to iState
2816>>>>>        End
2816>>>>>>
2816>>>>>    End_Procedure
2817>>>>>    
2817>>>>>    
2817>>>>>    Procedure Shadow_Display
2819>>>>>    End_Procedure
2820>>>>>    
2820>>>>>    // Item_shadow_state always gets the item's SS
2820>>>>>    //
2820>>>>>    Procedure Set Item_Shadow_State Integer iItem Integer iState
2822>>>>>        Forward Set Shadow_State iItem to iState
2824>>>>>    End_Procedure
2825>>>>>    
2825>>>>>    Function Item_Shadow_State Integer iItem Returns Integer
2827>>>>>        Integer iState
2827>>>>>        Forward Get Shadow_State iItem to iState
2829>>>>>        Function_Return iState
2830>>>>>    End_Function
2831>>>>>    
2831>>>>>    //  Current_Shadow_State sets the object's true shadow-state
2831>>>>>    //  With single item objects we use
2831>>>>>    //  the shadow_state of item 0 (the only item) to let store this
2831>>>>>    //  information. In multi-item this must be replaced (see multi-item below)
2831>>>>>    //  This is for the single item model
2831>>>>>    //
2831>>>>>    Procedure Set Current_Shadow_State Integer iState
2833>>>>>        Set Item_Shadow_State 0 to iState
2834>>>>>    End_Procedure
2835>>>>>    
2835>>>>>    // This returns if the object is truly shadowed. In single item we
2835>>>>>    // use item 0
2835>>>>>    //
2835>>>>>    Function Object_Shadow_State Returns Integer
2837>>>>>        Function_Return (Item_shadow_State(Self,0))
2838>>>>>    End_Function
2839>>>>>    
2839>>>>>    //  Enabled_State, for this rev, simply calls Object_Shadow_State but
2839>>>>>    //  inverts the parameter logic because Enabled_State is "enable centric"
2839>>>>>    //  vs. Shadow_State which is "disable centric"
2839>>>>>    //
2839>>>>>    Procedure Set Enabled_State Integer bState
2841>>>>>        Set Object_Shadow_State to (not(bState))
2842>>>>>    End_Procedure
2843>>>>>    
2843>>>>>    //  Again, we're calling upon Object_Shadow_State and simply inverting
2843>>>>>    //  the return value to match the context of the "enable centric"
2843>>>>>    //  property
2843>>>>>    //
2843>>>>>    Function Enabled_State Returns Integer
2845>>>>>        Function_Return (not(object_shadow_state(Self)))
2846>>>>>    End_Function
2847>>>>>    
2847>>>>>    // Shadow_State can apply either to the object or the item. In single
2847>>>>>    // item or no item objects it refers to the object. In multi-item it
2847>>>>>    // refers to the item. This is the single item model
2847>>>>>    Procedure Set Shadow_State Integer iItem Integer iState
2849>>>>>        Set Object_Shadow_State to iState
2850>>>>>    End_Procedure
2851>>>>>    
2851>>>>>    Function Shadow_State Integer iItem Returns Integer
2853>>>>>        Function_Return (Object_Shadow_State(Self))
2854>>>>>    End_Function
2855>>>>>    
2855>>>>>    
2855>>>>>    // if next or prior object results in a ring it cannot get out of, it calls this
2855>>>>>    // and expects this to return an object ID or 0, to tell what to do
2855>>>>>    Function StuckInRing Integer bDown Returns Handle
2857>>>>>        Handle hoID
2857>>>>>        If (scope_state(Self)) ;            Function_Return 0 // if scope, nothing we can do.
2860>>>>>        If (bDown) ;                             // else, we can try to get out            Get next_object_id 1 to hoId         // of the ring
2863>>>>>        Else ;            Get prior_object_id 1 to hoId
2865>>>>>        Function_Return hoId
2866>>>>>    End_Function
2867>>>>>    
2867>>>>>    
2867>>>>>    Function private.Next_object_id Integer fg Returns Integer
2869>>>>>        Integer hId
2869>>>>>        Forward Get Next_object_id fg to hId
2871>>>>>        Function_Return hId
2872>>>>>    End_Function
2873>>>>>    
2873>>>>>    Function private.prior_object_id Integer fg Returns Integer
2875>>>>>        Integer hId
2875>>>>>        Forward Get prior_object_id fg to hId
2877>>>>>        Function_Return hId
2878>>>>>    End_Function
2879>>>>>    
2879>>>>>    // needed by navigation (next_object_id). If the selected object is a container
2879>>>>>    // it will receive the activate message. If the container already has the focus, it
2879>>>>>    // will not do anything. We need to know if that will be the case. This is augmented
2879>>>>>    // by tab-pages which actually will change the focus when sent activate.
2879>>>>>    //
2879>>>>>    Function ContainerFocusWillNotChange Returns Integer
2881>>>>>        Function_Return (client_area_state(Self) and containsFocus(Self))
2882>>>>>    End_Function
2883>>>>>    
2883>>>>>    Function Prior_Object_Id Integer bNoDescend Returns Integer
2885>>>>>        Handle hoID hoFirst
2885>>>>>        
2885>>>>>        // If object is not if focus tree, we cannot do this. You should never
2885>>>>>        // send this to a non-active object
2885>>>>>        If (not(Active_state(Self))) ;            Function_Return 0
2888>>>>>        
2888>>>>>        If (Implicit_Shadow_State(Self) or Implicit_Hidden_State(Self)) ;            Move 1 to bNoDescend
2891>>>>>        Get Private.Prior_object_id bNoDescend to hoId
2892>>>>>        // Keep track of first object we check. This way if we descend into
2892>>>>>        // a ring we will know it.
2892>>>>>        Move hoId to hoFirst // use to test if we are stuck in a ring
2893>>>>>        While (hoId>Desktop and (Object_Shadow_State(hoId) or Implicit_Hidden_state(hoId) or Focus_mode(hoId)=Pointer_only))
2897>>>>>            If (Implicit_Hidden_State(hoId)) Begin
2899>>>>>                Repeat // if hidden, go up until you find not-hidden item (will be tab page)
2899>>>>>>
2899>>>>>                    Get Prior_level of hoId to hoId
2900>>>>>                Until (hoId<=desktop or Implicit_Hidden_state(hoId)=0)
2902>>>>>            End
2902>>>>>>
2902>>>>>            Else If (Implicit_Shadow_State(hoId)) Begin
2905>>>>>                Repeat // if implicit shadow, go up until it is not shadowed
2905>>>>>>
2905>>>>>                    Get Prior_level of hoId to hoId
2906>>>>>                Until (hoId<=desktop or Implicit_Shadow_state(hoId)=0)
2908>>>>>            End
2908>>>>>>
2908>>>>>            If (hoId>Desktop) ;                Get Private.Prior_Object_Id of hoId 0 to hoId
2911>>>>>            // if back to first object...get out
2911>>>>>            If (hoId=hoFirst) Begin
2913>>>>>                Get ringparent of hoId to hoId
2914>>>>>                If (hoId) ;                    Get StuckInRing of hoId 0 to hoId
2917>>>>>                Function_Return hoId
2918>>>>>            End
2918>>>>>>
2918>>>>>        Loop
2919>>>>>>
2919>>>>>        If (hoID=Self or hoID<=Desktop) ;            Move 0 to hoId
2922>>>>>        Function_Return hoId
2923>>>>>    End_Function
2924>>>>>    
2924>>>>>    Function Next_Object_Id Integer bNoDescend Returns Integer
2926>>>>>        Handle hoID hoFirst
2926>>>>>        Integer iCount
2926>>>>>        // If object is not if focus tree, we cannot do this. You should never
2926>>>>>        // send this to a non-active object
2926>>>>>        If (not(Active_state(Self))) ;            Function_Return 0
2929>>>>>        
2929>>>>>        // Never descend into shadowed objects...there's no point
2929>>>>>        If (bNoDescend=0 and Object_Shadow_State(Self)) ;            Move 1 to bNoDescend
2932>>>>>        Get Private.Next_object_id bNoDescend to hoId
2933>>>>>        Move hoId to hoFirst // use to test if we are stuck in a ring
2934>>>>>        // Loop until we find a valid object. Skip shadowed objects
2934>>>>>        While (hoId>Desktop and (Object_Shadow_State(hoId) or Implicit_hidden_state(Self) or Focus_mode(hoId)=Pointer_only))
2938>>>>>            // if shadowed, get id up one level
2938>>>>>            Get Private.Next_Object_Id of hoId 1 to hoId
2939>>>>>            // if back to first object...get out
2939>>>>>            If (hoId=hoFirst) Begin
2941>>>>>                Get ringparent of hoId to hoId
2942>>>>>                If (hoId) ;                    Get StuckInRing of hoId 1 to hoId
2945>>>>>                Function_Return hoId
2946>>>>>            End
2946>>>>>>
2946>>>>>            Increment iCount
2947>>>>>            If (iCount>5000) Begin
2949>>>>>                Function_Return 0
2950>>>>>            End
2950>>>>>>
2950>>>>>            
2950>>>>>        Loop
2951>>>>>>
2951>>>>>        // If we have a valid next object check to see if it is a container and if it has the focus
2951>>>>>        // If it does, sending activate will do nothing. So we must look inside the container to find
2951>>>>>        // the next focusable object.
2951>>>>>        Move 0 to hoFirst
2952>>>>>        While ( hoID<>Self and hoID>Desktop and ContainerFocusWillNotChange(hoId) and hoId<>hoFirst)
2956>>>>>            // use to test if we are stuck in a loop. This is unlikely, I can not think of any situations
2956>>>>>            // where it might occur, but we should protect against this anyway.
2956>>>>>            Move hoId to hoFirst
2957>>>>>            Get Next_object_id of hoId 0 to hoId
2958>>>>>        Loop
2959>>>>>>
2959>>>>>        If (hoID=Self or hoID<=Desktop) ;            Move 0 to hoId
2962>>>>>        Function_Return hoId
2963>>>>>    End_Function
2964>>>>>    
2964>>>>>    
2964>>>>>    Procedure Top_of_Panel
2966>>>>>        Handle hoFirst
2966>>>>>        // protect against sending this to a non active view
2966>>>>>        If (Active_state(Self)) Begin
2968>>>>>            Get Next_Object_ID 0 to hoFirst
2969>>>>>            If hoFirst Begin
2971>>>>>                If (client_area_state(hoFirst) and containsFocus(hoFirst)) ;                    Send top_of_panel to hoFirst
2974>>>>>                Else ;                    Send activate of hoFirst
2976>>>>>            End
2976>>>>>>
2976>>>>>            Else ;                Send Activate
2978>>>>>        End
2978>>>>>>
2978>>>>>    End_Procedure
2979>>>>>    
2979>>>>>    Procedure Bottom_of_Panel
2981>>>>>        Handle hoLast
2981>>>>>        // protect against sending this to a non active view
2981>>>>>        If (Active_state(Self)) Begin
2983>>>>>            Get next_level to holast
2984>>>>>            If hoLast ;                Get Prior_object_id of hoLast 0 to hoLast
2987>>>>>            If hoLast ;                Send activate of hoLast
2990>>>>>            Else ;                Send Activate
2992>>>>>        End
2992>>>>>>
2992>>>>>    End_Procedure
2993>>>>>    
2993>>>>>    // Move focus to first focusable object in panel
2993>>>>>    // "Panel" is defined as the scope object
2993>>>>>    //
2993>>>>>    Procedure Beginning_of_Panel
2995>>>>>        If (Scope_State(Self)) Begin
2997>>>>>            // you can not send beginning of panel to a non-active view because
2997>>>>>            // it send activate to some object within the (non-active) view
2997>>>>>            If (Active_State(Self)) Begin // if not active, do nothing
2999>>>>>                Send top_of_panel
3000>>>>>                // This sends OnBeginningOfPanel to all objects in panel
3000>>>>>                Send NotifyBeginningOfPanel Self
3001>>>>>            End
3001>>>>>>
3001>>>>>        End
3001>>>>>>
3001>>>>>        Else ; // delegate message to scope object            Delegate Send Beginning_of_Panel
3004>>>>>    End_Procedure
3005>>>>>    
3005>>>>>    
3005>>>>>    Procedure End_of_Panel
3007>>>>>        If (Scope_State(Self)) Begin
3009>>>>>            // you can not send end of panel to a non-active view because
3009>>>>>            // it send activate to some object within the (non-active) view
3009>>>>>            If (Active_State(Self)) ;                Send bottom_of_panel
3012>>>>>        End
3012>>>>>>
3012>>>>>        Else ;            Delegate Send End_of_Panel
3015>>>>>    End_Procedure
3016>>>>>    
3016>>>>>    // When Beginning_of_panel is called all child objects need to be sent the message
3016>>>>>    // OnBeginningOfPanel. This is the private notification process.
3016>>>>>    //
3016>>>>>    Procedure NotifyBeginningOfPanel Integer hoPanel
3018>>>>>        Send OnBeginningOfPanel hoPanel
3019>>>>>        Broadcast Send NotifyBeginningOfPanel hoPanel
3021>>>>>    End_Procedure
3022>>>>>    
3022>>>>>    // Public Event sent to all objects after a Beginning_of_panel is sent
3022>>>>>    //
3022>>>>>    Procedure OnBeginningOfPanel Integer hoPanel
3024>>>>>    End_Procedure
3025>>>>>    
3025>>>>>    
3025>>>>>    Procedure Activate Returns Integer
3027>>>>>        Integer rVal
3027>>>>>        If (active_state(Self) and (Object_Shadow_State(Self) or implicit_hidden_state(Self))) ;            Move 1 to rVal
3030>>>>>        Else ;            Forward Get MSG_Activate to rVal
3033>>>>>        Procedure_Return rVal
3034>>>>>    End_Procedure
3035>>>>>    
3035>>>>>    Procedure Entering Returns Integer
3037>>>>>        Integer rVal
3037>>>>>        // if entering is ok and single item check shadow state of that item.
3037>>>>>        Get Object_Shadow_State to rVal
3038>>>>>        If not rVal ;            Forward Get Msg_Entering to rVal  // Do Normal Entering
3042>>>>>        Procedure_Return rVal
3043>>>>>    End_Procedure
3044>>>>>    
3044>>>>>    //  Activate an object Area. If the object is not in the focus tree
3044>>>>>    //  delegate until a popup object, scoped object, or child of desktop is
3044>>>>>    //  encountered and activate that group. If TakeFocusFg is true, make sure
3044>>>>>    //  this object ends up with the focus. The is similar in logic to
3044>>>>>    //  deactivate area_flag. Used by Validate_Items to make sure a popup
3044>>>>>    //  object or a popup group takes the focus properly.
3044>>>>>    //
3044>>>>>    Procedure Activate_Area Integer TakeFocusFg
3046>>>>>        Integer PopSt
3046>>>>>        Get Popup_State to PopSt
3047>>>>>        // If not in focus tree make sure the entire object area is
3047>>>>>        // added to focus-tree. Treat popup and non-popup the same.
3047>>>>>        
3047>>>>>        // In VDF7 tab controls in tab pages can be active but hidden.
3047>>>>>        // So must be active and not hidden. If active and hidden, it is within a tab page and the
3047>>>>>        // entire page needs repaging.
3047>>>>>        If not (Active_State(Self) and (not(implicit_Hidden_state(Self))) ) Begin
3049>>>>>            If PopSt ;                Send Popup
3052>>>>>            Else If ( Scope_State(Self) or Parent(Self)=DESKTOP ) ;                Send Activate
3056>>>>>            Else ;                Delegate Send Activate_Area False
3059>>>>>        End
3059>>>>>>
3059>>>>>        // make sure this object has the focus if required.
3059>>>>>        If ( TakeFocusFg and Active_State(Self) and ;            Focus(Desktop)<>Self ) Begin
3061>>>>>            If popSt ;                Send Popup
3064>>>>>            Else ;                Send Activate
3066>>>>>        End
3066>>>>>>
3066>>>>>    End_Procedure
3067>>>>>    
3067>>>>>    
3067>>>>>End_Class
3068>>>>>
3068>>>>>// This replaces the message in shadow_mixin. With entry based single item
3068>>>>>// objects you must set the item options for noenter and noput to make
3068>>>>>// shadowing work. However, setting noenter, sends shadow_state which will
3068>>>>>// call this. This allows us to set displayonly fields by sending
3068>>>>>//
3068>>>>>//   Set Object_Shadow_State to T|F
3068>>>>>//
3068>>>>>Class Entry_Shadow_Mixin is a Mixin
3069>>>>>    
3069>>>>>    Procedure Set Object_Shadow_State Integer iState
3071>>>>>        Integer SS bHidden bOldSS
3071>>>>>        
3071>>>>>        // If the object is hidden then this may be getting called when it is not needed.
3071>>>>>        // A DEO refresh will see the shadow_state and think it must be changed. So, if hidden
3071>>>>>        // checkif the explicit SS is already set correctly. If so, do nothing.
3071>>>>>        Get Implicit_Hidden_State to bHidden
3072>>>>>        If (bHidden and Explicit_Shadow_state(Self)=iState) ;            Procedure_Return
3075>>>>>        
3075>>>>>        // if we have an item (we should) we will see if the item
3075>>>>>        // option NOENTER is correct. If not, we will set it Setting this can call
3075>>>>>        // set shadow_state which could cause recursion. So if needed we set shadow-state
3075>>>>>        // first, do the changes, and then reset SS. If SS should really be changed, it will happen
3075>>>>>        // later. This keeps item options and Shadow_state in synch
3075>>>>>        If (Item_Count(Self)) Begin
3077>>>>>            Get Item_Options 0 to SS
3078>>>>>            // We must also check skipfound (since this sets shadow_State) if
3078>>>>>            // this is a skipfound item we assume that it is the skipfound that
3078>>>>>            // is setting the shadow state and we do not change noenter or noput
3078>>>>>            // 16 = SkipFound
3078>>>>>            If ( (SS iand 16)=0) Begin // only check if skipfound is not used
3080>>>>>                // 8 = Noenter
3080>>>>>                Move ( (SS iand 8)<>0 ) to SS // SS = T if NOENTER not set (yet)
3081>>>>>                If (SS <> iState) Begin // if item opt is not what we want, set it
3083>>>>>                    Get Item_Shadow_state 0 to bOldSS // the current item SS
3084>>>>>                    If (bOldSS<>iState) ;                        Set Item_shadow_state  0 to iState
3087>>>>>                    // by setting the item's SS state first (above) we will
3087>>>>>                    // not trigger a change in shadow_state which would cause recursion
3087>>>>>                    // Note that the order matters. NoEnter MUST be first or shadow_state will get sent in C
3087>>>>>                    Set Item_Option 0 NOENTER to iState
3088>>>>>                    Set Item_Option 0 NOPUT   to iState
3089>>>>>                    // if we changed Item-SS we need to set it back.
3089>>>>>                    If (bOldSS<>iState) ;                        Set Item_shadow_state 0 to bOldSS
3092>>>>>                End
3092>>>>>>
3092>>>>>            End
3092>>>>>>
3092>>>>>        End
3092>>>>>>
3092>>>>>        //
3092>>>>>        Set Private.Explicit_Shadow_State to iState
3093>>>>>        If not (Implicit_Shadow_State(Self)) Begin
3095>>>>>            Set Current_Shadow_State to iState
3096>>>>>            Send Shadow_display
3097>>>>>            If (Broadcast_Implicit_Shadow_State(Self)) ;                Broadcast Set Implicit_Shadow_State to iState
3101>>>>>        End
3101>>>>>>
3101>>>>>    End_Procedure
3102>>>>>End_Class
3103>>>>>
3103>>>>>
