4960>>>>>    //
4960>>>>>    Procedure Set Focus Integer hwNewFoc Integer hwOldFoc
4962>>>>>        Forward Set focus to hwNewFoc hwOldFoc
4964>>>>>        Send Notify_Focus_Change True
4965>>>>>    End_Procedure
4966>>>>>    
4966>>>>>    // This fixes an issue in grids where activating a grid whose
4966>>>>>    // item's entry_state is false does not display the dotted outline
4966>>>>>    // if the item is not changed (set current_item not called). This is
4966>>>>>    // a temporary workaround that should be removed as soon as this is
4966>>>>>    // fixed in the runtime. We want to use base class new_item message
4966>>>>>    // which paints the rectangle but does little else. Note the use of
4966>>>>>    // forward send (a technique which is only used as a low level bug fix.
4966>>>>>    // NOTE: This replaces the activate in Shadow_mixin. When this is fixed
4966>>>>>    //       this can be removed. (it duplicates the shadow activate purpose)
4966>>>>>    //
4966>>>>>    Procedure Activate Returns Integer
4968>>>>>        Integer rVal itm
4968>>>>>        If (active_state(Self) and Object_Shadow_State(Self)) ;            Move 1 to rVal
4971>>>>>        Else Begin
4972>>>>>            Forward Get MSG_Activate to rVal
4974>>>>>            If (Rval=0 and item_count(Self)) Begin
4976>>>>>                // if activate is ok and we've got items and entry-state
4976>>>>>                // of the current item is false, force the repaint.
4976>>>>>                Get current_item to itm
4977>>>>>                If not (entry_state(Self,itm)) ;                    Forward Set new_item to itm // !!!!!!! FORWARD !!!!!!!!!
4981>>>>>            End
4981>>>>>>
4981>>>>>        End
4981>>>>>>
4981>>>>>        Procedure_Return rVal
4982>>>>>    End_Procedure
