5644>>>>>    // With entry based objects we can set capslock by setting
5644>>>>>    // the right bit in item_options AND form_Options. We use the
5644>>>>>    // options message instead of the option message because form_
5644>>>>>    // option doesn't seem to work right.
5644>>>>>    //
5644>>>>>    Procedure Set Capslock_State Integer bState
5646>>>>>        Integer iOptions
5646>>>>>        Get Item_Options 0 to iOptions
5647>>>>>        If bState ;            Move (AddBitValue(CAPSLOCK_BIT_VALUE, iOptions)) to iOptions
5650>>>>>        Else ;            Move (RemoveBitValue(CAPSLOCK_BIT_VALUE, iOptions)) to iOptions
5652>>>>>        Set Item_Options 0 to iOptions
5653>>>>>        // must also set form_options. We assume that item and form options
5653>>>>>        // should always be the same and the item_options are the boss. This
5653>>>>>        // is the way the DD handles it.
5653>>>>>        Set form_Options 0 to iOptions
5654>>>>>    End_Procedure
5655>>>>>    
5655>>>>>    // check capslock bit for capslock_state
5655>>>>>    //
5655>>>>>    Function CapsLock_State Returns Integer
5657>>>>>        Integer iOptions
5657>>>>>        Get Item_Options 0 to iOptions
5658>>>>>        Function_Return ( (iOptions iand CAPSLOCK_BIT_VALUE)<>0 )
5659>>>>>    End_Function
