10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10799>>>>>>>>>>>Use DDValtbl.pkg  // validation table classes
Including file: Ddvaltbl.pkg    (C:\Program Files\DataFlex 26.0\Pkg\Ddvaltbl.pkg)
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  Validation Table Support for Extended Data-Sets. Fields may
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  attached to validation tables which can then be used for
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  validation (if Validate_state is true) or list loading.
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  Developers can create their own validation tables as long as they
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  conform to the following external interface:
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Properties
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//   Static_State       - if list must be rebuilt each validation, load
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//   Allow_Blank_state  - If Blank or 0 is a valid response
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//   Validate_State     - should table be used for validation
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//   Table_Loaded_State - is the validation table initialized?
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Methods
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  Get Validate_Value sValue to iVal - if iVal=0, it is legal
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  Send Fill_list                    - fills a static list
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  Send Request_Fill_From_List iObject iMessage
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//        This is a callback that will fill an external list by sending
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//        the passed message (iMessage) back to the requesting object
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//        (iObject). It will send this message for each item in the
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//        validation table. It always passes back four params. Those are:
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//                     iItem - Item count being passed back
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//                     sData - The Database value of the item
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//                     sDesc - The Value's description, "" if none
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//                     iFile - File number associated with the item (if any)
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//                     iRec  - Record associated with the item (if any)
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Developers can create classes of any complexity to support validation
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>// tables. We have provided the following four classes.
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  ValidationTable is an Array
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           Provides simple one dimensional table support. The table must be
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           loaded manually by creating fill_list and sending the message
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           Add_Table_Value (send Add_Table_Value Value). If list is static
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           it is filled once. If non-static it is filled each time it is
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           requested to validate or fill a foreign lis.
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  DescriptionValidationTable is a ValidationTable
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           Provides a more complex three dimension array allowing the
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           object to store a data value, description value and a record
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           number. The developer must fill this list using the Add_table_
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           value message passing up to three values (data, desc, record).
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  FileValidationTable is a DescriptionValidationTable
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           Provides a data aware table. This can be used to load data from
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           data-files, from data-sets. If you use data-sets you can place
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           constraints within the data-set. You must define the file-number,
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           data-set (if any), the file index, the file's data field, and
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           the file's description field. You can also define an optional
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           "Type". All records are constrained to this type (with or with-
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           data-sets). If is assumed that this file has an optimized finding
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           index.
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  CodeValidationTable is a FileValidationTable
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           Used for Code lists. Simply set Type_Value to the "type"
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>Use VDFBase.pkg
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10799>>>>>>>>>>>>>Class ValidationTable is an Array
10800>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10800>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Construct_Object
10802>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Construct_Object
10804>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Static_State        True
10805>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
10805>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Table_Loaded_State  False
10806>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
10806>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Validate_State      True
10807>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Allow_Blank_State   False
10808>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Main_File           0
10809>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property String  Table_Title         DD_VALIDATION_LIST_TITLE
10810>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
10810>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Number_Elements     1
10811>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
10811>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // System maintained. Sub-classes use these
10811>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // These are SET by Next_Code_Record. You may GET their values
10811>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
10811>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property String  Current_Code            ''
10812>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
10812>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property String  Current_Description     ''
10813>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
10813>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property RowID Current_RowId
10814>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
10815>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10815>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Data_Item_Count Returns Integer
10817>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Item_Count(Self))
10818>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
10819>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10819>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Data_Value Integer iItem Returns String
10821>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Value(Self,iItem))
10822>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
10823>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10823>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Data_Value Integer iItem String sValue
10825>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Value  iItem to sValue
10826>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
10827>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10827>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Data_Description Integer iItem Returns String
10829>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return ''
10830>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
10831>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10831>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Data_Description Integer iItem String sValue
10833>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
10834>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10834>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Data_RowId Integer iItem Returns RowID
10836>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (NullRowId())
10837>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
10838>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10838>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Data_RowId Integer iItem RowID riValue
10840>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
10841>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10841>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10841>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Add_Table_Value String sValue
10843>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Data_Value  (Data_Item_Count(Self)) to sValue
10844>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
10845>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10845>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Value String sCode Returns Integer
10847>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
10847>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCnt
10847>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (sCode = '');            Function_Return (not(Allow_Blank_State(Self)))
10850>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Table_Loaded_State(Self)=0 or Static_State(Self)=0) Begin
10852>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Delete_Data
10853>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Fill_list
10854>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Table_Loaded_State to True
10855>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
10855>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10855>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Item_Count to iMax
10856>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
10857>>>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCnt from 0 to iMax
10863>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10863>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (sCode=Data_Value(Self,iCnt)) Begin
10865>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Set Current_Code        to sCode
10866>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Set Current_Description to (Data_Description(Self,iCnt))
10867>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Set Current_RowId       to (Data_RowId(Self,iCnt))
10868>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Function_Return 0
10869>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
10869>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10869>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
10870>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10870>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return 1 // 0=OK
10871>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
10872>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10872>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Find_Code_Description String sCode Returns String
10874>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (sCode='' or ;            (sCode<>Current_Code(Self) and ;            Validate_Value(Self,sCode) ) );            Function_Return ''
10877>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Current_Description(Self))
10878>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
10879>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10879>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10879>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //  The deveveloper (or a sub-class) must fill this list. It is done
10879>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //  by finding the item and sending the Message:
10879>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    Send Add_Table_Value sValue {sDescr}
10879>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
10879>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Fill_List
10881>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Table_Loaded_State to True
10882>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
10883>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10883>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Fill_From_List Integer iObj Integer iMsg
10885>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
10885>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCnt
10885>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
10885>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
10885>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iObj=0 or iMsg=0) ;            Procedure_Return
10888>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
10888>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Table_Loaded_State(Self)=0 or Static_State(Self)=0) Begin
10890>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Delete_Data
10891>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Fill_list
10892>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Table_Loaded_State to True
10893>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
10893>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10893>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iFile
10894>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Item_Count to iMax
10895>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
10896>>>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCnt from 0 to iMax
10902>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10902>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send iMsg to iObj iCnt (Data_Value(Self,iCnt)) ;                (Data_Description(Self,iCnt)) iFile ;                (Data_RowId(Self,iCnt))
10903>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
10904>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10904>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
10905>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10905>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10905>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // returns all data in a two dimension variant array.
10905>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // [i][0] = data
10905>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // [i][1] = description
10905>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This can be used by Crystal CDO classes (this is why a variant array is used)
10905>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function TableData Returns Variant[][]
10907>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Variant[][2] vData
10908>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax i
10908>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Table_Loaded_State(Self)=0 or Static_State(Self)=0) Begin
10910>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Delete_Data
10911>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Fill_list
10912>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Table_Loaded_State to True
10913>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
10913>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10913>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Item_Count to iMax
10914>>>>>>>>>>>>>        For i from 0 to (iMax-1)
10920>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10920>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Value       i to vData[i][0]
10921>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Description i to vData[i][1]
10922>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
10923>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10923>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return vData
10924>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
10925>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10925>>>>>>>>>>>>>End_Class
10926>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10926>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10926>>>>>>>>>>>>>
10926>>>>>>>>>>>>>Class DescriptionValidationTable is an ValidationTable
10927>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10927>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Construct_Object
10929>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Construct_Object
10931>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Number_Elements to 2
10932>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
10933>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
10933>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Data_Item_Count Returns Integer
10935>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (item_count(Self)/3)
10936>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
10937>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
