11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>// This is used by the DataDictionary class and provides a method for
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>// windows DDs (for now) to support local buffers for text and binary buffers.
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Field objects are created within the DD by sending the message:
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>// The DD interface is:
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Get  Field_Object iField to hExtFieldObject
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Send DefineExtendedField iField
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Send DefineAllExtendedFields
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Send ExtendedFieldsUpdate bSave
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Send ExtendedFieldsRefresh bCleared
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Set  File_Field_Current_Pointer_Value iFile iField iLen to pValue
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Set  Field_Current_Pointer_Value iField iLen to pValue
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Set  File_Field_Pointer_Entry iFile iField iLen bShowErr to pValue
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Set  Field_Pointer_Entry iField iOpts iLen bShowErr to pValue
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Get  File_Field_Current_Pointer_Value iFile iField to pData
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Get  Field_Current_Pointer_Value iField to pData
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Once object is identified, the following interface can be used
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Get FieldPointer of hExtFieldObject to iMemoryPointer
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Get FieldLength  of hExtFieldObject to iLen
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Get File_Number  of hExtFieldObject to iFile
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Get Field_Number of hExtFieldObject to iFile
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Set Update_Save_State of hExtFieldObject to bState         // be careful!
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Set Update_Find_State of hExtFieldObject to bState         // be careful
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Set FieldRefresh_Save_State of hExtFieldObject to bState   // be careful
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//  DD structure:
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//       DD Object           (property Field_objects points to child)
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//           FieldObjects    (array of field#s and field objs)
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//              FieldObject1 (heap alloc for each field)
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//              FieldObjectn
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>// This is used to create a single extended field object.
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Interface
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Get FieldPointer to iMemoryPointer
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Get FieldLength  to iLen
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Get File_Number  to iFile
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Get Field_Number to iFile
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      get/Set Update_Save_State to bState         // be careful!
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      get/Set Update_Find_State to bState         // be careful
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      get/Set FieldRefresh_Save_State to bState   // be careful
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      get/set FieldChangedState
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      send defineField  iFile iField
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Send FieldUpdate  bSave
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Send FieldRefresh bCleared bClearFieldChange
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Set  Field_pEntry iOpts iLen to pValue
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//      Set  Field_pValue iLen to pValue
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>Use VDFBase.pkg
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11253>>>>>>>>>>>>>Class FieldObject is a cObject
11254>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11254>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Construct_Object
11256>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send construct_object
11258>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // these are all set by DefineField and should not be changed
11258>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer File_Number        0
11259>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Field_Number       0
11260>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer FieldLength        0
11261>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
11261>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // maintained by object
11261>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property UChar[] pFieldArray
11262>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
11262>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // these can be changed, with care, by the developer
11262>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Update_Save_State  True
11263>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Update_Find_State  False // usually no point for finds
11264>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer FieldRefresh_State True
11265>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
11265>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // hopefully never used
11265>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Pointer pLegacyFieldPointer       0
11266>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
11266>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11267>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11267>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set FieldChangedState Integer bState
11269>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField
11269>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Number to iField
11270>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Set Field_Changed_state iField to bState
11272>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11273>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11273>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function FieldChangedState Returns Integer
11275>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField  bState
11275>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Number to iField
11276>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Changed_state iField to bState
11278>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bState
11279>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11280>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11280>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // return the field option specified
11280>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function IsSaveNoPut Returns Boolean
11282>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField
11282>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean  bState
11282>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Number to iField
11283>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get FieldSaveNoPut iField to bState
11285>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bState
11286>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11287>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11287>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // for object: define file, field, fieldlength and allocate heap memory
11287>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //             and set memory pointer
11287>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DefineField Integer iFile Integer iField
11289>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFldLen
11289>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set File_Number  to iFile
11290>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Field_Number to iField
11291>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_LENGTH of iFile iField to iFldLen
11294>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set FieldLength  to iFldLen
11295>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11296>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11296>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Move from the DD Buffer to the file buffer
11296>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure FieldUpdate Integer bSave
11298>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile iField iFieldLen
11298>>>>>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
11299>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iType
11299>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bNoPut
11299>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
11299>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if bSave, part of save which means only update if changed
11299>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if not bsave, part of find. You usually would not update this. You
11299>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // don't index on these types of fields
11299>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If ( (bSave and Update_Save_State(Self) and FieldChangedState(Self)) or ;            (not(bSave) and Update_Find_state(Self) ) ) Begin
11301>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if save, we must respect DD_NoPut
11301>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (bSave) Begin
11303>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // we are looking at the DD's field buffer itemoptions for, which
11303>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // should be set appropriately before a save. This setting has any
11303>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // changes made to support dd_commit
11303>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Get IsSaveNoPut to bNoPut
11304>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If bNoPut Begin
11306>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Procedure_Return
11307>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
11307>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11307>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11307>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11307>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get pFieldArray to FieldArray
11308>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get File_Number to iFile
11309>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Field_Number to iField
11310>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If iFile Begin
11312>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Set_Field_Value iFile iField to FieldArray // LENGTH iFieldLen
11315>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11315>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11315>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11315>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11315>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11316>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11316>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Move from File buffer to local DD Buffer
11316>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // bCleared determines if this is a find or a clear.
11316>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // bClearFieldChange determines if we should clear the FieldChangedState.
11316>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure FieldRefresh Boolean bCleared Boolean bClearFieldChange
11318>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile iField
11318>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer bOk
11318>>>>>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
11319>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (FieldRefresh_state(Self)) Begin
11321>>>>>>>>>>>>>            //Get FieldPointer to pField
11321>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get File_Number to iFile
11322>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Field_Number to iField
11323>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // move from file buffer to memory pointed to by pField
11323>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iFile) Begin
11325>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If not bCleared Begin
11327>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get_Field_Value iFile iField to FieldArray
11330>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
11330>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11330>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Set Field_UCValue to FieldArray
11331>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11331>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11331>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11331>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11331>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bClearFieldChange Begin
11333>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set FieldChangedstate to False
11334>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11334>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11334>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11335>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11335>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_pEntry Integer iOpts Integer iLen Integer bShowErr Pointer pValue
11337>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile iField iFldLen iMemLen
11337>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer bChanged
11337>>>>>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
11338>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
11338>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // currently we do nothing with bShowErr because we don't checkfor errors!
11338>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
11338>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if No-enter or Displayonly, this shouldn't be changed. For now we will
11338>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // let NoPut through, since a user might need it for finding.
11338>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iOpts iand DD_NOENTER) ;            Procedure_Return
11341>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
11341>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // maybe in the future
11341>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Force a caplsock if required
11341>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //If (iOpts IAND DD_CAPSLOCK) Move (Uppercase(sValue)) to sValue
11341>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
11341>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get File_Number  to iFile
11342>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Number to iField
11343>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iFile) Begin
11345>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Is_pValueChanged iLen pValue to bChanged
11346>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If ( bChanged or (iOpts iand DD_FORCEPUT) ) Begin
11348>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Set Field_pValue iLen to pValue
11349>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11349>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11349>>>>>>>>>>>>>            
11349>>>>>>>>>>>>>            
11349>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // Set changed state if changed and it is not No_put. This
11349>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // is an improvement on DEOs which would set changed-state for
11349>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // a no-put. This way, finds use the changed value but saves will
11349>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // not trigger a phony data loss
11349>>>>>>>>>>>>>            //If ( bChanged ) ;
11349>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If ( bChanged and not(iOpts iand DD_NOPUT) ) ;                Set FieldChangedState to True
11352>>>>>>>>>>>>>            
11352>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // The following is really highly unlikely!!!
11352>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // perform autofinds if needed. Note that required checking will occur as
11352>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // part of validation.
11352>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // We will only autofind if the field value is changed. This is consistent with
11352>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // DEOs which do not autofind on unchanged values. This provides optimizations
11352>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // when a parent record is already loaded.
11352>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (bChanged or FieldChangedState(Self)) Begin
11354>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (iOpts iand DD_AUTOFIND) ;                    Delegate Send File_Field_AutoFind iFile iField EQ
11358>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Else If (iOpts iand DD_AUTOFIND_GE) ;                    Delegate Send File_Field_AutoFind iFile iField GE
11363>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11363>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11363>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11363>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11363>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
11363>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11364>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11364>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // convert pointer to UChar[]
11364>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function PointerToUCharArray Pointer pValue Integer iLen Returns UChar[]
11366>>>>>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
11367>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOk
11367>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (ResizeArray(FieldArray,iLen)) to FieldArray
11368>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (MemCopy(AddressOf(FieldArray),pValue,iLen)) to bOK
11369>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return FieldArray
11370>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11371>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11371>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Raw update of pValue
11371>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_UCValue UChar[] FieldArray
11373>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set pFieldArray to FieldArray
11374>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send DestroyLegacyFieldHeap
11375>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11376>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11376>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Raw update of pValue
11376>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_pValue Integer iLen Pointer pValue
11378>>>>>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
11379>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get PointerToUCharArray pValue iLen to FieldArray
11380>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Field_UCValue to FieldArray
11381>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11382>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11382>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Is_pValueChanged Integer iLen Pointer pValue Returns Boolean
11384>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bChanged
11384>>>>>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
11385>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFldLen
11385>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pFieldArray to FieldArray
11386>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (SizeOfArray(FieldArray)) to iFldLen
11387>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iLen <> SizeOfArray(FieldArray)) Begin
11389>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Move True to bChanged
11390>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11390>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11390>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iLen) Begin // check for empty pointer
11393>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (MemCompare(AddressOf(FieldArray),pValue,iLen)) to bChanged
11394>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11394>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11394>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bChanged
11395>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11396>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11396>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // returns data as UChar array - best way to access the data
11396>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function FieldArray Returns UChar[]
11398>>>>>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
11399>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pFieldArray to FieldArray
11400>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return FieldArray
11401>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11402>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11402>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // legacy method. Hopefully this is never called.
11402>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function FieldPointer Returns Pointer
11404>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Pointer pValue pOldValue
11404>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iLen
11404>>>>>>>>>>>>>        UChar[] FieldArray
11405>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOk
11405>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pFieldArray to FieldArray
11406>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (SizeOfArray(FieldArray)) to iLen
11407>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (Alloc(iLen)) to pValue
11408>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (MemCopy(pValue,AddressOf(FieldArray),iLen)) to bOk
11409>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send DestroyLegacyFieldHeap
11410>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set pLegacyFieldPointer to pValue
11411>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return pValue
11412>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11413>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11413>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DestroyLegacyFieldHeap
11415>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer bOK
11415>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Pointer pField
11415>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pLegacyFieldPointer to pField
11416>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (pField ) Begin
11418>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Free(pField)) to bOk
11419>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set pLegacyFieldPointer to 0
11420>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11420>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11420>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11421>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11421>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // augment to release heap allocation
11421>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Destroy_Object
11423>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send DestroyLegacyFieldHeap
11424>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Destroy_object
11426>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11427>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11427>>>>>>>>>>>>>End_Class
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>// This contains all extended field objects.
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>// The array contains a list of all objects where item=field#
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>// and item+1=field object.
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>// Interface is:
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>//     Get Field_object iField to hFldObj
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>//     Send DefineFieldObject iField
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>//     Send ExtendedFieldsUpdate bSave
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>//     Send ExtendedFieldsRefresh bCleared
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>//
11428>>>>>>>>>>>>>Class FieldObjects is an Array
11429>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11429>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // return object Id for iField. 0 if none.
11429>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_Object Integer iField Returns Integer
11431>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iItm iCnt
11431>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Item_Count to iCnt
11432>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iItm
11433>>>>>>>>>>>>>        While iItm lt iCnt
11437>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Value(Self,iItm)=iField) ;                Function_Return (Value(Self,iItm+1))
11440>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
11441>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
11442>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
11443>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11443>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return 0
11444>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11445>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11445>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // define an extended object for field
11445>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DefineFieldObject Integer iField
11447>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hFld
11447>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCnt  iFile
11447>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bInUse
11447>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bHasRecord
11447>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
11449>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Object iField to hFld // this shouldn't exist yet
11450>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If not hFld Begin
11452>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Create U_FieldObject to hFld
11453>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send DefineField to hFld iFile iField
11454>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Item_Count to iCnt          // add to array
11455>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Value  iCnt to iField   // Pos   = field#
11456>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Value  (iCnt+1) to hFld // Pos+1 = field object
11457>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Get In_Use_State to bInUse
11459>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If bInUse Begin
11461>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Delegate Send Refind_Records
11463>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Delegate Get HasRecord to bHasRecord
11465>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // updating the newly created field with the file buffer contents we don't
11465>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // want to change the field's changed state, which might have been set already.
11465>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send FieldRefresh of hFld (not(bHasRecord)) False
11466>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11466>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11466>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11466>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11466>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11467>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11467>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // update all extended fields. Field buffer <-- DD buffer
11467>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ExtendedFieldsUpdate Integer bSave
11469>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iItm iCnt
11469>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Item_Count to iCnt
11470>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iItm
11471>>>>>>>>>>>>>        While iItm lt iCnt
11475>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
11476>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send FieldUpdate to (Value(Self,iItm)) bSave
11477>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
11478>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
11479>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11479>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11480>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11480>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // refresh all extended fields. Field buffer --> DD buffer
11480>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ExtendedFieldsRefresh Boolean bCleared
11482>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iItm iCnt
11482>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Item_Count to iCnt
11483>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iItm
11484>>>>>>>>>>>>>        While iItm lt iCnt
11488>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
11489>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send FieldRefresh to (Value(Self,iItm)) bCleared True
11490>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Increment iItm
11491>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
11492>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
11492>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11493>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11493>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
11493>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // these are sent from the child field object. We need to direct them
11493>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to the DDO (the parent).
11493>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Changed_State Integer iField Integer bState
11495>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Set Field_Changed_state iField to bState
11497>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11498>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11498>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_Changed_State Integer iField Returns Integer
11500>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer bState
11500>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Changed_state iField to bState
11502>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bState
11503>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11504>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11504>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure File_Field_AutoFind Integer iFile Integer iField Integer iMode
11506>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Send File_field_AutoFind iFile iField iMode
11508>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11509>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11509>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function FieldSaveNoPut Integer iField Returns Boolean
11511>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bIsCommited bNoPut
11511>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get IsCommitted to bIsCommited
11513>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // we don't know if this is foreign or not (DDOs never do by themselves). We
11513>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // will test for regular. This should never be an issue as the DEO itself
11513>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // will be DisplayOnly as needed (we don't have indexed NoEnter=T/Noput=F issues)
11513>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get FieldNoPut iField bIsCommited False to bNoPut
11515>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bNoPut
11516>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11517>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11517>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Destroy_Object
11519>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Set Field_Objects to 0
11521>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Destroy_object
11523>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11524>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11524>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
11524>>>>>>>>>>>>>End_Class
11525>>>>>>>>>>>// for text and binary. Must support Address Type
11525>>>>>>>>>>>
11525>>>>>>>>>>>// we need these from CLI.pkg for DAW drivers. These values must match what is defined
11525>>>>>>>>>>>// in cli.pkg
11525>>>>>>>>>>>Define DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER for 611
11525>>>>>>>>>>>Define DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER_ACTIVE for 624
11525>>>>>>>>>>>Define DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER_EQ for 636
11525>>>>>>>>>>>// same a CLI.pkg DF_FILE_TABLE_NAME but with a different name
11525>>>>>>>>>>>// used to avoid naming conflict. Must match cli.pkg df_file_table_name
11525>>>>>>>>>>>Define DF_FILE_SQL_TABLE_NAME for 609
11525>>>>>>>>>>>
11525>>>>>>>>>>>Define DF_FIELD_SQL_COLUMN_NAME         for 723
11525>>>>>>>>>>>
11525>>>>>>>>>>>Define DF_DATABASE_IDENTIFIER_QUOTE     for 1085
11525>>>>>>>>>>>Define DF_FILE_DATABASE_ID              for 622
11525>>>>>>>>>>>
11525>>>>>>>>>>>// Class helper for SQL/driver assistance.
11525>>>>>>>>>>>// This can only be used within a DataDictionary Class as it expects that
11525>>>>>>>>>>>// certain properties can be Get and Set via delegation.
11525>>>>>>>>>>>Class cDAWSQLDriverHelper is a cObject
11526>>>>>>>>>>>
11526>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DriverIndex String sDriver Returns Integer
11528>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sCurrentDriver
11528>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iNumberOfDrivers iDriver iCount
11528>>>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iDriver
11529>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_NUMBER_DRIVERS to iNumberOfDrivers
11532>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 1 to iNumberOfDrivers
11538>>>>>>>>>>>>
11538>>>>>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute DF_DRIVER_NAME of iCount to sCurrentDriver
11541>>>>>>>>>>>            If ( Uppercase(sCurrentDriver) = Uppercase(sDriver) ) Begin
11543>>>>>>>>>>>                Function_Return iCount
11544>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11544>>>>>>>>>>>>
11544>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
11545>>>>>>>>>>>>
11545>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return 0
11546>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11547>>>>>>>>>>>
11547>>>>>>>>>>>    // returns true if this table supports SQL filter interface
11547>>>>>>>>>>>    Function SupportsSQLFilters Returns Boolean
11549>>>>>>>>>>>        String sDriver
11549>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile iDriver iConformance
11549>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
11551>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_DRIVER of iFile to sDriver
11554>>>>>>>>>>>        Get DriverIndex sDriver to iDriver
11555>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iDriver) Begin
11557>>>>>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute DF_DRIVER_CONFORMANCE of iDriver to iConformance
11560>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11560>>>>>>>>>>>>
11560>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (iConformance iand 4)
11561>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11562>>>>>>>>>>>
11562>>>>>>>>>>>    // SQL Helper functions that return SQL Filters strings that can be used in a where clause
11562>>>>>>>>>>>
11562>>>>>>>>>>>    // Escape character to escape LIKE wildcards
11562>>>>>>>>>>>
11562>>>>>>>>>>>    Function SQLEscapedStr String sSQL Returns String
11564>>>>>>>>>>>        String sEscapedSQL
11564>>>>>>>>>>>        // Replace one single quote by 2 single quotes
11564>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (Replaces("'",sSQL,"''")) to sEscapedSQL
11565>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sEscapedSQL
11566>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11567>>>>>>>>>>>
11567>>>>>>>>>>>    Function SQLEscapeLikeWildcards String sSQL Returns String
11569>>>>>>>>>>>        // Escape the wildcard characters than can be used in a LIKE
11569>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Pos("%",sSQL)) ;            Move (Replaces("%",sSQL,(SQL_LIKE_ESC + "%"))) to sSQL
11572>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Pos("_",sSQL)) ;            Move (Replaces("_",sSQL,(SQL_LIKE_ESC + "_"))) to sSQL
11575>>>>>>>>>>>
11575>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sSQL
11576>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11577>>>>>>>>>>>
11577>>>>>>>>>>>    // Creates an SQL Like Filter for this field and search target
11577>>>>>>>>>>>    Function SQLStrLike Integer iField String sSearch Returns String
11579>>>>>>>>>>>        String sFilter sOrigFilter sField
11579>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
11579>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iHasLikeEscape
11579>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sPrefix
11579>>>>>>>>>>>
11579>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
11581>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get psSQLFilter to sOrigFilter
11583>>>>>>>>>>>        Get SQLStrFieldName iField to sField
11584>>>>>>>>>>>        Get SQLEscapedStr sSearch to sSearch
11585>>>>>>>>>>>
11585>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (Pos(SQL_LIKE_ESC,sSearch)) to iHasLikeEscape
11586>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(iHasLikeEscape)) Begin
11588>>>>>>>>>>>            Get SQLEscapeLikeWildcards sSearch to sSearch
11589>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11589>>>>>>>>>>>>
11589>>>>>>>>>>>
11589>>>>>>>>>>>        // Add the N prefix to properly handle Unicode data
11589>>>>>>>>>>>        Move 'N' to sPrefix
11590>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (sField + " LIKE " + sPrefix + "'%" + sSearch + "%'") to sFilter
11591>>>>>>>>>>>
11591>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(iHasLikeEscape)) Begin
11593>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Pos(SQL_LIKE_ESC,sFilter)) Begin
11595>>>>>>>>>>>                Move (sFilter + " ESCAPE '" + SQL_LIKE_ESC + "' "  ) to sFilter
11596>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11596>>>>>>>>>>>>
11596>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11596>>>>>>>>>>>>
11596>>>>>>>>>>>
11596>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sFilter
11597>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11598>>>>>>>>>>>
11598>>>>>>>>>>>    // Appends two Filters with an AND clause. Both or either can be empty
11598>>>>>>>>>>>    Function SQLStrAppend String sOrigFilter String sFilter Returns String
11600>>>>>>>>>>>        If (sOrigFilter<>"" and sFilter<>"") Begin
11602>>>>>>>>>>>            Move ( "(" + sOrigFilter + ") AND (" + sFilter + ")") to sFilter
11603>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11603>>>>>>>>>>>>
11603>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (sFilter="") Begin
11606>>>>>>>>>>>            Move sOrigFilter to sFilter
11607>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11607>>>>>>>>>>>>
11607>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sFilter
11608>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11609>>>>>>>>>>>
11609>>>>>>>>>>>    // Appends two filters with an or clause. Both or either can be empty.
11609>>>>>>>>>>>    // This may be used in OnConstrain methods when building SQL WHERE clauses in string values.
11609>>>>>>>>>>>    Function SQLStrAppendOr String sOrigFilter String sFilter Returns String
11611>>>>>>>>>>>        If (sOrigFilter<>"" and sFilter<>"") Begin
11613>>>>>>>>>>>            Move ("(" + sOrigFilter + ") OR (" + sFilter + ")") to sFilter
11614>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11614>>>>>>>>>>>>
11614>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (sFilter="") Begin
11617>>>>>>>>>>>            Move sOrigFilter to sFilter
11618>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11618>>>>>>>>>>>>
11618>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return sFilter
11619>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11620>>>>>>>>>>>
11620>>>>>>>>>>>    Function SQLIdentifierQuote Handle hTable Returns String
11622>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sDriver
11622>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iDriverIndex
11622>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle  hDatabase
11622>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sIdentifierQuote
11622>>>>>>>>>>>
11622>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_DRIVER of hTable to sDriver
11625>>>>>>>>>>>
11625>>>>>>>>>>>        Get DriverIndex sDriver to iDriverIndex
11626>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iDriverIndex) Begin
11628>>>>>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute DF_FILE_DATABASE_ID of hTable to hDatabase
11631>>>>>>>>>>>            If (hDatabase) Begin
11633>>>>>>>>>>>                Get_Attribute DF_DATABASE_IDENTIFIER_QUOTE of iDriverIndex hDatabase to sIdentifierQuote
11636>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11636>>>>>>>>>>>>
11636>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11636>>>>>>>>>>>>
11636>>>>>>>>>>>
11636>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sIdentifierQuote
11637>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11638>>>>>>>>>>>
11638>>>>>>>>>>>    // returns the name of the File and Field suitable for an SQL where statement ("Table"."Column")
