11687>>>>>>>>>>>    // called before an SQL Filter find. Make sure that any global and table attributes are
11687>>>>>>>>>>>    // stored.
11687>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure StoreDefaultSQLFilters
11689>>>>>>>>>>>        String sOldFilter
11689>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOldFilterActive bOldFilterEQ
11689>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMain
11689>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain
11690>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER of iMain to sOldFilter
11693>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER_ACTIVE of iMain to bOldFilterActive
11696>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER_EQ of iMain to bOldFilterEQ
11699>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Set psOldFilter to sOldFilter
11701>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Set pbOldFilterActive to bOldFilterActive
11703>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Set pbOldFilterEq to bOldFilterEQ
11705>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11706>>>>>>>>>>>
11706>>>>>>>>>>>    // called after an SQL find. Must restore the global and table SQL filter attributes
11706>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RestoreDefaultSQLFilters
11708>>>>>>>>>>>        String sOldFilter
11708>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOldFilterActive bOldFilterEQ
11708>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMain
11708>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iMain
11710>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get psOldFilter to sOldFilter
11712>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get pbOldFilterActive to bOldFilterActive
11714>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get pbOldFilterEq to bOldFilterEQ
11716>>>>>>>>>>>        Set_Attribute DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER of iMain to sOldFilter
11719>>>>>>>>>>>        Set_Attribute DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER_ACTIVE of iMain to bOldFilterActive
11722>>>>>>>>>>>        Set_Attribute DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER_EQ of iMain to bOldFilterEQ
11725>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11726>>>>>>>>>>>
11726>>>>>>>>>>>    // applies the passed SQL filter. If empty, it should make sure that no filter
11726>>>>>>>>>>>    // is applied. If non-empty it should set the filter active, set the filter string
11726>>>>>>>>>>>    // and make sure this is applied to all finds (including find EQ)
11726>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ApplySQLFilterStr String sFilter
11728>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMain
11728>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iMain
11730>>>>>>>>>>>        If (sFilter<>"") Begin
11732>>>>>>>>>>>            Set_Attribute DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER_ACTIVE of iMain to True
11735>>>>>>>>>>>            Set_Attribute DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER of iMain to sFilter
11738>>>>>>>>>>>            Set_Attribute DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER_EQ of iMain to True
11741>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11741>>>>>>>>>>>>
11741>>>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
11742>>>>>>>>>>>            Set_Attribute DF_FILE_SQL_FILTER_ACTIVE of iMain to False
11745>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11745>>>>>>>>>>>>
11745>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11746>>>>>>>>>>>End_Class
11747>>>>>>>>>>>
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// Every data_set will have a object based on this class. It will hold
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// the values for the fields, the entry_options and the messages IDs of the
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// iEntry, iExit and iValidate messages for each field.
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// It is assumed that an object of this class will always be used as a
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// child object of a Data_Set object.
11747>>>>>>>>>>>//
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// Currently the fieldtypes Overlap, Text and Binary are *not* supported.
11747>>>>>>>>>>>//
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// ITEM-PROPERTY   ASSIGNED-FUNCTION
11747>>>>>>>>>>>//
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// Value           The value of the field. Will be updated whenever the
11747>>>>>>>>>>>//                 value of a field changes due to data-entry or a found
11747>>>>>>>>>>>//                 record.
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// Data_File       Contains the filenumber. Is the same for every item.
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// Data_Field      Contains the fieldnumber for the item. Is equal to the
11747>>>>>>>>>>>//                 items' itemnumber.
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// Item_Options    Used to store the standard item-options of a field.
11747>>>>>>>>>>>// Aux_Value       Used to store the foreign-item-options of a field.
11747>>>>>>>>>>>Class cRecordBuffer is an cDDBuffer
11748>>>>>>>>>>>
11748>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure will be called from the Data_Set when the Main_File is
11748>>>>>>>>>>>    // being set. It will create an item for each field of the file in this
11748>>>>>>>>>>>    // object. Fields of the types DF_OVERLAP, DF_TEXT and DF_BINARY are
11748>>>>>>>>>>>    // currently not added.
11748>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Create_Items Integer iFile
11750>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField_Count iField
11750>>>>>>>>>>>
11750>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_NUMBER_FIELDS of iFile to iField_Count
11753>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Main_File to iFile
11754>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Delete_Data
11755>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Item_Count to (iField_Count+1)
11756>>>>>>>>>>>        For iField from 0 to iField_Count
11762>>>>>>>>>>>>
11762>>>>>>>>>>>            // will skip recnum (field 0) if non-recnum table
11762>>>>>>>>>>>            // will set to skip if binary, text or overlap
11762>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Data_Field iField to iField
11763>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
11764>>>>>>>>>>>>
11764>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11765>>>>>>>>>>>
11765>>>>>>>>>>>    // when an alias is created, we want to clear any values that will not be applied to
11765>>>>>>>>>>>    // this alias DD such as prompt and zoom objects (which would point to the superclass master)
11765>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ReDefineAliasItems Integer iFile
11767>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer i iItems
11767>>>>>>>>>>>
11767>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Main_File to iFile
11768>>>>>>>>>>>        Get item_count to iItems
11769>>>>>>>>>>>        For i from 0 to (iItems-1)
11775>>>>>>>>>>>>
11775>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Prompt_Object i to 0
11776>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Zoom_Object i to 0
11777>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
11778>>>>>>>>>>>>
11778>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11779>>>>>>>>>>>
11779>>>>>>>>>>>
11779>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure will be called from the parent Data_Set whenever the
11779>>>>>>>>>>>    // Data_Set changes its Current_Record property, or after a Save, Delete or Clear operation.
11779>>>>>>>>>>>    // We use this event to store the values of the fields in our local record buffer.
11779>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure OnNewCurrentRecord RowID riOld RowID riNew
11781>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMain_File
11781>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOldState
11781>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
11781>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
11782>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bRetain bInReSync
11782>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFld iFlds iIndex
11782>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
11782>>>>>>>>>>>
11782>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Parent to hoDD
11783>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iMain_File
11785>>>>>>>>>>>
11785>>>>>>>>>>>        If not (IsNullRowId(riNew)) ;            Send Entry_Display
11788>>>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
11789>>>>>>>>>>>            If (OPERATION_ORIGIN) Begin
11791>>>>>>>>>>>                // This gets set by webapp during a resync. During resyncs, you don't want to rely
11791>>>>>>>>>>>                // on the values in the buffers (as they may not be yours), so you cannot do retain of rememberlast.
11791>>>>>>>>>>>                // Fortunately, you don't need to, as this information is not needed during a resync.
11791>>>>>>>>>>>                Get pbInResync of operation_origin to bInResync
11792>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11792>>>>>>>>>>>>
11792>>>>>>>>>>>
11792>>>>>>>>>>>            // If we have any 17.0 Remember last value items, we must add those items to our array.
11792>>>>>>>>>>>            // Only do this if this is the operation origin or a parent (i.e., skip if a child DDO).
11792>>>>>>>>>>>            // Also skip if a resync. See above
11792>>>>>>>>>>>            If ( not(bInReSync) and ;                ( (Operation_Origin=hoDD) or ;                ( OPERATION_ORIGIN and (Which_data_set(Operation_Origin,iMain_File)<>0) ) ) ) Begin
11794>>>>>>>>>>>                Delegate Get pDDDefaults to DefaultValues
11796>>>>>>>>>>>                Move (SizeOfArray(DefaultValues)) to iFlds
11797>>>>>>>>>>>                For iFld from 0 to (iFlds-1)
11803>>>>>>>>>>>>
11803>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move (DefaultValues[iFld].sDefault=DD_RememberLast) to bRetain // if this is a dynamically assigned remember-last
11804>>>>>>>>>>>                    If bRetain Begin
11806>>>>>>>>>>>                        Get Value DefaultValues[iFld].iField to DefaultValues[iFld].sLastValue
11807>>>>>>>>>>>                    End
11807>>>>>>>>>>>>
11807>>>>>>>>>>>                    Else Begin
11808>>>>>>>>>>>                        Move '' to DefaultValues[iFld].sLastValue
11809>>>>>>>>>>>                    End
11809>>>>>>>>>>>>
11809>>>>>>>>>>>                Loop
11810>>>>>>>>>>>>
11810>>>>>>>>>>>                Delegate Set pDDDefaults to DefaultValues
11812>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11812>>>>>>>>>>>>
11812>>>>>>>>>>>
11812>>>>>>>>>>>            // we must do this to make retains not set changed_state
11812>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Get Change_Disabled_State to iOldState
11814>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Set Change_Disabled_State to True
11816>>>>>>>>>>>            // If mode is anything other than clear, we do a clear all (clear keeps retains, clear all does not)
11816>>>>>>>>>>>            // Also do clear all if the DDO is foreign.
11816>>>>>>>>>>>
11816>>>>>>>>>>>            // If bInReSync, we never use retains, as the buffer is not ours yet.
11816>>>>>>>>>>>            // The Entry_Clear, Entry_Clear_All parameter is bIgnoreRetains.
11816>>>>>>>>>>>            // When True, retain and retain_all states are ignored and cleared.
11816>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Operation_Mode=MODE_CLEARING and ;                ( (Operation_Origin=parent(Self)) or ;                (Which_data_set(Operation_Origin,iMain_File)<>0) ) ) Begin
11818>>>>>>>>>>>                    Send Entry_Clear bInReSync
11819>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11819>>>>>>>>>>>>
11819>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
11820>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Entry_Clear_all bInResync
11821>>>>>>>>>>>            End
11821>>>>>>>>>>>>
11821>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Set Change_Disabled_State to iOldState
11823>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Changed_State to False
11824>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11824>>>>>>>>>>>>
11824>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11825>>>>>>>>>>>
11825>>>>>>>>>>>    // Make sure to set the Changed_State of the Data_Set to TRUE when a
11825>>>>>>>>>>>    // field value changes and it's not during the Setting of the Defaults.
11825>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Changed_State Integer iState
11827>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iNoChange
11827>>>>>>>>>>>        // Server.pkg in dso already knows this property
11827>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Change_disabled_State to iNoChange
11829>>>>>>>>>>>        If not iNoChange Begin
11831>>>>>>>>>>>            Forward Set Changed_State to iState
11833>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Set Changed_State to iState
11835>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11835>>>>>>>>>>>>
11835>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11836>>>>>>>>>>>
11836>>>>>>>>>>>End_Class
11837>>>>>>>>>>>
11837>>>>>>>>>>>
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// Objects of this class will be used to store all kinds of attributes
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// which belong to a field.
11837>>>>>>>>>>>//
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// FA_MIN_VALUE
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// Used to store the mininum value of field.
11837>>>>>>>>>>>//
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// FA_MAX_VALUE
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// Used to store the maximum value of a field.
11837>>>>>>>>>>>//
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// FA_CHECK_VALUE
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// Used to store a string which contains all possible values of a field.
11837>>>>>>>>>>>//
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// Used to store the TRUE value for a checkbox field
11837>>>>>>>>>>>//
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// FA_CHECKBOX_FALSE
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// Used to store the FALSE value of a checkbox field
11837>>>>>>>>>>>//
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// FA_TABLE_OBJECT
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// Stores object Id of a validation table.
11837>>>>>>>>>>>//
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// FA_ERROR_MESSAGE
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// Used to store a error text which will be shown to a user when a fields
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// value violates one of the rules defined for it.
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// This field may contain the special strings @MIN, @MAX and @CHECK. When
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// these are used, these will be replaced by the actual value of MIN_VALUE,
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// MAX_VALUE or CHECK_VALUE.
11837>>>>>>>>>>>//
11837>>>>>>>>>>>
11837>>>>>>>>>>>
11837>>>>>>>>>>>// Validation Types
11837>>>>>>>>>>>Enumeration_List
11837>>>>>>>>>>>    Define FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_NONE
11837>>>>>>>>>>>    Define FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_RANGE
11837>>>>>>>>>>>    Define FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECK
11837>>>>>>>>>>>    Define FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX
11837>>>>>>>>>>>    Define FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_TABLE
11837>>>>>>>>>>>End_Enumeration_List
11837>>>>>>>>>>>
11837>>>>>>>>>>>
11837>>>>>>>>>>>Class Field_Attributes is a Array
11838>>>>>>>>>>>
11838>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Construct_Object
11840>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Construct_Object
11842>>>>>>>>>>>        // Private: This replaces the use of arrays to get at this value. This
11842>>>>>>>>>>>        // allows us to find specific validation types (like checkboxes) more
11842>>>>>>>>>>>        // quickly than scanning an array
11842>>>>>>>>>>>        Property String Private.Validation_Types     ''
11843>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11844>>>>>>>>>>>
11844>>>>>>>>>>>    // Returns the extended validation type for the passed field.
11844>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_Validation_Type Integer iField Returns Integer
11846>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iType
11846>>>>>>>>>>>        If iField ;            Move (mid(Private.Validation_Types(Self),1,iField)) to iType
11849>>>>>>>>>>>        Else ;            Move FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_NONE to iType
11851>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iType
11852>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11853>>>>>>>>>>>
11853>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Validation_Type Integer iField String sType
11855>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iType
11855>>>>>>>>>>>        String sTypes
11855>>>>>>>>>>>        If iField Begin
11857>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Private.Validation_Types to sTypes
11858>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Private.Validation_Types to (Overstrike(sType, sTypes, iField))
11859>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11859>>>>>>>>>>>>
11859>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11860>>>>>>>>>>>
11860>>>>>>>>>>>    // Set any defaults required by this class when the main file is created.
11860>>>>>>>>>>>    // Create a string which contains all validation types. Set all to
11860>>>>>>>>>>>    // No extended validation type.
11860>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Create_Items
11862>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sType
11862>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
11862>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Count to iCOunt
11864>>>>>>>>>>>        Move FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_NONE to sType
11865>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Private.Validation_Types to (Repeat(sType,iCount))
11866>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11867>>>>>>>>>>>
11867>>>>>>>>>>>    // Return field number of next field matching the passed validation type.
11867>>>>>>>>>>>    // Pass validation type and last position checked. Return 0 if no match
11867>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Next_Validation_Type String sType Integer iOffset Returns Integer
11869>>>>>>>>>>>        String sTypes
11869>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iPos
11869>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Private.Validation_Types to sTypes
11870>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (Pos(sType, mid(sTypes,255,iOffset+1))) to iPos
11871>>>>>>>>>>>        If iPos ;            Add iOffset to iPos
11874>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iPos
11875>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11876>>>>>>>>>>>
11876>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure will be called by the Extended_Data_Set to set the
11876>>>>>>>>>>>    // errornumber and message which will be triggered when it needs to.
11876>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Error Integer iField Integer iErr String sMsg
11878>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
11878>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
11879>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_ERROR_NUMBER) to iErr
11880>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_ERROR_MESSAGE) to sMsg
11881>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11882>>>>>>>>>>>
11882>>>>>>>>>>>    // Used to retreive the error number and message for a particular field
11882>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_Error_Number Integer iField Returns Integer
11884>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iErr
11884>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iField*FA_COUNT + FA_ERROR_NUMBER)  to iErr
11885>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iErr
11886>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11887>>>>>>>>>>>
11887>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_Error_Message Integer iField Returns String
11889>>>>>>>>>>>        String sValue
11889>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iField*FA_COUNT + FA_ERROR_MESSAGE) to sValue
11890>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sValue
11891>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11892>>>>>>>>>>>
11892>>>>>>>>>>>
11892>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function manages the validation of a field against its extended
11892>>>>>>>>>>>    // validations.
11892>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field Integer iField Returns Integer
11894>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iType
11894>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
11894>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Validation_Type iField to iType
11895>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_RANGE) ;            Get Validate_Field_Range iField to iResult
11898>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECK) ;            Get Validate_Field_Check iField to iResult
11902>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX) ;            Get Validate_Field_Checkbox iField to iResult
11906>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_TABLE) ;            Get Validate_Field_Table iField to iResult
11910>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iResult
11911>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11912>>>>>>>>>>>
11912>>>>>>>>>>>    // All extended validations know how to send callback messages (iMsg) to
11912>>>>>>>>>>>    // the calling object (iObj). This allows external lists to get filled w/
11912>>>>>>>>>>>    // the contents of a range. Used by combo boxes, spinners, etc.
11912>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Field_Fill_List Integer iField Integer iObj Integer iMsg
11914>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iType
11914>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
11914>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Validation_Type iField to iType
11915>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_RANGE) ;            Send Field_Fill_List_Field_Range iField iObj iMsg
11918>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECK) ;            Send Field_Fill_List_Field_Check iField iObj iMsg
11922>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX) ;            Send Field_Fill_List_Field_Checkbox iField iObj iMsg
11926>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_TABLE) ;            Send Field_Fill_List_Field_Table iField iObj iMsg
11930>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11931>>>>>>>>>>>
11931>>>>>>>>>>>    // Return the id of the validation table if one exists. Otherwise return
11931>>>>>>>>>>>    // a zero.
11931>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_Table_Object Integer iField Returns Integer
11933>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iType
11933>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iObj
11933>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
11933>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
11934>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Validation_Type iField to iType
11935>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iType = FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_TABLE) ;            Get Value (iBase + FA_TABLE_OBJECT) to iObj
11938>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iObj
11939>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11940>>>>>>>>>>>
11940>>>>>>>>>>>    // Procedure to set the range for a field. It will automatically set the
11940>>>>>>>>>>>    // validation type of the field as well.
11940>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Value_Range Integer iField String sMin String sMax
11942>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
11942>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
11943>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_MIN_VALUE) to sMin
11944>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_MAX_VALUE) to sMax
11945>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Field_Validation_Type iField to FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_RANGE
11946>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11947>>>>>>>>>>>
11947>>>>>>>>>>>    // Function to check a fields value agains a given check string.
11947>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field_Range Integer iField Returns Integer
11949>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sMin
11949>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sMax
11949>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sValue
11949>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField_Type
11949>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
11949>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
11949>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
11949>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
11950>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_MIN_VALUE) to sMin
11951>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_MAX_VALUE) to sMax
11952>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
11954>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
11956>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_TYPE of iFile iField to iField_Type
11959>>>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iResult
11960>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iField_Type=DF_ASCII) ;            Move (sValue < sMin or sValue > sMax) to iResult
11963>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iField_Type=DF_BCD) ;            Move (Number(sValue) < Number(sMin) or ;            Number(sValue) > Number(sMax)) to iResult
11967>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iField_Type=DF_DATE) ;            Move (Date(sValue) < Date(sMin) or Date(sValue) > Date(sMax)) to iResult
11971>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iField_Type=DF_DATETIME) ;            Move (Cast(sValue,DateTime) < Cast(sMin,DateTime) or Cast(sValue,DateTime) > Cast(sMax,DateTime)) to iResult
11975>>>>>>>>>>>        If iResult Begin
11977>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Send Field_Error iField DD_INVALID_RANGE sMin sMax
11979>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return 1
11980>>>>>>>>>>>        End
11980>>>>>>>>>>>>
11980>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
11981>>>>>>>>>>>
11981>>>>>>>>>>>    // Callback to provide all valid value for this validation.
11981>>>>>>>>>>>    // Just call back with the two range values
11981>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Field_Fill_List_Field_Range Integer iField Integer iObj Integer iMsg
11983>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sMin
11983>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sMax
11983>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
11983>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
11984>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_MIN_VALUE) to sMin
11985>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_MAX_VALUE) to sMax
11986>>>>>>>>>>>        Send iMsg to iObj 0 sMin '' 0 (NullrowId())
11987>>>>>>>>>>>        Send iMsg to iObj 1 sMax '' 0 (NullrowId())
11988>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11989>>>>>>>>>>>
11989>>>>>>>>>>>    // Procedure to set the check for a field. It will automatically set the
11989>>>>>>>>>>>    // validation type of the field as well.
11989>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Value_Check Integer iField String sCheck
11991>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
11991>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
11992>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_CHECK_VALUE) to sCheck
11993>>>>>>>>>>>        //Set Value iBase to FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECK
11993>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Field_Validation_Type iField to FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECK
11994>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
11995>>>>>>>>>>>
11995>>>>>>>>>>>    // Function to check a fields value agains a given check string.
11995>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field_Check Integer iField Returns Integer
11997>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sCheck
11997>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sValue
11997>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
11997>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iPos
11997>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iLength
11997>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
11997>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
11997>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
11998>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECK_VALUE) to sCheck
11999>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
12001>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
12003>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_LENGTH of iFile iField to iLength
12006>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (Pad( sValue,iLength)) to sValue
12007>>>>>>>>>>>        // Replace the seperation characters with two of them so the user
12007>>>>>>>>>>>        // can't bypass the check by entering a seperation character.
12007>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (Replaces("|", sValue, "||")) to sValue
12008>>>>>>>>>>>        // Report an error if rules are violated.
12008>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (Pos( sValue, sCheck)) to iPos
12009>>>>>>>>>>>        If not iPos Begin
12011>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Send Field_Error iField DD_INVALID_CHECK sCheck
12013>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return 1
12014>>>>>>>>>>>        End
12014>>>>>>>>>>>>
12014>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
12015>>>>>>>>>>>
12015>>>>>>>>>>>    // Callback to provide all valid value for this validation.
12015>>>>>>>>>>>    // Call back with all valid check values
12015>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Field_Fill_List_Field_Check Integer iField Integer iObj Integer iMsg
12017>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sCheck
12017>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
12017>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iPos
12017>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iItem
12017>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
12018>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECK_VALUE) to sCheck
12019>>>>>>>>>>>        Append sCheck "|"
12020>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (Pos( "|", sCheck)) to iPos
12021>>>>>>>>>>>        While iPos
12025>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iPos > 1) Begin
12027>>>>>>>>>>>                Send iMsg to iObj iItem (Left(sCheck,iPos-1)) '' 0 (NullrowId())
12028>>>>>>>>>>>                Increment iItem
12029>>>>>>>>>>>            End
12029>>>>>>>>>>>>
12029>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Mid( sCheck, 255, iPos+1))  to sCheck
12030>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Pos( "|", sCheck)) to iPos
12031>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
12032>>>>>>>>>>>>
12032>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
12033>>>>>>>>>>>
12033>>>>>>>>>>>    // Procedure to set up a checkbox field. We will store the TRUE and FALSE
12033>>>>>>>>>>>    // Values in the extended array.
12033>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_CheckBox_Values Integer iField String sTrue String sFalse
12035>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
12035>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
12036>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE) to sTrue
12037>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_FALSE) to sFalse
12038>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Field_Validation_Type iField to FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX
12039>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
12040>>>>>>>>>>>
12040>>>>>>>>>>>    // Return the Value associated with the field and its select-state.
12040>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_CheckBox_Value Integer iField Integer iState Returns String
12042>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
12042>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iType
12042>>>>>>>>>>>        String sValue
12042>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
12043>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Validation_Type iField to iType
12044>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iType <> FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX) ;            Move iState to sValue
12047>>>>>>>>>>>        Else ;            Get Value (iBase + If(iState,FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE,FA_CHECKBOX_FALSE));            to sValue
12049>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sValue
12050>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
12051>>>>>>>>>>>
12051>>>>>>>>>>>    // Return the select_state based on the passed value and field
12051>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_Value_Select_State Integer iField String sValue Returns Integer
12053>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
12053>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iType
12053>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sTrue
12053>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iState
12053>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
12053>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField_Type
12053>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
12054>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Validation_Type iField to iType
12055>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE) to sTrue
12056>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iType <> FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_CHECKBOX) ;            Move (not(sValue=0 or sValue='')) to iState
12059>>>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
12060>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
12062>>>>>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_TYPE of iFile iField to iField_Type
12065>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iField_Type = DF_BCD) ;                Move (Number(sValue)=Number(sTrue)) to iState
12068>>>>>>>>>>>            Else ; // DF_ASCII                Move (sValue=sTrue) to iState
12070>>>>>>>>>>>        End
12070>>>>>>>>>>>>
12070>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iState
12071>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
12072>>>>>>>>>>>
12072>>>>>>>>>>>
12072>>>>>>>>>>>    // Check that the buffer value is one of the two checkbox values.
12072>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field_Checkbox Integer iField Returns Integer
12074>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sTrue
12074>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sFalse
12074>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sValue
12074>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField_Type
12074>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
12074>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
12074>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
12074>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
12075>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE) to sTrue
12076>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_FALSE) to sFalse
12077>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
12079>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Main_File to iFile
12081>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_TYPE of iFile iField to iField_Type
12084>>>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iResult
12085>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iField_Type = DF_BCD) ;            Move (Number(sValue)=Number(sTrue) or ;            Number(sValue)=Number(sFalse)) to iResult
12088>>>>>>>>>>>        Else ; // DF_ASCII            Move (sValue=sTrue or sValue=sFalse) to iResult
12090>>>>>>>>>>>        If not iResult Begin
12092>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Send Field_Error iField DD_INVALID_CHECKBOX sTrue sFalse
12094>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return 1
12095>>>>>>>>>>>        End
12095>>>>>>>>>>>>
12095>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
12096>>>>>>>>>>>
12096>>>>>>>>>>>    // Callback to provide all valid value for this validation.
12096>>>>>>>>>>>    // Just call back with the two true and false values
12096>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Field_Fill_List_Field_Checkbox Integer iField Integer iObj Integer iMsg
12098>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sTrue
12098>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sFalse
12098>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
12098>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
12099>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_TRUE) to sTrue
12100>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_CHECKBOX_FALSE) to sFalse
12101>>>>>>>>>>>        Send iMsg to iObj 0 sTrue '' 0 (NullrowId())
12102>>>>>>>>>>>        Send iMsg to iObj 1 sFalse '' 0 (NullrowId())
12103>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
12104>>>>>>>>>>>
12104>>>>>>>>>>>    // The object keeps track of a validation table object. This table object
12104>>>>>>>>>>>    // can be any type of object must at a minimum understand a small message
12104>>>>>>>>>>>    // protocol (see xvaltbl.pkg for info)
12104>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_Value_Table Integer iField Integer iObj
12106>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
12106>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
12107>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Value (iBase + FA_TABLE_OBJECT) to iObj
12108>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Field_Validation_Type iField to FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_TABLE
12109>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
12110>>>>>>>>>>>
12110>>>>>>>>>>>    // This valdates against a validation table if appropriate (if a table
12110>>>>>>>>>>>    // exists and the table's validate_State is T). It validates by passing
12110>>>>>>>>>>>    // the message validate_value to the validation table object
12110>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field_Table Integer iField Returns Integer
12112>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
12112>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iTableObj
12112>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sValue
12112>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
12112>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
12113>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_TABLE_OBJECT) to iTableObj
12114>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iTableObj and Validate_State(iTableObj) ) Begin
12116>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
12118>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Validate_Value of iTableOBj sValue to iResult
12119>>>>>>>>>>>            If iResult ;                Delegate Send Field_Error iField DD_INVALID_VALUE_TABLE
12123>>>>>>>>>>>        End
12123>>>>>>>>>>>>
12123>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iResult
12124>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
12125>>>>>>>>>>>
12125>>>>>>>>>>>    // Callback to provide all valid value for this validation.
12125>>>>>>>>>>>    // Pass the request on to the validation table. This is the most common
12125>>>>>>>>>>>    // use of this.
12125>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Field_Fill_List_Field_Table Integer iField Integer iObj Integer iMsg
12127>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iBase
12127>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iTableObj
12127>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (iField * FA_COUNT) to iBase
12128>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Value (iBase + FA_TABLE_OBJECT) to iTableObj
12129>>>>>>>>>>>        If iTableObj ;            Send Request_Fill_From_List to iTableObj iObj iMsg
12132>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
12133>>>>>>>>>>>
12133>>>>>>>>>>>    // Often extended valditation types can provide automatic prompt
12133>>>>>>>>>>>    // objects. If the extended type supports a prompt object and there is
12133>>>>>>>>>>>    // a global validation_list object, we will use it
12133>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Prompt_Object Integer iField Returns Integer
12135>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iType
12135>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iObj
12135>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Validation_Type iField to iType
12136>>>>>>>>>>>        If not (iType=FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_NONE or iType=FA_VALIDATION_TYPE_RANGE) ;            Move DD_Global_Validation_Prompt_Object to iObj
12139>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iObj
12140>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
12141>>>>>>>>>>>
12141>>>>>>>>>>>
12141>>>>>>>>>>>End_Class
12142>>>>>>>>>>>
12142>>>>>>>>>>>
12142>>>>>>>>>>>
12142>>>>>>>>>>>// use to keep track of file field pairs such as system file file/field
12142>>>>>>>>>>>Struct tDDFileField
12142>>>>>>>>>>>    Integer iFile
12142>>>>>>>>>>>    Integer iField
12142>>>>>>>>>>>End_Struct
