13222>>>>>>>>>>>
13222>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function will be called indirectly by DEOs when an item is being
13222>>>>>>>>>>>    // entered, exited or needs validation. The first argument holds the
13222>>>>>>>>>>>    // fieldnumber for the field and the second holds the id of the message
13222>>>>>>>>>>>    // which can be send to retrieve the message which needs to be send for
13222>>>>>>>>>>>    // this Field/Event combination. The value of the second argument can be
13222>>>>>>>>>>>    // GET_Field_Entry_MSG, GET_Field_Exit_MSG or GET_Field_Validate_MSG.
13222>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Exec_Field_Message Integer iField Integer iMsg_ID Returns Integer
13224>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMsg
13224>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
13224>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sValue
13224>>>>>>>>>>>        Get iMsg_ID iField to iMsg
13225>>>>>>>>>>>        If iMsg Begin
13227>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
13228>>>>>>>>>>>            Get iMsg iField sValue to iResult
13229>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13229>>>>>>>>>>>>
13229>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iResult
13230>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13231>>>>>>>>>>>
13231>>>>>>>>>>>
13231>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function will be called from within DEOs when an item is being
13231>>>>>>>>>>>    // entered, exited or needs validation. The first argument holds the
13231>>>>>>>>>>>    // file number, the second argument holds the field and the third
13231>>>>>>>>>>>    // holds the id of the message  which can be send to retrieve the message
13231>>>>>>>>>>>    // which needs to be send for this File/Field/Event combination.
13231>>>>>>>>>>>    // The value of the second argument can be  GET_Field_Entry_MSG,
13231>>>>>>>>>>>    // GET_Field_Exit_MSG or GET_Field_Validate_MSG.
13231>>>>>>>>>>>    // This will redirect to the proper data-set object.
13231>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Exec_File_Field_Message Integer iFile Integer iField Integer iMsg_ID Returns Integer
13233>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
13233>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
13233>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_set iFile to iDSO
13234>>>>>>>>>>>        If iDSO ;            Get Exec_Field_Message of iDSO iField iMsg_ID to iResult
13237>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iResult
13238>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13239>>>>>>>>>>>
13239>>>>>>>>>>>    // Find the data-set whose main_file is the same as File#. The message
13239>>>>>>>>>>>    // Which_data_set includes updating parent files, we will throw those out.
13239>>>>>>>>>>>    // This has been augmented to search down the DDO tree if we do not find
13239>>>>>>>>>>>    // the DD with our quick C Which_Data_set search
13239>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Data_Set Integer iFile Returns Integer
13241>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iTmp
13241>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
13241>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iTmp
13242>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iTmp = iFile) ;            Function_Return Self
13245>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Which_Data_Set iFile to iDSO
13246>>>>>>>>>>>        If iDSO Begin
13248>>>>>>>>>>>            // check that DS's main-file is the File (and not a parent file)
13248>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of iDSO to iTmp
13249>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iTmp = iFile) ;                Function_Return iDSO
13252>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13252>>>>>>>>>>>>
13252>>>>>>>>>>>
13252>>>>>>>>>>>        // This really should have succeeded by now. If not we need to do a
13252>>>>>>>>>>>        // downward sweep looking for DD. This will be a slower process since it
13252>>>>>>>>>>>        // involves flex level DDO structure traversal. We should very rarely ever
13252>>>>>>>>>>>        // get to this point. If we do, it takes longer!
13252>>>>>>>>>>>
13252>>>>>>>>>>>        // Unlike other traversals we will mark and check in a single
13252>>>>>>>>>>>        // step.
13252>>>>>>>>>>>        // This Mark_Id creates a sequence Id for this clear. This way
13252>>>>>>>>>>>        // DSOs only get cleared one time during this process.
13252>>>>>>>>>>>        Send IncrementCurrentMarkId
13253>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Private.Data_set iFile to iDSO // this does the recursive downward search
13254>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iDSO
13255>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13256>>>>>>>>>>>
13256>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Private.Data_Set Integer iFile Returns Integer
13258>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
13258>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO hDD
13258>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
13258>>>>>>>>>>>
13258>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iFile=Main_file(Self)) ;            Function_Return Self
13261>>>>>>>>>>>
13261>>>>>>>>>>>        // We are only looking at sequence ID.
13261>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Last_Mark_Sequence_id to DD_Current_mark_id
13262>>>>>>>>>>>
13262>>>>>>>>>>>        // recurse Down first, since we already tried upward direction.
13262>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
13263>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
13264>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
13270>>>>>>>>>>>>
13270>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to iDSO
13271>>>>>>>>>>>            // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
13271>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(iDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) Begin
13273>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Private.Data_Set of iDSO iFile to hDD
13274>>>>>>>>>>>                If hDD ;                    Function_Return hDD // when found...get out
13277>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13277>>>>>>>>>>>>
13277>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13278>>>>>>>>>>>>
13278>>>>>>>>>>>        // recurse up server list next. We do this 2nd because it is
13278>>>>>>>>>>>        // the less likely path for success.
13278>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
13279>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
13280>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
13286>>>>>>>>>>>>
13286>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to iDSO
13287>>>>>>>>>>>            // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
13287>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(iDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) Begin
13289>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Private.Data_Set of iDSO iFile to hDD
13290>>>>>>>>>>>                If hDD ;                    Function_Return hDD // when found...get out
13293>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13293>>>>>>>>>>>>
13293>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13294>>>>>>>>>>>>
13294>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return 0 // if here, our traversal has failed.
13295>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13296>>>>>>>>>>>
13296>>>>>>>>>>>    // These methods can be used to set/get a field property in a flexible
13296>>>>>>>>>>>    // way. The first two argument are the file- and fieldnumber followed by
13296>>>>>>>>>>>    // the ID of the message that should be send. The last argument should
13296>>>>>>>>>>>    // be the value to set or the variable to store the value in.
13296>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set File_Field_Property Integer iFile Integer iField Integer iMsg String sValue
13298>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
13298>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set iFile to iDSO
13299>>>>>>>>>>>        If iDSO Begin
13301>>>>>>>>>>>            Set iMsg of iDSO iField to sValue
13302>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return sValue
13303>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13303>>>>>>>>>>>>
13303>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13304>>>>>>>>>>>
13304>>>>>>>>>>>    Function File_Field_Property Integer iFile Integer iField Integer iMsg Returns Integer
13306>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
13306>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sValue
13306>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set iFile to iDSO
13307>>>>>>>>>>>        If iDSO Begin
13309>>>>>>>>>>>            Get iMsg of iDSO iField to sValue
13310>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return sValue
13311>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13311>>>>>>>>>>>>
13311>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13312>>>>>>>>>>>
13312>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure will return the number of fields in the object
13312>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_Count Returns Integer
13314>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Item_Count(Record_Buffer(Self)) - 1)
13315>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13316>>>>>>>>>>>
13316>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure will clear all flags in the visited_fields string so
13316>>>>>>>>>>>    // that all field will be validated on the next requests.
13316>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Clear_Visited_Fields
13318>>>>>>>>>>>        // this clears field visitation marks
13318>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_Fields to (Repeat(" ", Field_Count(Self)))
13319>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13320>>>>>>>>>>>
13320>>>>>>>>>>>    // Private.Initialize_Visited
13320>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure will be called when validations (and perhaps other
13320>>>>>>>>>>>    // events) is requested. It clears the visited marks and then proceeds
13320>>>>>>>>>>>    // to clear the marks up the server tree.
13320>>>>>>>>>>>    // This is passed two parameters: Up_and_down, If true upward and downward
13320>>>>>>>>>>>    // initialize. If Clear_Fields also clear the field string
13320>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Private.Initialize_Visited Integer Up_and_Down Integer Clear_Fields
13322>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
13322>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
13322>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
13322>>>>>>>>>>>
13322>>>>>>>>>>>        // recurse up server list first. Only recurse up
13322>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
13323>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
13324>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
13330>>>>>>>>>>>>
13330>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to iDSO
13331>>>>>>>>>>>            // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
13331>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(iDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) ;                Send Private.Initialize_Visited to iDSO False Clear_Fields
13334>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13335>>>>>>>>>>>>
13335>>>>>>>>>>>
13335>>>>>>>>>>>        If Clear_Fields ;            Send Clear_Visited_Fields // clear all markers in this object
13338>>>>>>>>>>>        // this clears the visited mark for the entire object
13338>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to False
13339>>>>>>>>>>>        Set DownDelete_State to False
13340>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Last_Mark_Sequence_id to DD_Current_mark_id
13341>>>>>>>>>>>
13341>>>>>>>>>>>        // If Up_and_Down recurse Down server list
13341>>>>>>>>>>>        If Up_and_Down Begin
13343>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
13344>>>>>>>>>>>            Decrement iMax // **EK** This line was missing
13345>>>>>>>>>>>            For iCount from 0 to iMax
13351>>>>>>>>>>>>
13351>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Data_Set_Client iCount to iDSO
13352>>>>>>>>>>>                // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
13352>>>>>>>>>>>                If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(iDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) ;                    Send Private.Initialize_Visited to iDSO True Clear_Fields
13355>>>>>>>>>>>            Loop
13356>>>>>>>>>>>>
13356>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13356>>>>>>>>>>>>
13356>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13357>>>>>>>>>>>
13357>>>>>>>>>>>
13357>>>>>>>>>>>    // Clears Visited marks and (maybe) field visited marks in all required
13357>>>>>>>>>>>    // DSOs. If Up_and_Down is TRUE DSOs are marked up and Down (delete style)
13357>>>>>>>>>>>    // propagation. If False, DSOs are marked up (save style). This does not
13357>>>>>>>>>>>    // have a mode to mark ALL DSOs in a structure. (Not needed so far).
13357>>>>>>>>>>>    // If Clear_Fields is T the field string marker is also cleared.
13357>>>>>>>>>>>    // The method of using the global integer DD_Current_Mark_ID is an opt-
13357>>>>>>>>>>>    // imizer. This is private - do not tamper with it!
13357>>>>>>>>>>>    // Note that Intialize_Visited does not always Clear all DDOs in the structure. When
13357>>>>>>>>>>>    // Up_and_Down is true, it is marking all DDOs that will participate in a cascade delete
13357>>>>>>>>>>>    // which may not be all DDOs in the structure. If you want to initialize all DDOs use InitializeAllVisited
13357>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Initialize_Visited Integer Up_and_Down Integer Clear_Fields
13359>>>>>>>>>>>        Send IncrementCurrentMarkId
13360>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Private.Initialize_Visited Up_and_Down Clear_Fields
13361>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13362>>>>>>>>>>>
13362>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure InitializeAllVisited2
13364>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax iCount
13364>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDSO
13364>>>>>>>>>>>
13364>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to False
13365>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Last_Mark_Sequence_id to DD_Current_mark_id // marks this as visited
13366>>>>>>>>>>>
13366>>>>>>>>>>>        // recurse up server list.
13366>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
13367>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
13373>>>>>>>>>>>>
13373>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hoDSO
13374>>>>>>>>>>>            // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
13374>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(hoDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) ;                Send InitializeAllVisited2 of hoDSO
13377>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13378>>>>>>>>>>>>
13378>>>>>>>>>>>
13378>>>>>>>>>>>        // recurse down client list.
13378>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
13379>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
13385>>>>>>>>>>>>
13385>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to hoDSO
13386>>>>>>>>>>>            // If already cleared during this sequence...do nothing
13386>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Last_Mark_Sequence_id(hoDSO)<>DD_Current_mark_id) ;                Send InitializeAllVisited2 to hoDSO
13389>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13390>>>>>>>>>>>>
13390>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13391>>>>>>>>>>>
13391>>>>>>>>>>>    // clears visited flag for *all* ddos in the structure.
13391>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure InitializeAllVisited
13393>>>>>>>>>>>        Send IncrementCurrentMarkId
13394>>>>>>>>>>>        Send InitializeAllVisited2
13395>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13396>>>>>>>>>>>
13396>>>>>>>>>>>
13396>>>>>>>>>>>    // Internal recursive message to check file connections. Called from
13396>>>>>>>>>>>    // Valid_connections only. Private message
13396>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Private.Valid_Structure Integer Up_And_Down Returns Integer
13398>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRval iCount iMax
13398>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle iDSO iPDSO
13398>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iPMax iPCount iPMain
13398>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bUpDown bNull bCascadeNull bDown
13398>>>>>>>>>>>
13398>>>>>>>>>>>        // Check Current Connections
13398>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Valid_Servers to iRval           // always check servers
13399>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iRval=0 and Up_and_Down) ;       // check Clients if required            Get Valid_Clients to iRval
13402>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
13403>>>>>>>>>>>
13403>>>>>>>>>>>        // Ask Server data-sets to check their server connections
13403>>>>>>>>>>>        If not iRval Begin // check up
13405>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
13406>>>>>>>>>>>            Decrement iMax
13407>>>>>>>>>>>            For iCount from 0 to iMax
13413>>>>>>>>>>>>
13413>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Data_Set_Server iCount to iDSO
13414>>>>>>>>>>>                If not (Visited_state(iDSO)) ;                    Get Private.Valid_Structure of iDSO False to iRVal
13417>>>>>>>>>>>            Until iRval
13419>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13419>>>>>>>>>>>>
13419>>>>>>>>>>>
13419>>>>>>>>>>>        // If required, Ask Clients to check their server and client connections
13419>>>>>>>>>>>        //
13419>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iRval=0 and Up_and_Down) Begin // check down
13421>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
13422>>>>>>>>>>>            Decrement iMax
13423>>>>>>>>>>>            For iCount from 0 to iMax
13429>>>>>>>>>>>>
13429>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Data_Set_Client iCount to iDSO
13430>>>>>>>>>>>                If not (Visited_state(iDSO)) Begin
13432>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get Data_Set_Server_Count of iDSO to iPMax
13433>>>>>>>>>>>                    // test if all deletable parents for a non parent null allowed/cascade delete null
13433>>>>>>>>>>>                    For iPCount from 0 to (iPMax-1)
13439>>>>>>>>>>>>
13439>>>>>>>>>>>                        Get Data_Set_Server of iDSO iPCount to iPDSO
13440>>>>>>>>>>>                        Get DownDelete_State of iPDSO to bDown
13441>>>>>>>>>>>                        If (bDown) Begin
13443>>>>>>>>>>>                            Get Main_File of iPDSO to iPMain
13444>>>>>>>>>>>                            Get IsNullParentAllowed of iDSO iPMain to bNull
13445>>>>>>>>>>>                            Get IsCascadeDeleteNull of iDSO iPMain to bCascadeNull
13446>>>>>>>>>>>                            Move (not(bNull) or not(bCascadeNull)) to bUpDown
13447>>>>>>>>>>>                        End
13447>>>>>>>>>>>>
13447>>>>>>>>>>>                    Until bUpDown
13449>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get Private.Valid_Structure of iDSO bUpDown to iRVal
13450>>>>>>>>>>>                End
13450>>>>>>>>>>>>
13450>>>>>>>>>>>            Until iRval
13452>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13452>>>>>>>>>>>>
13452>>>>>>>>>>>
13452>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRVal
13453>>>>>>>>>>>
13453>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13454>>>>>>>>>>>
13454>>>>>>>>>>>    // Validate data-set updating connections against required connections
13454>>>>>>>>>>>    // Pass: Up_and_down=T if we should check Server and Client connections
13454>>>>>>>>>>>    //                  =F is we only check servers
13454>>>>>>>>>>>    // Ret: 0 if ok, Missing File# if not ok.
13454>>>>>>>>>>>    // Up_And_Down should be true when testing for cascade delete structures and
13454>>>>>>>>>>>    // false when testing for save / delete-no-cascade structures
13454>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Valid_Structure Integer Up_And_Down Returns Integer
13456>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Initialize_Visited Up_and_Down False // False=don't clear field marks
13457>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Up_And_Down) Begin
13459>>>>>>>>>>>            Send MarkDDOsForCascadeDelete
13460>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13460>>>>>>>>>>>>
13460>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (Private.Valid_Structure(Self,Up_and_Down))
13461>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13462>>>>>>>>>>>
13462>>>>>>>>>>>    // mark all DDOs which are part of this deletes cascade delete tree
13462>>>>>>>>>>>    // mark this and all clients as Downward deletable. This includes
13462>>>>>>>>>>>    // cacscade delete and cascade set to null (not for cascade_delete_state=F)
13462>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure MarkDDOsForCascadeDelete
13464>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax  iCount
13464>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDown
13464>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDDO
13464>>>>>>>>>>>        Set DownDelete_State to True
13465>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
13466>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
13472>>>>>>>>>>>>
13472>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to hoDDO
13473>>>>>>>>>>>            Get DownDelete_State of hoDDO to bDown
13474>>>>>>>>>>>            If not bDown Begin // circular DDO test - never do this
13476>>>>>>>>>>>                Send MarkDDOsForCascadeDelete of hoDDO
13477>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13477>>>>>>>>>>>>
13477>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13478>>>>>>>>>>>>
13478>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13479>>>>>>>>>>>
13479>>>>>>>>>>>
13479>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function will execute the validation message for each field within
13479>>>>>>>>>>>    // this object. If DoAllFG is true all items are validated. If false
13479>>>>>>>>>>>    // only unvisited items are checked.
13479>>>>>>>>>>>    // Added bNoStop, If true, all items are validated. It is up to you to
13479>>>>>>>>>>>    // do something with the possible cascade of errors
13479>>>>>>>>>>>    // if the err returns DFERR_ENTER_VALID_REC_ID we will not continue
13479>>>>>>>>>>>    // the validation (the other fields will be bad). This works best if the
13479>>>>>>>>>>>    // findreq appears as one of the first fields in the file (which is almost
13479>>>>>>>>>>>    // always the case
13479>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Fields Integer DoAllFg Integer bNoStop Returns Integer
13481>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRetval
13481>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
13481>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
13481>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
13481>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iErr
13481>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sVS
13481>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Visited_Fields to sVS
13482>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Count to iMax
13483>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iFile
13484>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 1 to iMax
13490>>>>>>>>>>>>
13490>>>>>>>>>>>            If (DoAllFG or Mid(sVS, 1, iCount)=" ") Begin
13492>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Validate_Field iCount to iErr
13493>>>>>>>>>>>                If iErr Begin
13495>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move iErr to iRetVal
13496>>>>>>>>>>>                    // error occurred. If not no-stop or the error is
13496>>>>>>>>>>>                    // a findreq error - we are done.
13496>>>>>>>>>>>                    If (not(bNoStop) or iRetVal=DFERR_ENTER_VALID_REC_ID) ;                        Function_Return iRetVal
13499>>>>>>>>>>>                End
13499>>>>>>>>>>>>
13499>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13499>>>>>>>>>>>>
13499>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13500>>>>>>>>>>>>
13500>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRetval
13501>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13502>>>>>>>>>>>
13502>>>>>>>>>>>    // 17.0 - added support for null-parents. If null parents allowed, req lets it through
13502>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Required Integer iField Returns Integer
13504>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bNull bErr
13504>>>>>>>>>>>
13504>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (trim(Field_Current_Value(Self,iField))='') to bErr
13505>>>>>>>>>>>        If bErr ;            Send Data_set_Error iField DFERR_ENTRY_REQUIRED ""
13508>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bErr
13509>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13510>>>>>>>>>>>
13510>>>>>>>>>>>    // return true if we should skip validation for this field. This can happen with Null allowed parents.
13510>>>>>>>>>>>    // if this is foreign, new and has no changes and is null allowed we will skip.
13510>>>>>>>>>>>    Function SkipValidate Integer iField Returns Boolean
13512>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bSkip bFieldChanged bEmpty
13512>>>>>>>>>>>        String sValue
13512>>>>>>>>>>>
13512>>>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_ORIGIN<>Self and not(HasRecord(Self)) and not(changed_state(Self))) Begin
13514>>>>>>>>>>>            // We must also check field_changed_state and only skip if this is not changed.
13514>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Field_Changed_State iField to bFieldChanged
13515>>>>>>>>>>>            // Retain and remember may set field_changed_state to true even when empty. If this field is changed
13515>>>>>>>>>>>            // but its value is empty we assume it is a candidate for Null checking, so we will set field-changed to false
13515>>>>>>>>>>>            If bFieldChanged Begin
13517>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
13518>>>>>>>>>>>                Get IsEmptyField iField sValue to bEmpty
13519>>>>>>>>>>>                If bEmpty Begin
13521>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move False to bFieldChanged
13522>>>>>>>>>>>                End
13522>>>>>>>>>>>>
13522>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13522>>>>>>>>>>>>
13522>>>>>>>>>>>            If (not(bFieldChanged)) Begin
13524>>>>>>>>>>>                // we must find the child that points to this DD, starting with operation_origin. If a child
13524>>>>>>>>>>>                // is found, it will be in array position 1 (0 is self, 1 is child)
13524>>>>>>>>>>>                Get IsNullParentOrAncestor to bSkip
13525>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13525>>>>>>>>>>>>
13525>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13525>>>>>>>>>>>>
13525>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bSkip
13526>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13527>>>>>>>>>>>
13527>>>>>>>>>>>
13527>>>>>>>>>>>    // This will tell us if this DD can be treated as either a null parent
13527>>>>>>>>>>>    // or an ancestor of a null parent. This should only be called for a DD
13527>>>>>>>>>>>    // that is a candidate for this meaning that it does not have a change.
13527>>>>>>>>>>>    // We will test if its child allows this parent to be null or if this
13527>>>>>>>>>>>    // is in the path of an allowed null parent. We assume that parents of
13527>>>>>>>>>>>    // null parents will also be null. This is used to test if validations are
13527>>>>>>>>>>>    // needed.
13527>>>>>>>>>>>    Function IsNullParentOrAncestor Returns Boolean
13529>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle[] hoDDs
13530>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer i iSize iMain
13530>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bNullAllowed
13530>>>>>>>>>>>        // gets an array where 0 is self, 1 is parent, 2 is grandparent, and the
13530>>>>>>>>>>>        // last item is the operation_origin.
13530>>>>>>>>>>>        Send DDOServerPath of operation_origin Self (&hoDDs)
13531>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (SizeOfArray(hoDDs)) to iSize
13532>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iSize) Begin
13534>>>>>>>>>>>            // see if the immediate child allows this to be null.
13534>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File to iMain
13535>>>>>>>>>>>            Get IsNullParentAllowed of hoDDs[1] iMain to bNullAllowed
13536>>>>>>>>>>>
13536>>>>>>>>>>>            // if null not allowed, see if this is an ancestor to a null allowed
13536>>>>>>>>>>>            // parent where all DDs in this path are unchanged. For example:
13536>>>>>>>>>>>            // G.DD <- P.DD <- C.DD where we C.DD allows P.DD to be null and we
13536>>>>>>>>>>>            // want to test if G.DD needs validation
13536>>>>>>>>>>>            Move 1 to i
13537>>>>>>>>>>>            While (not(bNullAllowed) and (i+1<iSize) and not(changed_state(hoDDs[i])) )
13541>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Main_File of hoDDs[i] to iMain
13542>>>>>>>>>>>                Get IsNullParentAllowed of hoDDs[i+1] iMain to bNullAllowed
13543>>>>>>>>>>>                Increment i
13544>>>>>>>>>>>            Loop
13545>>>>>>>>>>>>
13545>>>>>>>>>>>
13545>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13545>>>>>>>>>>>>
13545>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bNullAllowed
13546>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13547>>>>>>>>>>>
13547>>>>>>>>>>>
13547>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_FindReq Integer iField Returns Integer
13549>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer bErr iOpts
13549>>>>>>>>>>>        // if no current record, we have not found the required record.
13549>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (not(HasRecord(Self))) to bErr
13550>>>>>>>>>>>        // We also need to check if the field is changed. If the field is changed and this
13550>>>>>>>>>>>        // is an autofind field, this indicates that an autofind was attempted and failed. We
13550>>>>>>>>>>>        // can't jut rely on current_record because a failed autofind restores the old current
13550>>>>>>>>>>>        // record. For this to work, DEOs must set the DD field's changed_state to true on
13550>>>>>>>>>>>        // no-put fields (dd_deomx.pkg was changed to do this).
13550>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bErr) and field_changed_state(Self,iField)) Begin
13552>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Field_Options iField to iOpts
13553>>>>>>>>>>>            Move ( ((iOpts iand DD_AUTOFIND)=DD_AUTOFIND) or ;                ((iOpts iand DD_AUTOFIND_GE)=DD_AUTOFIND_GE) ) ;                to bErr
13554>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13554>>>>>>>>>>>>
13554>>>>>>>>>>>        If bErr ;            Send Data_set_Error iField DFERR_ENTER_VALID_REC_ID ""
13557>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bErr
13558>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13559>>>>>>>>>>>
13559>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function will be called to validate a field.
13559>>>>>>>>>>>    // mark field currently being validated
13559>>>>>>>>>>>    // Altered to Check DD options (required, findreq)
13559>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Field Integer iField Returns Integer
13561>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
13561>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMsg
13561>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iObj
13561>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sValue
13561>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
13561>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOpts iMain
13561>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bSkipValidate
13561>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle[] hoDDs
13562>>>>>>>>>>>
13562>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Current_Validate_Field to iField
13563>>>>>>>>>>>
13563>>>>>>>>>>>        // test if we should skip validation on this field
13563>>>>>>>>>>>        Get SkipValidate iField to bSkipValidate
13564>>>>>>>>>>>
13564>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bSkipValidate)) Begin
13566>>>>>>>>>>>
13566>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Record_Buffer(Self)) to iObj
13567>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File to iFile
13568>>>>>>>>>>>
13568>>>>>>>>>>>            // Check for DD option failures: required, find_required
13568>>>>>>>>>>>            // "File_field" gets regular and foreign fields as needed
13568>>>>>>>>>>>            //Get File_Field_Options iFile iField to iOpts
13568>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Field_Options iField to iOpts  // get reg options
13569>>>>>>>>>>>            // if this is not the DDO that started the validation, we will assume that
13569>>>>>>>>>>>            // this is foreign. Operation_origin is set in Request_Validate
13569>>>>>>>>>>>            // If foreign (as defined above) and we do not allow new saves when
13569>>>>>>>>>>>            // foreign, we will consider this to be foreign and add foreign options
13569>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Operation_Origin<>Self and ;                Allow_Foreign_New_Save_State(Self)=0)  ;                Move (iOpts ior Foreign_Field_Options(Self, iField)) to iOpts
13572>>>>>>>>>>>
13572>>>>>>>>>>>
13572>>>>>>>>>>>            // Check for FindReq first. If it fails, set iResult to DFERR_ENTER_VALID_REC_ID so
13572>>>>>>>>>>>            // the calling function knows that a findreq failed. Always do this validation first
13572>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iOpts iand DD_FINDREQ) ;                Get Validate_FindReq  iField to iResult
13575>>>>>>>>>>>            If iResult Begin
13577>>>>>>>>>>>                Send AddDDHasFindReqError
13578>>>>>>>>>>>                Move DFERR_ENTER_VALID_REC_ID to iResult
13579>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13579>>>>>>>>>>>>
13579>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
13580>>>>>>>>>>>
13580>>>>>>>>>>>                If (iOpts iand DD_REQUIRED) ;                    Get Validate_Required iField to iResult
13583>>>>>>>>>>>
13583>>>>>>>>>>>                If (iResult=0) Begin
13585>>>>>>>>>>>                    // First execute the user defined validation message
13585>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get Item_Validate_MSG of iObj iField to iMsg
13586>>>>>>>>>>>                    If iMsg Begin
13588>>>>>>>>>>>                        Get Field_Current_Value iField to sValue
13589>>>>>>>>>>>                        Get iMsg iField sValue to iResult
13590>>>>>>>>>>>                    End
13590>>>>>>>>>>>>
13590>>>>>>>>>>>                End
13590>>>>>>>>>>>>
13590>>>>>>>>>>>
13590>>>>>>>>>>>                // Check for keys
13590>>>>>>>>>>>                If (iResult=0 and Key_Field_State(Self, iField)) ;                    Get Validate_Key_Field iField to iResult
13593>>>>>>>>>>>
13593>>>>>>>>>>>                // Do extended validations
13593>>>>>>>>>>>                If (iResult=0) ;                    Get Validate_Field of (Field_Attributes(Self)) iField to iResult
13596>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13596>>>>>>>>>>>>
13596>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13596>>>>>>>>>>>>
13596>>>>>>>>>>>
13596>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Current_Validate_Field to 0
13597>>>>>>>>>>>        // Mark this field being validated
13597>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Visited_Fields to sValue
13598>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_Fields to (Overstrike("X", sValue, iField))
13599>>>>>>>>>>>
13599>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iResult
13600>>>>>>>>>>>
13600>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13601>>>>>>>>>>>
13601>>>>>>>>>>>
13601>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function will be called to validate a field.
13601>>>>>>>>>>>    Function File_Field_Validate_Field Integer iFile Integer iField Returns Integer
13603>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
13603>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iResult
13603>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hOldOrigin
13603>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set iFile to iDSO
13604>>>>>>>>>>>        If not iDSO ;            Function_Return 0
13607>>>>>>>>>>>
13607>>>>>>>>>>>        // This function is only called by the DEOs.
13607>>>>>>>>>>>        // It is possible for validate_item when called as part of
13607>>>>>>>>>>>        // request_validate to get called more than once
13607>>>>>>>>>>>        // when a field is foreign (it is attached to both its DDO and the
13607>>>>>>>>>>>        // child-main ddo). This makes sure the validation is only called once.
13607>>>>>>>>>>>        // (vdf7 change: previously we set OpMode to Mode_Saving and checked that, now we have
13607>>>>>>>>>>>        // a mode just for request_validate).
13607>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Operation_Mode=MODE_VALIDATING and ;         // if from request_validate            Mid(Visited_Fields(iDSO), 1, iField)="X" ) ; // and already marked            Function_Return 0                         // skip it
13610>>>>>>>>>>>
13610>>>>>>>>>>>        Move Operation_origin to hOldOrigin
13611>>>>>>>>>>>
13611>>>>>>>>>>>        // if from request_validate operation_origin will be set and should not
13611>>>>>>>>>>>        // be reset here.
13611>>>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_ORIGIN=0) Begin
13613>>>>>>>>>>>            Move Self to Operation_Origin
13614>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13614>>>>>>>>>>>>
13614>>>>>>>>>>>
13614>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Validate_Field of iDSO iField to iResult
13615>>>>>>>>>>>        Move hOldOrigin to Operation_Origin
13616>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iResult
13617>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13618>>>>>>>>>>>
13618>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function will be called to check if a key has been changed.
13618>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Key_Field Integer iField Returns Integer
13620>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sOld_Value
13620>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sNew_Value
13620>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sKeys
13620>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iState
13620>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bMultiKeys
13620>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Protect_Key_State to iState
13621>>>>>>>>>>>        If iState Begin
13623>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Key_Value to sNew_Value
13624>>>>>>>>>>>            // Only check existing records.
13624>>>>>>>>>>>            If (HasRecord(Self)) Begin
13626>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Existing_Key_Value to sOld_Value
13627>>>>>>>>>>>                If (sNew_Value <> sOld_Value) Begin
13629>>>>>>>>>>>                    // we have an error. If there is only one key field we know
13629>>>>>>>>>>>                    // where the field is and we can report that field. If we have
13629>>>>>>>>>>>                    // multiple key fields, we don't really know where the offending key change
13629>>>>>>>>>>>                    // is, so we will not report a field.
13629>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get Key_Fields to sKeys
13630>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move (Pos("X",sKeys)<>RightPos("X",sKeys)) to bMultiKeys
13631>>>>>>>>>>>                    Send Data_set_Error (If(bMultiKeys, -1, iField)) 0 DD_TEXT_NO_KEY_CHANGE_ALLOWED
13632>>>>>>>>>>>                    Function_Return 1
13633>>>>>>>>>>>                End
13633>>>>>>>>>>>>
13633>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13633>>>>>>>>>>>>
13633>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13633>>>>>>>>>>>>
13633>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13634>>>>>>>>>>>
13634>>>>>>>>>>>
13634>>>>>>>>>>>    // During request_validate process tell us if this DD has had a find_request error. This
13634>>>>>>>>>>>    // is handled by the DD that originated the request_validate. Very private
13634>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DDHasFindReqError Returns Boolean
13636>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle[] DDsWithFindReqErrors
13637>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
13637>>>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_ORIGIN) Begin
13639>>>>>>>>>>>            Get pDDsWithFindReqErrors of OPERATION_ORIGIN to DDsWithFindReqErrors
13640>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (SearchArray(Self,DDsWithFindReqErrors)) to iIndex
13641>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return (iIndex<>-1)
13642>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13642>>>>>>>>>>>>
13642>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13643>>>>>>>>>>>
13643>>>>>>>>>>>    // During a request_validate a find_request error has occurred. Add this DD
13643>>>>>>>>>>>    // to list of DDs that have this error. This is handled by the DD that
13643>>>>>>>>>>>    // originated the request_validate.  Very private
13643>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure AddDDHasFindReqError
13645>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle[] DDsWithFindReqErrors
13646>>>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_ORIGIN) Begin
13648>>>>>>>>>>>            Get pDDsWithFindReqErrors of OPERATION_ORIGIN to DDsWithFindReqErrors
13649>>>>>>>>>>>            Move Self to DDsWithFindReqErrors[SizeOfArray(DDsWithFindReqErrors)]
13650>>>>>>>>>>>            Set pDDsWithFindReqErrors of OPERATION_ORIGIN to DDsWithFindReqErrors
13651>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13651>>>>>>>>>>>>
13651>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13652>>>>>>>>>>>
13652>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function will execute the validation message for each field of the
13652>>>>>>>>>>>    // data set and all of its parents in parent first order.
13652>>>>>>>>>>>    // Pass: DoALLFg bNoStop
13652>>>>>>>>>>>    // Added bNoStop, If true, all items are validated. It is up to you to
13652>>>>>>>>>>>    // do something with the possible cascade of errors
13652>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Data_Sets Integer DoAllFg Integer bNoStop Returns Integer
13654>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
13654>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRetval
13654>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
13654>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
13654>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer bErr
13654>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDDHasFindReqError
13654>>>>>>>>>>>        // ShowLn "Validate_Data_Sets in Data_Set in " (Name(self))
13654>>>>>>>>>>>        // Validate if not foreign, or foreign new saves allowed, or
13654>>>>>>>>>>>        // foreign validation is supported (it normally is)
13654>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Operation_Origin=Self or ;            Allow_Foreign_New_Save_State(Self) or ;            Validate_Foreign_File_State(Self)) Begin
13656>>>>>>>>>>>
13656>>>>>>>>>>>            If (bNoStop) Begin
13658>>>>>>>>>>>                // if do all, it is possible that this DD as a find-req error. If so there is no
13658>>>>>>>>>>>                // need to look for more errors in this DD or its parents. This makes the do all checking
13658>>>>>>>>>>>                // a little more intelligent and doesn't return a bunch of errors when it is not needed
13658>>>>>>>>>>>                Get DDHasFindReqError to bDDHasFindReqError
13659>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13659>>>>>>>>>>>>
13659>>>>>>>>>>>
13659>>>>>>>>>>>            If (not(bDDHasFindReqError)) Begin
13661>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
13662>>>>>>>>>>>                Decrement iMax
13663>>>>>>>>>>>                For iCount from 0 to iMax
13669>>>>>>>>>>>>
13669>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get Data_Set_Server iCount to iDSO
13670>>>>>>>>>>>                    If not (Visited_state(iDSO)) Begin
13672>>>>>>>>>>>                        Get Validate_Data_Sets of iDSO DoAllFg bNoStop to bErr
13673>>>>>>>>>>>                        If bErr Begin
13675>>>>>>>>>>>                            Move bErr to iRetVal
13676>>>>>>>>>>>                            If bNoStop ;                                Move 0 to bErr
13679>>>>>>>>>>>                        End
13679>>>>>>>>>>>>
13679>>>>>>>>>>>                    End
13679>>>>>>>>>>>>
13679>>>>>>>>>>>                Until bErr
13681>>>>>>>>>>>                If not bErr Begin
13683>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get Validate_Fields DoAllFg bNoStop to bErr
13684>>>>>>>>>>>                    If bErr ;                        Move bErr to iRetVal
13687>>>>>>>>>>>                End
13687>>>>>>>>>>>>
13687>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13687>>>>>>>>>>>>
13687>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13687>>>>>>>>>>>>
13687>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
13688>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRetval
13689>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13690>>>>>>>>>>>
13690>>>>>>>>>>>    // This tests the DDO and all "up" DDOs to see if a switched parent / commit test even needs to be
13690>>>>>>>>>>>    // tested. This is called by the top ValidateSwitchedCommittedParents to see if a switch parent test
13690>>>>>>>>>>>    // even needs to be applied before it has to refinds records.
13690>>>>>>>>>>>    // Return true is there is nothing to test (i.e., the shortcut worked).
13690>>>>>>>>>>>    Function IsCommittedRecursiveUpParentChangeAllowed Returns Boolean
13692>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bAllowed bCommitted bVisited bHasRecord
13692>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iServers iSrvr iParent
13692>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoSrvr
13692>>>>>>>>>>>
13692>>>>>>>>>>>
13692>>>>>>>>>>>        // optimization. We only test committed parents if one parent does not allow changing committed records.
13692>>>>>>>>>>>        // This avoids extra finds and relates when not needed
13692>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
13693>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iServers
13694>>>>>>>>>>>        Get IsCommitted to bCommitted
13695>>>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iSrvr
13696>>>>>>>>>>>        Move True to bAllowed
13697>>>>>>>>>>>        While (iSrvr<iServers and bAllowed)
13701>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iSrvr to hoSrvr
13702>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoSrvr to iParent
13703>>>>>>>>>>>            // if committed and parent change not allowed, we are done
13703>>>>>>>>>>>            If (bCommitted) Begin
13705>>>>>>>>>>>                Get IsCommittedParentChangeAllowed iParent to bAllowed
13706>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13706>>>>>>>>>>>>
13706>>>>>>>>>>>            // if still allowed, check all parents
13706>>>>>>>>>>>            If (bAllowed) Begin
13708>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Visited_State of hoSrvr to bVisited
13709>>>>>>>>>>>                If not bVisited Begin
13711>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get IsCommittedRecursiveUpParentChangeAllowed of hoSrvr to bAllowed
13712>>>>>>>>>>>                End
13712>>>>>>>>>>>>
13712>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13712>>>>>>>>>>>>
13712>>>>>>>>>>>            Increment iSrvr
13713>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13714>>>>>>>>>>>>
13714>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bAllowed
13715>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13716>>>>>>>>>>>
13716>>>>>>>>>>>
13716>>>>>>>>>>>    // special validate-save check for changed committed parent. If the record is committed
13716>>>>>>>>>>>    // and it has a switched parent and this is not allowed, we have an error. This should rarely happen because the
13716>>>>>>>>>>>    // DEOs should guard aginst this. This is a recursive routine that requires special attention the first time through.
13716>>>>>>>>>>>    // When called from the we must refind the original record and all original parents. This way we can compare these parent
13716>>>>>>>>>>>    // rowids to the DD row id (if different, they've changed). At the end we must restore the DD records. Because this takes time
13716>>>>>>>>>>>    // we only even do this if this is committed and there is a chance that there are changed parents
13716>>>>>>>>>>>
13716>>>>>>>>>>>    Function ValidateSwitchedCommittedParents Boolean bTop Returns Boolean
13718>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iServers iSrvr iMain iParent iPMain
13718>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoSrvr
13718>>>>>>>>>>>        RowID riCrnt riParent riPCrnt
13718>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bChanged bCommitted bAllowed bErr bParentChanged bVisited
13718>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bHasRecord bPHasRecord bFound
13718>>>>>>>>>>>
13718>>>>>>>>>>>
13718>>>>>>>>>>>        // Shortcut optimization. This tests for any committed DDO with a parent that doesn't allow a switch
13718>>>>>>>>>>>        // return true if there is any reason to actually test any DDO up the tree for a parent change
13718>>>>>>>>>>>        If bTop Begin
13720>>>>>>>>>>>            // init visited nodes, these will be tested and set in IsCommittedRecursiveUpParentChangeAllowed
13720>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Initialize_Visited False False //false=up only, true=clear fields
13721>>>>>>>>>>>            Get IsCommittedRecursiveUpParentChangeAllowed to bAllowed
13722>>>>>>>>>>>            If bAllowed Begin
13724>>>>>>>>>>>                Function_Return False // if all are allowed, we have nothing to test - its ok
13725>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13725>>>>>>>>>>>>
13725>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13725>>>>>>>>>>>>
13725>>>>>>>>>>>
13725>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain
13726>>>>>>>>>>>        Get CurrentRowId to riCrnt
13727>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iServers
13728>>>>>>>>>>>        Get HasRecord to bHasRecord
13729>>>>>>>>>>>
13729>>>>>>>>>>>        If (bHasRecord and (bTop or not(IsSameRowID(GetRowID(iMain),riCrnt))) ) Begin
13731>>>>>>>>>>>            // this refinds the main record and, most importantly, relates all original parents on up
13731>>>>>>>>>>>            // We now have the original parents which we can test to see if they are changed.
13731>>>>>>>>>>>            Get ReadByRowIdEx iMain riCrnt to bFound
13732>>>>>>>>>>>            If not bFound Begin
13734>>>>>>>>>>>                Error DFERR_CANT_REFIND_RECORD
13735>>>>>>>>>>>>
13735>>>>>>>>>>>                Function_Return True
13736>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13736>>>>>>>>>>>>
13736>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13736>>>>>>>>>>>>
13736>>>>>>>>>>>
13736>>>>>>>>>>>        If (bTop) Begin
13738>>>>>>>>>>>            // If at start, init visited nodes, these will be tested and set during recursive calls to this function
13738>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Initialize_Visited False False // false=up only, true=clear fields
13739>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13739>>>>>>>>>>>>
13739>>>>>>>>>>>
13739>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
13740>>>>>>>>>>>        Get IsCommitted to bCommitted
13741>>>>>>>>>>>        If bCommitted Begin
13743>>>>>>>>>>>            // Parent_Changed_State tells us a parent is changed but not which one. Look at each child to see if it is changed.
13743>>>>>>>>>>>            // First see any any of the parents are changed.
13743>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Parent_Changed_State to bChanged
13744>>>>>>>>>>>            If bChanged Begin
13746>>>>>>>>>>>                // Parent_Changed_State tells us a parent is changed but not which one. Look at each child to see if it is changed.
13746>>>>>>>>>>>                Move 0 to iSrvr
13747>>>>>>>>>>>                While (iSrvr<iServers and not(bErr))
13751>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get Data_Set_Server iSrvr to hoSrvr
13752>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get Main_File of hoSrvr to iParent
13753>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get CurrentRowId of hoSrvr to riParent
13754>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move (not(IsSameRowID(GetRowID(iParent),riParent))) to bParentChanged // is parent changed?
13755>>>>>>>>>>>                    If bParentChanged Begin
13757>>>>>>>>>>>                        Get IsCommittedParentChangeAllowed iParent to bAllowed // is changing committed parent allowed?
13758>>>>>>>>>>>                        If not bAllowed Begin
13760>>>>>>>>>>>                            Move True to bErr
13761>>>>>>>>>>>                            If bErr Begin
13763>>>>>>>>>>>                                Send Data_Set_Error of hoSrvr -1 0 DD_CANNOT_SWITCH_PARENT
13764>>>>>>>>>>>                            End
13764>>>>>>>>>>>>
13764>>>>>>>>>>>                        End
13764>>>>>>>>>>>>
13764>>>>>>>>>>>                    End
13764>>>>>>>>>>>>
13764>>>>>>>>>>>                    Increment iSrvr
13765>>>>>>>>>>>                Loop
13766>>>>>>>>>>>>
13766>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13766>>>>>>>>>>>>
13766>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13766>>>>>>>>>>>>
13766>>>>>>>>>>>
13766>>>>>>>>>>>        // no error in immediate we must continue this check up the parent tree.
13766>>>>>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iSrvr
13767>>>>>>>>>>>        While (iSrvr<iServers and not(bErr))
13771>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iSrvr to hoSrvr
13772>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoSrvr to bVisited
13773>>>>>>>>>>>            If (not(bVisited)) Begin
13775>>>>>>>>>>>
13775>>>>>>>>>>>                // if new record, we need to refind parent records from here since you cannot
13775>>>>>>>>>>>                // have done a find/relate on a new record.
13775>>>>>>>>>>>                If (not(bHasRecord)) Begin
13777>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get HasRecord of hoSrvr to bPHasRecord
13778>>>>>>>>>>>                    If (bPHasRecord) Begin
13780>>>>>>>>>>>                        Get Main_File of hoSrvr to iPMain
13781>>>>>>>>>>>                        Get CurrentRowId of hoSrvr to riPCrnt
13782>>>>>>>>>>>                        If (not(IsNullRowID(riPCrnt))) Begin
13784>>>>>>>>>>>                            Get ReadByRowIdEx of hoSrvr iPMain riPCrnt to bFound
13785>>>>>>>>>>>                            If not bFound Begin
13787>>>>>>>>>>>                                Error DFERR_CANT_REFIND_RECORD
13788>>>>>>>>>>>>
13788>>>>>>>>>>>                                Function_Return True
13789>>>>>>>>>>>                            End
13789>>>>>>>>>>>>
13789>>>>>>>>>>>                        End
13789>>>>>>>>>>>>
13789>>>>>>>>>>>                    End
13789>>>>>>>>>>>>
13789>>>>>>>>>>>                End
13789>>>>>>>>>>>>
13789>>>>>>>>>>>
13789>>>>>>>>>>>                Get ValidateSwitchedCommittedParents of hoSrvr False to bErr // call recursively up the parent tree
13790>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13790>>>>>>>>>>>>
13790>>>>>>>>>>>            Increment iSrvr
13791>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13792>>>>>>>>>>>>
13792>>>>>>>>>>>
13792>>>>>>>>>>>        If bTop Begin // if back to the top, make sure our buffers are correct.
13794>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Refind_Records
13795>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13795>>>>>>>>>>>>
13795>>>>>>>>>>>
13795>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bErr
13796>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13797>>>>>>>>>>>
13797>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Entry_Update_Data_Sets Integer iFile Integer iAll
13799>>>>>>>>>>>
13799>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoBuff hoDSO
13799>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bCommit bIsFind bVisited bIsForeign
13799>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax iCount iItems iOpts iChanges
13799>>>>>>>>>>>
13799>>>>>>>>>>>
13799>>>>>>>>>>>        Move record_buffer to hoBuff
13800>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (OPERATION_MODE<>MODE_SAVING) to bIsFind
13801>>>>>>>>>>>
13801>>>>>>>>>>>        // first recurse to all parent ddos
13801>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
13802>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
13803>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
13809>>>>>>>>>>>>
13809>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hoDSO
13810>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoDSO to bVisited
13811>>>>>>>>>>>            If not (bVisited) Begin
13813>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Entry_Update_Data_Sets to hoDSO iFile iAll
13814>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13814>>>>>>>>>>>>
13814>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13815>>>>>>>>>>>>
13815>>>>>>>>>>>
13815>>>>>>>>>>>        // if find, we only do this if the main file is the same as the find file
13815>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bIsFind) or iFile=Main_File(Self)) Begin
13817>>>>>>>>>>>            If (not(bIsFind)) Begin
13819>>>>>>>>>>>                // if a save, we care if it is committed.
13819>>>>>>>>>>>                Get IsCommitted to bCommit
13820>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13820>>>>>>>>>>>>
13820>>>>>>>>>>>
13820>>>>>>>>>>>            // pass if Find (True) or save (False). We only care about commit on saves
13820>>>>>>>>>>>            // The setting of bIsForeign is an approximation. Foreign is really a DEO and and not
13820>>>>>>>>>>>            // a DD concept - in fact, at this point we don't really know. For example, a save in a header/dtl
13820>>>>>>>>>>>            // detail DEO (ordrdtl grid)has header DEOs that are not really foreign. This test errs on the side
13820>>>>>>>>>>>            // of assuming it's foreign. This would cause problems with incorrect parent NoPuts except we also
13820>>>>>>>>>>>            // set a flag, Field_NoPutValueChangedByDeo, when a field is changed via a NoPut DEO. The DD will still update
13820>>>>>>>>>>>            // foreign NoPuts unless this field flag is set.
13820>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (OPERATION_ORIGIN<>Self and Allow_Foreign_New_Save_State(Self)=0) to bIsForeign
13821>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Entry_Update of hoBuff bIsFind (If(bCommit,1,0) + If(bIsForeign,2,0))
13822>>>>>>>>>>>
13822>>>>>>>>>>>            // also move data from extended dd fields to buffer
13822>>>>>>>>>>>            Send ExtendedFieldsUpdate (not(bIsFind))
13823>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13823>>>>>>>>>>>>
13823>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
13824>>>>>>>>>>>
13824>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13825>>>>>>>>>>>
13825>>>>>>>>>>>    // is this field NoPut based passed Commit and Foreign flags.
13825>>>>>>>>>>>    Function FieldNoPut Integer iField Boolean bIsCommited Boolean bIsForeign Returns Boolean
13827>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bNoPut
13827>>>>>>>>>>>        // this uses runtime logic - the same use for moving DD Buffer to Field Buffer
13827>>>>>>>>>>>        Get IsFieldDDNoPut of Record_Buffer iField (If(bIsCommited,1,0) + If(bIsForeign,2,0)) to bNoPut
13828>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bNoPut
13829>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13830>>>>>>>>>>>
13830>>>>>>>>>>>
13830>>>>>>>>>>>    // Check that Server data-sets exist for all required server file numbers
13830>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Valid_Servers Returns Integer
13832>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRval
13832>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
13832>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
13832>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
13832>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iPos
13832>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
13832>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sFiles
13832>>>>>>>>>>>
13832>>>>>>>>>>>        // First assemble a string of all server file#s in ','##',' format
13832>>>>>>>>>>>        Move ',' to sFiles
13833>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
13834>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
13835>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
13841>>>>>>>>>>>>
13841>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to iDSO
13842>>>>>>>>>>>            Move ( sFiles + String(Main_file(iDSO)) + ",") to sFiles
13843>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13844>>>>>>>>>>>>
13844>>>>>>>>>>>
13844>>>>>>>>>>>        // Make sure each required File exists
13844>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server_File_Count to iMax
13845>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
13846>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
13852>>>>>>>>>>>>
13852>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Server_File iCount to iFile
13853>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Pos ( ','+String(iFile)+',' , sFiles)) to iPos
13854>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iPos = 0) ;                Move iFile to iRVal
13857>>>>>>>>>>>        Until iRval
13859>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRVal
13860>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13861>>>>>>>>>>>
13861>>>>>>>>>>>
13861>>>>>>>>>>>    // Check that Client data-sets exist for all required Client file numbers
13861>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Valid_Clients Returns Integer
13863>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRval
13863>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
13863>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
13863>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iDSO
13863>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iPos
13863>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
13863>>>>>>>>>>>        String  sFiles
13863>>>>>>>>>>>
13863>>>>>>>>>>>        // First assemble a string of all Client file#s in ','##',' format
13863>>>>>>>>>>>        Move ',' to sFiles
13864>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
13865>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
13866>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
13872>>>>>>>>>>>>
13872>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to iDSO
13873>>>>>>>>>>>            Move ( sFiles + String(Main_file(iDSO))+",") to sFiles
13874>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
13875>>>>>>>>>>>>
13875>>>>>>>>>>>
13875>>>>>>>>>>>        // Make sure each required File exists
13875>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Client_File_Count to iMax
13876>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
13877>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
13883>>>>>>>>>>>>
13883>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Client_File iCount to iFile
13884>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Pos( ','+String(iFile)+',', sFiles)) to iPos
13885>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iPos = 0) ;                Move iFile to iRVal
13888>>>>>>>>>>>        Until iRval
13890>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRVal
13891>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13892>>>>>>>>>>>
13892>>>>>>>>>>>
13892>>>>>>>>>>>    // Validates save updating connections. If error returns file# that is
13892>>>>>>>>>>>    // expected and missing. If no error Set Validated_Save_connectio_State
13892>>>>>>>>>>>    // indicating that the connection validation has occurred and is ok
13892>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Save_Structure Integer ForceFg Returns Integer
13894>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRval
13894>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMode
13894>>>>>>>>>>>        If not ForceFg Begin
13896>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Validate_Save_Structure_Mode to iMode
13897>>>>>>>>>>>            Move ( iMode=DD_VALIDATE_STRUCTURE_ALWAYS or ;                (iMode=DD_VALIDATE_STRUCTURE_ONCE and ;                Save_Structure_Validated_state(Self)=0 ) ) ;                to ForceFg
13898>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13898>>>>>>>>>>>>
13898>>>>>>>>>>>        If ForceFg Begin
13900>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Valid_Structure False to iRval
13901>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iRVal = 0) ;                Set Save_Structure_Validated_State to True
13904>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13904>>>>>>>>>>>>
13904>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRVal
13905>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13906>>>>>>>>>>>
13906>>>>>>>>>>>    // Validates Delete Structure. If cascade_state is true this must check
13906>>>>>>>>>>>    // up and down the tree. If no cascade_state just check up the tree.  If
13906>>>>>>>>>>>    // Ok, set Validated_Delete_no_Cascade_Connection_State and and or
13906>>>>>>>>>>>    // Validated_Delete_Cascade_Connection_State
13906>>>>>>>>>>>    // Pass: ForceFg - if TRUE force the validation.
13906>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Validate_Delete_Structure Integer ForceFg Returns Integer
13908>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCascade
13908>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMode
13908>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iSt
13908>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRval
13908>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Cascade_delete_State to iCascade
13909>>>>>>>>>>>        If not ForceFg Begin
13911>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Validate_Delete_Structure_Mode to iMode
13912>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iMode=DD_VALIDATE_STRUCTURE_ONCE and iCascade );                Get Cascade_Delete_Structure_Validated_state to iSt
13915>>>>>>>>>>>            Else ;                Get No_Cascade_Delete_Structure_Validated_state to iSt
13917>>>>>>>>>>>            Move ( iMode=DD_VALIDATE_STRUCTURE_ALWAYS or ;                (iMode=DD_VALIDATE_STRUCTURE_ONCE and iSt=0) ) to ForceFg
13918>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13918>>>>>>>>>>>>
13918>>>>>>>>>>>
13918>>>>>>>>>>>        If ForceFg Begin
13920>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Valid_Structure iCascade to iRval
13921>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iRval = 0) Begin
13923>>>>>>>>>>>                Set No_Cascade_Delete_Structure_Validated_State to True
13924>>>>>>>>>>>                If iCascade ;                    Set Cascade_Delete_Structure_Validated_State to True
13927>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13927>>>>>>>>>>>>
13927>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13927>>>>>>>>>>>>
13927>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRval
13928>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13929>>>>>>>>>>>
13929>>>>>>>>>>>
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure will be called whenever the Data_Set wants its DEOs to
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // write their values to the record buffer. The value of OPERATION_MODE
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // determines if this is for finding an record or before saving a record.
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // We use this event to tell our Record_Buffer to update the
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // global record buffer.
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // Modified to visit all server DSOs
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // Note that this is only sent to the DSO starting the operation.
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // We must manually send this to all server data-sets ourselves
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // Note that during a DSO save this will get passed iFile=0 and iAll=3
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // Changed to Support EntryUpdateLocalState (private)
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // as of 17.0, EntryUpdateLocalState is True which means that entry_updates
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    // for finds now through the DD Buffer (saves always did).
13929>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Entry_Update Integer iFile Integer iAll
13931>>>>>>>>>>>        If ((Operation_Mode=MODE_SAVING and iAll=3) or (EntryUpdateLocalState(Self)) ) Begin //3=dso save
13933>>>>>>>>>>>            If (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_WAITING) Begin
13935>>>>>>>>>>>                // we will only not be in an operation if we are doing a find with EntryUpdateLocalState
13935>>>>>>>>>>>                // set to true. In such a case make this a finding. I am not this is actually needed
13935>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Update_Focus_Field_For_Operation MODE_FINDING
13936>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13936>>>>>>>>>>>>
13936>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
13937>>>>>>>>>>>                // if here we already have an operation_mode so there is no need to do anything special
13937>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Update_Focus_Field // Make sure buffer has latest focus item changes
13938>>>>>>>>>>>            End
13938>>>>>>>>>>>>
13938>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Initialize_Visited False False // Clear up, do not clear fields
13939>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Entry_Update_Data_Sets iFile iAll
13940>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13940>>>>>>>>>>>>
13940>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Request_Entry_Update iFile iAll
13942>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13943>>>>>>>>>>>
13943>>>>>>>>>>>
13943>>>>>>>>>>>
13943>>>>>>>>>>>    // Forces the focus field to get update its value with the data-set.
13943>>>>>>>>>>>    // This insures that the DSO and DEO contain the same values.
13943>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Update_Focus_Field
13945>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFocObj
13945>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Focus of desktop to iFocObj
13946>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Extended_DEO_State(iFocObj)) ;            Send Update_Focus_Field to iFocObj
13949>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13950>>>>>>>>>>>
13950>>>>>>>>>>>    // very internal. Used to set Operation_mode and Operation_origin before the
13950>>>>>>>>>>>    // update. A developer can use this in the DEO to know what state the update is in.
13950>>>>>>>>>>>    // This was created because a DEO value change will trigger an OnChange event and you
13950>>>>>>>>>>>    // can look at this and know that this is part of a DD operation.
13950>>>>>>>>>>>    // This is *only* called by the DD operations in this class and the change is made for as
13950>>>>>>>>>>>    // small of a period as possible.
13950>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Update_Focus_Field_For_Operation Integer iOperationMode
13952>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOldMode iOldOrigin
13952>>>>>>>>>>>
13952>>>>>>>>>>>        Move OPERATION_MODE to iOldMode
13953>>>>>>>>>>>        Move OPERATION_ORIGIN to iOldOrigin
13954>>>>>>>>>>>        Move iOperationMode to OPERATION_MODE
13955>>>>>>>>>>>        Move Self to OPERATION_ORIGIN
13956>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Update_Focus_Field
13957>>>>>>>>>>>        Move iOldMode to OPERATION_MODE
13958>>>>>>>>>>>        Move iOldOrigin to OPERATION_ORIGIN
13959>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
13960>>>>>>>>>>>
13960>>>>>>>>>>>
13960>>>>>>>>>>>    // Augment to validate all field values that do not get
13960>>>>>>>>>>>    // validated as part of the item validation process. The advantage
13960>>>>>>>>>>>    // of item validation (over only field validation) is that an error
13960>>>>>>>>>>>    // returns you to the offending item.
13960>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Request_Validate Returns Integer
13962>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRetval iOldOrigin iOldMode iRetVal2
13962>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle[] DDsWithFindReqErrors
13963>>>>>>>>>>>
13963>>>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_WAITING) Begin
13965>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Update_Focus_Field_For_Operation MODE_VALIDATING // added 12.1/15.1
13966>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13966>>>>>>>>>>>>
13966>>>>>>>>>>>        Move Operation_Origin to iOldOrigin
13967>>>>>>>>>>>        Move Self to Operation_Origin
13968>>>>>>>>>>>        Move Operation_Mode to iOldMode
13969>>>>>>>>>>>        // clear all find req DD markers at the origin of the validate request. When request validates occur
13969>>>>>>>>>>>        // they will get added to this array and can be tested to see of such an error has occurred.
13969>>>>>>>>>>>        Set pDDsWithFindReqErrors to DDsWithFindReqErrors
13970>>>>>>>>>>>        // Prior to VDF7, we set this to Mode_Saving. We now have a special mode just for request_validate.
13970>>>>>>>>>>>        // We do this because:
13970>>>>>>>>>>>        //   1) because it is useful (more detail never hurts) and
13970>>>>>>>>>>>        //   2) we will allow set_field_current_value to update when mode_validation is set
13970>>>>>>>>>>>        Move MODE_VALIDATING to Operation_Mode
13971>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Initialize_Visited False True //false=up only, true=clear fields
13972>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Get Request_Validate to iRetval // normal deo validate
13974>>>>>>>>>>>        // If DEO validation failed, do not validate other fields unless Validate_All_Fields is set
13974>>>>>>>>>>>        If ( (iRetval=0 or (Validate_All_Fields_State(Self))) and Validate_DEOs_Only_State(Self)=0) Begin
13976>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Validate_Data_Sets False (Validate_All_Fields_State(Self)) to iRetval2
13977>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (iRetval or iRetVal2) to iRetval
13978>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13978>>>>>>>>>>>>
13978>>>>>>>>>>>
13978>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iRetval=0) Begin
13980>>>>>>>>>>>            Get ValidateSwitchedCommittedParents True to iRetval
13981>>>>>>>>>>>        End
13981>>>>>>>>>>>>
13981>>>>>>>>>>>
13981>>>>>>>>>>>        Move iOldMode   to Operation_Mode
13982>>>>>>>>>>>        Move iOldOrigin to Operation_Origin
13983>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRetval
13984>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13985>>>>>>>>>>>
13985>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Request_Validate_All Returns Integer
13987>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer bOld iRetVal
13987>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Validate_All_Fields_State to bOld
13988>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Validate_All_Fields_State to True
13989>>>>>>>>>>>        Get request_validate to iretVal
13990>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Validate_All_Fields_State to bOld
13991>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iRetval
13992>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
13993>>>>>>>>>>>
13993>>>>>>>>>>>
13993>>>>>>>>>>>
13993>>>>>>>>>>>    // Like Item_find except entry-update is forced through the DD, not DEO
13993>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure File_Field_Find Integer iFindMode Integer iFile Integer iField ;            Integer bEntUpdt  Integer bShowErr Integer bDfrd
13995>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer bOld
13995>>>>>>>>>>>        Get EntryUpdateLocalState to bOld
13996>>>>>>>>>>>        Set EntryUpdateLocalState to True
13997>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Item_Find iFindMode iFile iField bEntUpdt bShowErr bDfrd
13998>>>>>>>>>>>        Set EntryUpdateLocalState to bOld
13999>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14000>>>>>>>>>>>
14000>>>>>>>>>>>    // Autofind for requestd file, field and mode.
14000>>>>>>>>>>>    //    If mode not passed, EQ is assummed
14000>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure File_Field_AutoFind Integer iFile Integer iField Integer iFindMode
14002>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer eMode
14002>>>>>>>>>>>        If iFile  Begin
14004>>>>>>>>>>>            // if no 3rd argument, default to autofind
14004>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (If(Num_Arguments<3,EQ,iFindMode)) to eMode
14005>>>>>>>>>>>            Send File_Field_Find eMode iFile iField True False False
14006>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14006>>>>>>>>>>>>
14006>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14007>>>>>>>>>>>
14007>>>>>>>>>>>    // Autofind in default mode (does not set changed states). Can be used
14007>>>>>>>>>>>    // within Clear and Clear_all to autofind parents. Parent values can be
14007>>>>>>>>>>>    // maintained using retainAll option
14007>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure File_Field_Default_AutoFind Integer iFile Integer iField
14009>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iOldState
14009>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle  hoDD
14009>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_set iFile to hoDD
14010>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoDD Begin
14012>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Change_disabled_State of hoDD to iOldState
14013>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Change_disabled_State of hoDD to True
14014>>>>>>>>>>>            Send File_Field_AutoFind  of hoDD iFile iField EQ
14015>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Change_disabled_State of hoDD to iOldState
14016>>>>>>>>>>>            Set changed_state to False
14017>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14017>>>>>>>>>>>>
14017>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14018>>>>>>>>>>>
14018>>>>>>>>>>>    // File_Index_find
14018>>>>>>>>>>>    // Like item_find except you pass the index you want to find with and
14018>>>>>>>>>>>    // ent-update occurs through DDO buffers not deo buffers.
14018>>>>>>>>>>>    // This is currently private and is only used by web-applications
14018>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure File_Index_Find Integer iFindMode Integer iFile Integer iIndex ;            Integer bEntUpdt  Integer bShowErr Integer bDfrd
14020>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer bOld
14020>>>>>>>>>>>        RowID riRec
14020>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer wasChanged hDD iOldStat
14020>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOk
14020>>>>>>>>>>>
14020>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set iFile to hDD
14021>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hDD=0) Begin
14023>>>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM C_$CannotFindDD
14024>>>>>>>>>>>>
14024>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
14025>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14025>>>>>>>>>>>>
14025>>>>>>>>>>>
14025>>>>>>>>>>>        Get EntryUpdateLocalState to bOld
14026>>>>>>>>>>>        Set EntryUpdateLocalState to True
14027>>>>>>>>>>>
14027>>>>>>>>>>>        //  'hold' buffer to prepare for entry_update
14027>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (getRowId(iFile)) to riRec
14028>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_STATUS of iFile to iOldStat
14031>>>>>>>>>>>        Set_Attribute DF_FILE_STATUS of iFile to DF_FILE_INACTIVE
14034>>>>>>>>>>>
14034>>>>>>>>>>>        If bEntUpdt Begin
14036>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Request_Entry_Update to hDD iFile 1  //entUpdt all DEOs as required
14037>>>>>>>>>>>
14037>>>>>>>>>>>            //
14037>>>>>>>>>>>            // we really only need to know if any segment of the index changed
14037>>>>>>>>>>>            // but since we don't have field-changed flags, we look at the
14037>>>>>>>>>>>            // whole recbuf - this is consistent with 2.3b and 3.0 non-dataset
14037>>>>>>>>>>>            // behavior.
14037>>>>>>>>>>>            //
14037>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (iOldStat<>DF_FILE_INACTIVE) to wasChanged
14038>>>>>>>>>>>            If not wasChanged ;                Get_Attribute DF_FILE_CHANGED of iFile to wasChanged
14043>>>>>>>>>>>            If not wasChanged ;                Constrained_Clear iFindMode iFile by iIndex
14048>>>>>>>>>>>
14048>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14048>>>>>>>>>>>>
14048>>>>>>>>>>>        Move False to Err
14049>>>>>>>>>>>        If bDfrd ;            Send Request_Read iFindMode iFile iIndex
14052>>>>>>>>>>>        Else ;            Send Request_Find iFindMode iFile iIndex
14054>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(Found) and  not(err)) Begin
14056>>>>>>>>>>>            // refind original record (or leave it cleared if not record)
14056>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (FindByRowId(iFile,riRec)) to bOk
14057>>>>>>>>>>>
14057>>>>>>>>>>>            If bShowErr ;                Error (If(iFindMode<2, DFERR_FIND_PRIOR_BEG_OF_FILE, DFERR_FIND_PAST_END_OF_FILE))
14060>>>>>>>>>>>            Move False to Err
14061>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14061>>>>>>>>>>>>
14061>>>>>>>>>>>        Set EntryUpdateLocalState to bOld
14062>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14063>>>>>>>>>>>
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // This does a refind of all records based on the contents of the
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // refine_record_id property.
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // This would be used after clearing the DDs and loading the local rencum
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // buffer with recnums. This can be used by remote DEOs (BPOs).
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    //
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // Find all existing records. This must be done in bottom-up, breadth
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // first order. i.e., Start with the passed DD, find it and then find for
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // parents. Only find if the record is non-zero and it is different than
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // the current_record.
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // This order will allow us to support changed parents.
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // Don't use this if you do not understand what it does.
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // Private.Find_Records is a helper. We will keep this private because
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    // it is rather specialized and only used by WebApp.
14063>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_Records
14065>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Initialize_Visited False False // Clear up, do not clear fields
14066>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Private.Find_Records           // refind all records in upward sweep
14067>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14068>>>>>>>>>>>
14068>>>>>>>>>>>
14068>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Private.Find_Records
14070>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hPrnt
14070>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax
14070>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCount
14070>>>>>>>>>>>        RowID riRec
14070>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRec iMain
14070>>>>>>>>>>>        // works with both recId and rowId. Only one should ever be set.
14070>>>>>>>>>>>        // find(clear) record, if needed
14070>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain
14071>>>>>>>>>>>        // assume that either prFindRowId or Find_record_id has a value - never both
14071>>>>>>>>>>>        // also assume Find_record_id only has values when you are using a recnum table
14071>>>>>>>>>>>        Get prFindRowId to riRec
14072>>>>>>>>>>>        If not (IsNullRowId(riRec)) Begin
14074>>>>>>>>>>>            If not (IsSameRowId(riRec, CurrentRowId(Self) ) ) Begin
14076>>>>>>>>>>>                Send FindByRowId iMain riRec // find an Relate all parents
14077>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14077>>>>>>>>>>>>
14077>>>>>>>>>>>            Set prFindRowId to (NullRowId())  // reset refind rec back to zero.
14078>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14078>>>>>>>>>>>>
14078>>>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
14079>>>>>>>>>>>            // if this has a recnum, it better be a recnum table or an error will occur.
14079>>>>>>>>>>>            // This is not being tested for a recnum table on purpose. If someone is setting Find_record_id
14079>>>>>>>>>>>            // on a non-recnum table, they doing something wrong. An Error will be a good thing.
14079>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Find_Record_Id to iRec
14080>>>>>>>>>>>            If iRec Begin
14082>>>>>>>>>>>                If (iRec<>Current_record(Self)) Begin
14084>>>>>>>>>>>                    Send Find_By_Recnum iMain iRec // find an Relate all parents
14085>>>>>>>>>>>                End
14085>>>>>>>>>>>>
14085>>>>>>>>>>>                Set Find_record_id to 0 // reset refind rec back to zero.
14086>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14086>>>>>>>>>>>>
14086>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14086>>>>>>>>>>>>
14086>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
14087>>>>>>>>>>>
14087>>>>>>>>>>>        // recurse and do the same to all parent files
14087>>>>>>>>>>>        // in almost all cases, there will be no new finding here since the relate has
14087>>>>>>>>>>>        // found the records. If the record is different than the relate, we have
14087>>>>>>>>>>>        // a switched parent state (should_save will be set appropriately).
14087>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
14088>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
14089>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
14095>>>>>>>>>>>>
14095>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hPrnt
14096>>>>>>>>>>>            If not (Visited_state(hPrnt)) ;                Send Private.Find_Records to hPrnt
14099>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
14100>>>>>>>>>>>>
14100>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14101>>>>>>>>>>>
14101>>>>>>>>>>>    // This Mark_Id creates a sequence Id for this clear. This way
14101>>>>>>>>>>>    // DDOs only get cleared one time during this process.
14101>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure IncrementCurrentMarkId
14103>>>>>>>>>>>        If (DD_Current_Mark_ID>65536) Begin
14105>>>>>>>>>>>            Move 0 to DD_Current_Mark_id
14106>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14106>>>>>>>>>>>>
14106>>>>>>>>>>>        Increment DD_Current_Mark_id
14107>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14108>>>>>>>>>>>
14108>>>>>>>>>>>
14108>>>>>>>>>>>    // private use by new webapp framework as of 18.2.
14108>>>>>>>>>>>    // pass bStart as True if this is the start of the resynch.
14108>>>>>>>>>>>    Function ReSyncRecords Boolean bStart Returns Handle
14110>>>>>>>>>>>        RowID riRowId riCrnt
14110>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOk bOldReSync bVisited
14110>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoOtherDDO hoBadDDO hoBadPrntDDO
14110>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax iCount iMain
14110>>>>>>>>>>>
14110>>>>>>>>>>>        If bStart Begin
14112>>>>>>>>>>>            Send InitializeAllVisited
14113>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14113>>>>>>>>>>>>
14113>>>>>>>>>>>
14113>>>>>>>>>>>        // we want depth first traversal. Make sure children are handled before parents
14113>>>>>>>>>>>        // Recursively traverse Children, Find by RowId, Recursively traverse Parents
14113>>>>>>>>>>>        // Use visited_state logic to avoid multiple visits caused by diamond DDO strutures
14113>>>>>>>>>>>
14113>>>>>>>>>>>        //mark first so we don't visit this coming back up.
14113>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
14114>>>>>>>>>>>
14114>>>>>>>>>>>        // traverse downward first
14114>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
14115>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
14121>>>>>>>>>>>>
14121>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to hoOtherDDO
14122>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoOtherDDO to bVisited
14123>>>>>>>>>>>            If not bVisited Begin
14125>>>>>>>>>>>                Get ReSyncRecords of hoOtherDDO False to hoBadPrntDDO
14126>>>>>>>>>>>                If (hoBadPrntDDO and not(hoBadDDO)) Begin
14128>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move hoBadPrntDDO to hoBadDDO
14129>>>>>>>>>>>                End
14129>>>>>>>>>>>>
14129>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14129>>>>>>>>>>>>
14129>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
14130>>>>>>>>>>>>
14130>>>>>>>>>>>
14130>>>>>>>>>>>        // Find record for DD. It might already be correct if child has already
14130>>>>>>>>>>>        // related it in. If not correct after a relate, this has been switched by this
14130>>>>>>>>>>>        // user or switched by another user, in which case it will be swtitched back
14130>>>>>>>>>>>        // (DDOs have always worked this way).
14130>>>>>>>>>>>        Get prFindRowId to riRowId
14131>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain
14132>>>>>>>>>>>        Get CurrentRowId to riCrnt
14133>>>>>>>>>>>        If ( not(IsSameRowId(riRowID, riCrnt)) ) Begin
14135>>>>>>>>>>>            Get pbInReSync to bOldReSync
14136>>>>>>>>>>>            Set pbInReSync to True
14137>>>>>>>>>>>
14137>>>>>>>>>>>            If (IsNullRowId(riRowID)) Begin
14139>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Clear
14140>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14140>>>>>>>>>>>>
14140>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
14141>>>>>>>>>>>                Get FindByRowIdExNoAutoFill iMain riRowId to bOk
14142>>>>>>>>>>>                If not bOk Begin
14144>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move Self to hoBadDDO
14145>>>>>>>>>>>                End
14145>>>>>>>>>>>>
14145>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14145>>>>>>>>>>>>
14145>>>>>>>>>>>            Set pbInReSync to bOldReSync
14146>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14146>>>>>>>>>>>>
14146>>>>>>>>>>>
14146>>>>>>>>>>>        // finally traverse to parents
14146>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
14147>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
14153>>>>>>>>>>>>
14153>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hoOtherDDO
14154>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoOtherDDO to bVisited
14155>>>>>>>>>>>            If not bVisited Begin
14157>>>>>>>>>>>                Get ReSyncRecords of hoOtherDDO False to hoBadPrntDDO
14158>>>>>>>>>>>                If (hoBadPrntDDO and not(hoBadDDO)) Begin
14160>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move hoBadPrntDDO to hoBadDDO
14161>>>>>>>>>>>                End
14161>>>>>>>>>>>>
14161>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14161>>>>>>>>>>>>
14161>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
14162>>>>>>>>>>>>
14162>>>>>>>>>>>
14162>>>>>>>>>>>        If bStart Begin
14164>>>>>>>>>>>            Send InitializeAllVisited
14165>>>>>>>>>>>            Send ResetChangedStates
14166>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14166>>>>>>>>>>>>
14166>>>>>>>>>>>
14166>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoBadDDO
14167>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
14168>>>>>>>>>>>
14168>>>>>>>>>>>
14168>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ResetChangedStates
14170>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bVisited
14170>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoOtherDDO
14170>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax iCount
14170>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDChangedInfo DDChangedInfo
14170>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDChangedInfo DDChangedInfo
14170>>>>>>>>>>>
14170>>>>>>>>>>>        // we want depth first traversal.
14170>>>>>>>>>>>        //mark first so we don't visit this coming back up.
14170>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
14171>>>>>>>>>>>
14171>>>>>>>>>>>        // traverse downward first
14171>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
14172>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
14178>>>>>>>>>>>>
14178>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to hoOtherDDO
14179>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoOtherDDO to bVisited
14180>>>>>>>>>>>            If not bVisited Begin
14182>>>>>>>>>>>                Send ResetChangedStates of hoOtherDDO
14183>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14183>>>>>>>>>>>>
14183>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
14184>>>>>>>>>>>>
14184>>>>>>>>>>>
14184>>>>>>>>>>>        // Set changed states for this DDO
14184>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pDDChangedInfo to DDChangedInfo
14185>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Changed_State to False // clears changed_state and parent_changed_states
14186>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Changed_State to DDChangedInfo.bChanged
14187>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (SizeOfArray(DDChangedInfo.ParentChanged)-1)
14193>>>>>>>>>>>>
14193>>>>>>>>>>>            Send SetParentDDOSwitched DDChangedInfo.ParentChanged[iCount].iTable DDChangedInfo.ParentChanged[iCount].bSwitched
14194>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
14195>>>>>>>>>>>>
14195>>>>>>>>>>>
14195>>>>>>>>>>>        // finally traverse to parents
14195>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
14196>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
14202>>>>>>>>>>>>
14202>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hoOtherDDO
14203>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoOtherDDO to bVisited
14204>>>>>>>>>>>            If not bVisited Begin
14206>>>>>>>>>>>                Send ResetChangedStates of hoOtherDDO
14207>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14207>>>>>>>>>>>>
14207>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
14208>>>>>>>>>>>>
14208>>>>>>>>>>>
14208>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14209>>>>>>>>>>>
14209>>>>>>>>>>>    // private use by new webapp framework (pre 18.2)
14209>>>>>>>>>>>    Function ReSyncRecord Returns Boolean
14211>>>>>>>>>>>        RowID riRowId
14211>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOk bOldReSync
14211>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hPrnt
14211>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMax iCount iMain
14211>>>>>>>>>>>
14211>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbInReSync to bOldReSync
14212>>>>>>>>>>>
14212>>>>>>>>>>>        Get prFindRowId to riRowId
14213>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain
14214>>>>>>>>>>>        If not (IsSameRowId(riRowID, CurrentRowId(Self) ) ) Begin
14216>>>>>>>>>>>            If (IsNullRowId(riRowID)) Begin
14218>>>>>>>>>>>                Set pbInReSync to True
14219>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Clear
14220>>>>>>>>>>>                Set pbInReSync to bOldReSync
14221>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14221>>>>>>>>>>>>
14221>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
14222>>>>>>>>>>>                Set pbInReSync to True
14223>>>>>>>>>>>                Get FindByRowIdExNoAutoFill iMain riRowId to bOk
14224>>>>>>>>>>>                Set pbInReSync to bOldReSync
14225>>>>>>>>>>>                If not bOk Begin
14227>>>>>>>>>>>                    Function_Return False
14228>>>>>>>>>>>                End
14228>>>>>>>>>>>>
14228>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14228>>>>>>>>>>>>
14228>>>>>>>>>>>
14228>>>>>>>>>>>            // check that the relate found all the parent records we expect.
14228>>>>>>>>>>>            // This should be correct unless a parent has been switched. Constrained
14228>>>>>>>>>>>            // parents, by definition, should already be correct. See **Note** below
14228>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
14229>>>>>>>>>>>            For iCount from 0 to (iMax-1)
14235>>>>>>>>>>>>
14235>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hPrnt
14236>>>>>>>>>>>                If (Constrain_File(Self)<>Main_File(hPrnt) and ;                    not (IsSameRowID(prFindRowId(hPrnt),CurrentRowId(hPrnt)))) Begin
14238>>>>>>>>>>>                    // the parent is either wrong or not processed yet. Either way
14238>>>>>>>>>>>                    // make it right.
14238>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get ReSyncRecord of hPrnt to bOk
14239>>>>>>>>>>>                    If not bOk Begin
14241>>>>>>>>>>>                        Function_Return False
14242>>>>>>>>>>>                    End
14242>>>>>>>>>>>>
14242>>>>>>>>>>>                End
14242>>>>>>>>>>>>
14242>>>>>>>>>>>            Loop
14243>>>>>>>>>>>>
14243>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14243>>>>>>>>>>>>
14243>>>>>>>>>>>
14243>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
14244>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
14245>>>>>>>>>>>
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // **Note** - dealing with changed parents and diamonds during a resync.
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // If there is not a relates-to contraint between DD and child it is possible
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // that the child find's relate will change the just found parent DD.
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // Assuming this is not a structure bug, it means the parent is changed parent and that
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // change must occur after the child record has been found and related. Therefore we add
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // check after each child find to see if an parent is incorrect. If it is, either it is a
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // switched parent or we haven't processed it yet. If the record is fine it
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // just does nothing. For example (where *=relates-to):
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    //     W
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    //   */  \*
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    //   X    Y
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    //    \  /*
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    //     Z
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // Assume you found a Z and changed its parent X.
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // The refind order can be: WXZY or WYZX
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // If WXZY the refound parent will be lost because Z will relate after the X
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // find and replace it with the original parent. To control this we add this check
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // after child Z has done its work. We only need to do this when child DDOs exist
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // that are not constrained. This can change the order that DDOs are resynced but it
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // should not matter.
14245>>>>>>>>>>>
14245>>>>>>>>>>>
14245>>>>>>>>>>>
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    // Private use by new webapp framework
14245>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ReSyncClearAll
14247>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOldReSync
14247>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbInReSync to bOldReSync
14248>>>>>>>>>>>        // we need this to stop RememberLast and retains. We don't want those during a resyc clear
14248>>>>>>>>>>>        Set pbInReSync to True
14249>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Clear_All
14250>>>>>>>>>>>        Set pbInReSync to bOldReSync
14251>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14252>>>>>>>>>>>
14252>>>>>>>>>>>    // returns table name for error display. By default it returns the logical name
14252>>>>>>>>>>>    // can be augmented to return other information
14252>>>>>>>>>>>    Function ErrorMessageTableName Integer iTable Returns String
14254>>>>>>>>>>>        String sTable
14254>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_LOGICAL_NAME of iTable to sTable
14257>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sTable
14258>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
14259>>>>>>>>>>>
14259>>>>>>>>>>>
14259>>>>>>>>>>>    // Augmented to test updating connections.
14259>>>>>>>>>>>    // If error report it.
14259>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Save
14261>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRval
14261>>>>>>>>>>>        String sTable
14261>>>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_WAITING) Begin
14263>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Update_Focus_Field_For_Operation MODE_SAVING // added in 12.1/15.1
14264>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Validate_Save_Structure False to iRval
14265>>>>>>>>>>>            If iRval Begin
14267>>>>>>>>>>>                Get ErrorMessageTableName iRval to sTable
14268>>>>>>>>>>>                Move (String(iRval) * "(" - sTable -")") to sTable
14269>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Data_Set_Error -1 DFERR_PROGRAM DD_INVALID_SAVE_STRUCTURE sTable
14270>>>>>>>>>>>                Procedure_Return
14271>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14271>>>>>>>>>>>>
14271>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14271>>>>>>>>>>>>
14271>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Request_Save
14273>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14274>>>>>>>>>>>
14274>>>>>>>>>>>    // Augmented to test updating connections.
14274>>>>>>>>>>>    // If error report it.
14274>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Request_Delete
14276>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iRval
14276>>>>>>>>>>>        String sTable
14276>>>>>>>>>>>        If (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_WAITING) Begin
14278>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Update_Focus_Field_For_Operation MODE_DELETING // added to 12.1/15.1
14279>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Validate_Delete_Structure False to iRval
14280>>>>>>>>>>>            If iRval Begin
14282>>>>>>>>>>>                Get ErrorMessageTableName iRval to sTable
14283>>>>>>>>>>>                Move (String(iRval) * "(" - sTable -")") to sTable
14284>>>>>>>>>>>                Send data_Set_Error -1 DFERR_PROGRAM DD_INVALID_DELETE_STRUCTURE sTable
14285>>>>>>>>>>>                Procedure_Return
14286>>>>>>>>>>>            End
14286>>>>>>>>>>>>
14286>>>>>>>>>>>        End
14286>>>>>>>>>>>>
14286>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Request_Delete
14288>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
14289>>>>>>>>>>>
14289>>>>>>>>>>>    // Set status-line help for the passed field. This could have been named
14289>>>>>>>>>>>    // Set Field_Status_Help but this keeps this message interface consistent
14289>>>>>>>>>>>    // with the rest of DF for windows.
