15396>>>>>>>>>>>        Get HasRecord to bHasRecord
15397>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bHasRecord
15398>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15399>>>>>>>>>>>
15399>>>>>>>>>>>    // is the field committed. It assumes the record is already committed
15399>>>>>>>>>>>    Function IsFieldCommitted Integer iField Returns Boolean
15401>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bIsCommitted
15401>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Field_Option iField DD_COMMIT to bIsCommitted
15402>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bIsCommitted
15403>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15404>>>>>>>>>>>
15404>>>>>>>>>>>    // is a parent change allowed for this parent server.
15404>>>>>>>>>>>    Function IsCommittedParentChangeAllowed Integer iServer Returns Boolean
15406>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bNoSwitch
15406>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ParentNoSwitchIfCommitted iServer to bNoSwitch
15407>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (not(bNoSwitch))
15408>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15409>>>>>>>>>>>
15409>>>>>>>>>>>    // Are we allowed to find with this file when it is used as a parent?
15409>>>>>>>>>>>    // Check all child DDOs and see if any are committed and do not allow switching parents when committed.
15409>>>>>>>>>>>    //  The rules for each child are switching is ok If:
15409>>>>>>>>>>>    // 1. the child is not committed,
15409>>>>>>>>>>>    // 2. it has a relates-to constraint (Find will change child which is ok)
15409>>>>>>>>>>>    // 3. if IsCommittedParentChangeAllowed allowed.
15409>>>>>>>>>>>    //
15409>>>>>>>>>>>    Function AllowParentFind Returns Boolean
15411>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iClients iClient iMain
15411>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoChild
15411>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bIsCommitted
15411>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iClients
15412>>>>>>>>>>>        For iClient from 0 to (iClients-1)
15418>>>>>>>>>>>>
15418>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iClient to hoChild
15419>>>>>>>>>>>            Get IsCommitted of hoChild to bIsCommitted
15420>>>>>>>>>>>            If bIsCommitted Begin
15422>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Main_File to iMain
15423>>>>>>>>>>>                Get IsRelatesToConstrained of hoChild iMain to bIsCommitted
15424>>>>>>>>>>>                If not bIsCommitted Begin
15426>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get IsCommittedParentChangeAllowed of hoChild iMain to bIsCommitted
15427>>>>>>>>>>>                    If (not(bIsCommitted)) Begin
15429>>>>>>>>>>>                        Function_Return False
15430>>>>>>>>>>>                    End
15430>>>>>>>>>>>>
15430>>>>>>>>>>>                End
15430>>>>>>>>>>>>
15430>>>>>>>>>>>            End
15430>>>>>>>>>>>>
15430>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
15431>>>>>>>>>>>>
15431>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return True
15432>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15433>>>>>>>>>>>
15433>>>>>>>>>>>    // aumgented to do nothing if there is no index (instead of annoying error message) and
15433>>>>>>>>>>>    // to do nothing if a find is not allowed because it is a no switch parent of a committed child.
15433>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Item_Find Integer eFindMode ;            Integer iFile Integer iField ;            Integer bDoEntryUpdate Integer bShowFindErr Integer bDeferred
15435>>>>>>>>>>>
15435>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex iMain
15435>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle  hoOwner
15435>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bOk
15435>>>>>>>>>>>
15435>>>>>>>>>>>        Get File_Field_Index iFile iField to iIndex
15436>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iIndex=-1)  Begin
15438>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
15439>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15439>>>>>>>>>>>>
15439>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain
15440>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iMain<>iFile) Begin
15442>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Which_Data_Set iFile to hoOwner
15443>>>>>>>>>>>            If hoOwner Begin
15445>>>>>>>>>>>                Get AllowParentFind of hoOwner to bOk
15446>>>>>>>>>>>                If not bOk Begin
15448>>>>>>>>>>>                    Procedure_Return
15449>>>>>>>>>>>                End
15449>>>>>>>>>>>>
15449>>>>>>>>>>>            End
15449>>>>>>>>>>>>
15449>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15449>>>>>>>>>>>>
15449>>>>>>>>>>>
15449>>>>>>>>>>>        If not bDeferred Begin
15451>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Refind_Records // make sure the buffers are correct before the find
15452>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15452>>>>>>>>>>>>
15452>>>>>>>>>>>
15452>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Item_Find eFindMode iFile iField bDoEntryUpdate bShowFindErr bDeferred
15454>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15455>>>>>>>>>>>
15455>>>>>>>>>>>
15455>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_CommitNoEnterOnIndex Integer iField Returns Boolean
15457>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return False
15458>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15459>>>>>>>>>>>
15459>>>>>>>>>>>    // Return the committed options for this field based on the committed status or this record,
15459>>>>>>>>>>>    // the committed status of the field and whether, if committed, it should be noput or noput+noenter
15459>>>>>>>>>>>    Function File_Field_Committed_Options Integer iFile Integer iField Returns Integer
15461>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bIsCommitted bNoEnter
15461>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iNewOpts iIndex
15461>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoOwner
15461>>>>>>>>>>>
15461>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Which_Data_Set iFile to hoOwner
15462>>>>>>>>>>>        If not hoOwner ;            Function_Return 0
15465>>>>>>>>>>>
15465>>>>>>>>>>>        Get File_Field_Index iFile iField to iIndex
15466>>>>>>>>>>>        Get IsCommitted of hoOwner to bIsCommitted
15467>>>>>>>>>>>        If bIsCommitted Begin
15469>>>>>>>>>>>            Get IsFieldCommitted of hoOwner iField to bIsCommitted
15470>>>>>>>>>>>            If bIsCommitted Begin
15472>>>>>>>>>>>                Move True to bNoEnter
15473>>>>>>>>>>>                If (iIndex<>-1) Begin
15475>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get Field_CommitNoEnterOnIndex iField to bNoEnter
15476>>>>>>>>>>>                End
15476>>>>>>>>>>>>
15476>>>>>>>>>>>                // if committed, it is noput and, if non-indexed, also noenter
15476>>>>>>>>>>>                Move (If(bNoEnter,DD_DISPLAYONLY,DD_NOPUT)) to iNewOpts
15477>>>>>>>>>>>            End
15477>>>>>>>>>>>>
15477>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15477>>>>>>>>>>>>
15477>>>>>>>>>>>        // if a finding parent field, we want to know if you are allowed to switch parents as we will assume
15477>>>>>>>>>>>        // that this field is used for finding.
15477>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoOwner<>Self and iIndex>-1) Begin
15479>>>>>>>>>>>            Get AllowParentFind of hoOwner to bIsCommitted
15480>>>>>>>>>>>            If not bIsCommitted Begin
15482>>>>>>>>>>>                Move DD_DISPLAYONLY to iNewOpts
15483>>>>>>>>>>>            End
15483>>>>>>>>>>>>
15483>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15483>>>>>>>>>>>>
15483>>>>>>>>>>>
15483>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iNewOpts
15484>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15485>>>>>>>>>>>
15485>>>>>>>>>>>    // Returns the current field-field options based on regular options, foreign field status
15485>>>>>>>>>>>    // plus committed record status
15485>>>>>>>>>>>    Function File_Field_DynamicEntryOptions Integer iFile Integer iField Returns Integer
15487>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCOpts iFOpts
15487>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iFile=0) Begin
15489>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return 0
15490>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15490>>>>>>>>>>>>
15490>>>>>>>>>>>        Get File_Field_Options iFile iField to iFOpts            // regular options (handles regular and foreign)
15491>>>>>>>>>>>        Get File_Field_Committed_Options iFile iField to iCOpts  // possible NoPut, NoEnter additions
15492>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (iFOpts ior iCOpts)
15493>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15494>>>>>>>>>>>
15494>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DDRememberedFieldIndex Integer iField Returns Integer
15496>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
15496>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
15497>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered SearchItem
15497>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered SearchItem
15497>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
15497>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pDDDefaults to DefaultValues
15498>>>>>>>>>>>        Move iField to SearchItem.iField
15499>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (SearchArray(SearchItem,DefaultValues)) to iIndex
15500>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iIndex
15501>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15502>>>>>>>>>>>
15502>>>>>>>>>>>    // Interface used to set or clear a dynamic default (remembered) value for a DD field. If the
15502>>>>>>>>>>>    // value passed is empty ("" or as empty as defined by the data-type) it is cleared. If the value
15502>>>>>>>>>>>    // is DD_RememberLast, it will use the last value before a clear as the default, else it uses the
15502>>>>>>>>>>>    // passed value as the default
15502>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Field_RememberedValue Integer iField String sValue
15504>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
15504>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
15505>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
15505>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bNull
15505>>>>>>>>>>>        Get DDRememberedFieldIndex iField to iIndex
15506>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pDDDefaults to DefaultValues
15507>>>>>>>>>>>        If (sValue<>DD_RememberLast) Begin // if it is rememberlast, we know it is not null
15509>>>>>>>>>>>            Get IsEmptyField iField sValue to bNull
15510>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15510>>>>>>>>>>>>
15510>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bNull)) Begin
15512>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iIndex=-1) Begin
15514>>>>>>>>>>>                Move (SizeOfArray(DefaultValues)) to iIndex
15515>>>>>>>>>>>                Move iField to DefaultValues[iIndex].iField
15516>>>>>>>>>>>            End
15516>>>>>>>>>>>>
15516>>>>>>>>>>>            Move sValue to DefaultValues[iIndex].sDefault
15517>>>>>>>>>>>            Set pDDDefaults to DefaultValues
15518>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15518>>>>>>>>>>>>
15518>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If  (iIndex<>-1) Begin
15521>>>>>>>>>>>            Set pDDDefaults to (RemoveFromArray(DefaultValues,iIndex))
15522>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15522>>>>>>>>>>>>
15522>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15523>>>>>>>>>>>
15523>>>>>>>>>>>    // get the remembered value as per rules above
15523>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Field_RememberedValue Integer iField Returns String
15525>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
15525>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
15526>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
15526>>>>>>>>>>>        Get DDRememberedFieldIndex iField to iIndex
15527>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iIndex<>-1) Begin
15529>>>>>>>>>>>            Get pDDDefaults to DefaultValues
15530>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return DefaultValues[iIndex].sDefault
15531>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15531>>>>>>>>>>>>
15531>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return ''
15532>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15533>>>>>>>>>>>
15533>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure AssignDynamicDefaults
15535>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iField iFields iFile
15535>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
15535>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
15536>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bMain
15536>>>>>>>>>>>        String sValue
15536>>>>>>>>>>>
15536>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iFile
15537>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pDDDefaults to DefaultValues
15538>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (SizeOfArray(DefaultValues)) to iFields
15539>>>>>>>>>>>        For iField from 0 to (iFields-1)
15545>>>>>>>>>>>>
15545>>>>>>>>>>>            If ( DefaultValues[iField].sDefault<>"") Begin
15547>>>>>>>>>>>                If (DefaultValues[iField].sDefault=DD_RememberLast) Begin
15549>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move DefaultValues[iField].sLastValue to sValue
15550>>>>>>>>>>>                End
15550>>>>>>>>>>>>
15550>>>>>>>>>>>                Else Begin
15551>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move DefaultValues[iField].sDefault to sValue
15552>>>>>>>>>>>                End
15552>>>>>>>>>>>>
15552>>>>>>>>>>>                Set Field_Changed_Value DefaultValues[iField].iField to sValue
15553>>>>>>>>>>>            End
15553>>>>>>>>>>>>
15553>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
15554>>>>>>>>>>>>
15554>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15555>>>>>>>>>>>
15555>>>>>>>>>>>    // Clears all remembered defaults for this DD.
15555>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ClearRememberedDefaults
15557>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
15557>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDRemembered[] DefaultValues
15558>>>>>>>>>>>        Set pDDDefaults to DefaultValues
15559>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15560>>>>>>>>>>>
15560>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure PrivateClearAllRememberedDefaults
15562>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iCount iMax
15562>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoDD
15562>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bVisisted
15562>>>>>>>>>>>
15562>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Visited_State to True
15563>>>>>>>>>>>
15563>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iMax
15564>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
15565>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
15571>>>>>>>>>>>>
15571>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server iCount to hoDD
15572>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoDD to bVisisted
15573>>>>>>>>>>>            If not (bVisisted) Begin
15575>>>>>>>>>>>                Send PrivateClearAllRememberedDefaults of hoDD
15576>>>>>>>>>>>            End
15576>>>>>>>>>>>>
15576>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
15577>>>>>>>>>>>>
15577>>>>>>>>>>>
15577>>>>>>>>>>>        Send ClearRememberedDefaults
15578>>>>>>>>>>>
15578>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Client_Count to iMax
15579>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement iMax
15580>>>>>>>>>>>        For iCount from 0 to iMax
15586>>>>>>>>>>>>
15586>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Client iCount to hoDD
15587>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Visited_State of hoDD to bVisisted
15588>>>>>>>>>>>            If not (bVisisted) Begin
15590>>>>>>>>>>>                Send PrivateClearAllRememberedDefaults of hoDD
15591>>>>>>>>>>>            End
15591>>>>>>>>>>>>
15591>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
15592>>>>>>>>>>>>
15592>>>>>>>>>>>
15592>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15593>>>>>>>>>>>
15593>>>>>>>>>>>    // Clears all remembered defaults for all DDs in this structure.
15593>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ClearAllRememberedDefaults
15595>>>>>>>>>>>        Send InitializeAllVisited
15596>>>>>>>>>>>        Send PrivateClearAllRememberedDefaults
15597>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15598>>>>>>>>>>>
15598>>>>>>>>>>>    // This is called after a clear or clear all is sent to this DD. It does autofinds as needed
15598>>>>>>>>>>>    // for any parent DDs. It does this if the parent is not a relates to contraining parent, if
15598>>>>>>>>>>>    // a field has an index, it has a changed value and it is autofind or autofind_ge.
15598>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DefaultParentAutofinds
15600>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer i iServers iField iFields iFile iIndex iOpts
15600>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDoAutoFind bRelates bIsEmptyField
15600>>>>>>>>>>>        String sValue
15600>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
15600>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count to iServers
15601>>>>>>>>>>>        For i from 0 to (iServers-1)
15607>>>>>>>>>>>>
15607>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server i to hoServer
15608>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Main_File of hoServer to iFile
15609>>>>>>>>>>>            Get IsRelatesToConstrained iFile to bRelates
15610>>>>>>>>>>>            // never autofind on a relates-to constraining parent
15610>>>>>>>>>>>            If not (bRelates) Begin
15612>>>>>>>>>>>
15612>>>>>>>>>>>                Get Field_Count of hoServer to iFields
15613>>>>>>>>>>>                Move False to bDoAutoFind
15614>>>>>>>>>>>                Move 1 to iField
15615>>>>>>>>>>>                While (not(bDoAutoFind) and (iField<=iFields))
15619>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get_Attribute DF_FIELD_INDEX of iFile iField to iIndex
15622>>>>>>>>>>>                    If (iIndex>0) Begin
15624>>>>>>>>>>>                        Get Field_Changed_State of hoServer iField to bDoAutoFind
15625>>>>>>>>>>>                        If bDoAutoFind Begin
15627>>>>>>>>>>>                            Get Field_Current_Value of hoServer iField to sValue
15628>>>>>>>>>>>                            Get IsEmptyField of hoServer iField sValue to bIsEmptyField
15629>>>>>>>>>>>                            Move (not(bIsEmptyField)) to bDoAutoFind
15630>>>>>>>>>>>                            If bDoAutoFind Begin
15632>>>>>>>>>>>                                Get File_Field_Options iFile iField to iOpts
15633>>>>>>>>>>>                                // if this is a retain or retainall we don't do this because we want
15633>>>>>>>>>>>                                // to maintain backwards compatibility
15633>>>>>>>>>>>                                Move ( (iOpts iand DD_AUTOFIND or iOpts iand DD_AUTOFIND_GE) and ;                                    not( iOpts iand DD_RETAIN or iOpts iand DD_RETAINALL) ) to bDoAutoFind
15634>>>>>>>>>>>                                If bDoAutoFind Begin
15636>>>>>>>>>>>                                    Send File_Field_Default_AutoFind iFile iField
15637>>>>>>>>>>>                                    Set Changed_State to False // clears parent changed state
15638>>>>>>>>>>>                                End
15638>>>>>>>>>>>>
15638>>>>>>>>>>>                            End
15638>>>>>>>>>>>>
15638>>>>>>>>>>>                        End
15638>>>>>>>>>>>>
15638>>>>>>>>>>>                    End
15638>>>>>>>>>>>>
15638>>>>>>>>>>>                    Increment iField
15639>>>>>>>>>>>                Loop
15640>>>>>>>>>>>>
15640>>>>>>>>>>>
15640>>>>>>>>>>>                // Only check for grandparent autofinds if this parent did not do a an autofind
15640>>>>>>>>>>>                // Doing an autofind on an autofind parent's parent is just too confusing
15640>>>>>>>>>>>                If not bDoAutoFind Begin
15642>>>>>>>>>>>                    Send DefaultParentAutofinds of hoServer
15643>>>>>>>>>>>                End
15643>>>>>>>>>>>>
15643>>>>>>>>>>>            End
15643>>>>>>>>>>>>
15643>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
15644>>>>>>>>>>>>
15644>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15645>>>>>>>>>>>
15645>>>>>>>>>>>    // Set this DD to be an alias, passing the file number of the alias
15645>>>>>>>>>>>    // This can only be called once per instance and the Main_File must already have been set
15645>>>>>>>>>>>    // most likely in a superclass.
15645>>>>>>>>>>>    // This sets Main_File to the alias, stores the original master file (accessed via MasterForAlias).
15645>>>>>>>>>>>    // It also clears all existing relatonships. Normally we expect the alias class to set
15645>>>>>>>>>>>    // sets pbUseDDRelates and pbNoCascadeDeleteStrict to true. We don't do that automatically so that
15645>>>>>>>>>>>    // the Studio's property panel will show the correct values. When an alias is defined using the
15645>>>>>>>>>>>    // studio it will set these two properties.
15645>>>>>>>>>>>    // This means you must set any required relationships yourself
15645>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Alias_File Integer iTable
15647>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMain iMaster iFieldsM iFieldsA
15647>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File to iMain
15648>>>>>>>>>>>        Get MasterForAlias to iMaster
15649>>>>>>>>>>>
15649>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iTable=0 and iMaster) Begin
15651>>>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM "Cannot unset alias table"
15652>>>>>>>>>>>>
15652>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
15653>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15653>>>>>>>>>>>>
15653>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iTable=iMain) Begin
15655>>>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM "Cannot set alias table to self"
15656>>>>>>>>>>>>
15656>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
15657>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15657>>>>>>>>>>>>
15657>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iMaster) Begin
15659>>>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM "Cannot redefine alias table"
15660>>>>>>>>>>>>
15660>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
15661>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15661>>>>>>>>>>>>
15661>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_NUMBER_FIELDS of iMain to iFieldsM
15664>>>>>>>>>>>        Get_Attribute DF_FILE_NUMBER_FIELDS of iTable to iFieldsA
15667>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iFieldsA<>iFieldsM) Begin
15669>>>>>>>>>>>            Error DFERR_PROGRAM "Alias and Master file are not based on the same table"
15670>>>>>>>>>>>>
15670>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
15671>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15671>>>>>>>>>>>>
15671>>>>>>>>>>>
15671>>>>>>>>>>>        Set piMasterTable to iMain
15672>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Main_File to iTable
15673>>>>>>>>>>>        Send DefineAsAlias
15674>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15675>>>>>>>>>>>
15675>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure DefineAsAlias
15677>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer i iFile
15677>>>>>>>>>>>
15677>>>>>>>>>>>        // We expect he developer to set these properties to True
15677>>>>>>>>>>>        //Set pbUseDDRelates to True
15677>>>>>>>>>>>        //Set pbNoCascadeDeleteStrict to True
15677>>>>>>>>>>>
15677>>>>>>>>>>>        Send ClearDDRelates
15678>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Client_File_Count to i
15679>>>>>>>>>>>        While i
15683>>>>>>>>>>>            Decrement i
15684>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Client_File i to iFile
15685>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_Client_File iFile
15686>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
15687>>>>>>>>>>>>
15687>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server_File_Count to i
15688>>>>>>>>>>>        While i
15692>>>>>>>>>>>            Decrement i
15693>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Server_File i to iFile
15694>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_Server_File iFile
15695>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
15696>>>>>>>>>>>>
15696>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15697>>>>>>>>>>>
15697>>>>>>>>>>>    Function MasterForAlias Returns Integer
15699>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMaster
15699>>>>>>>>>>>        Get piMasterTable to iMaster
15700>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return iMaster
15701>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15702>>>>>>>>>>>
15702>>>>>>>>>>>    Function IsAlias Returns Boolean
15704>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iMaster
15704>>>>>>>>>>>        Get piMasterTable to iMaster
15705>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return (iMaster<>0)
15706>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15707>>>>>>>>>>>
15707>>>>>>>>>>>
15707>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure OnSaveRecord
15709>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15710>>>>>>>>>>>
15710>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure StoreDefaultSQLFilters
15712>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoSQLHelper
15712>>>>>>>>>>>        Get phoSQLHelper to hoSQLHelper
15713>>>>>>>>>>>        Send StoreDefaultSQLFilters of hoSQLHelper
15714>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15715>>>>>>>>>>>
15715>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure RestoreDefaultSQLFilters
15717>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoSQLHelper
15717>>>>>>>>>>>        Get phoSQLHelper to hoSQLHelper
15718>>>>>>>>>>>        Send RestoreDefaultSQLFilters of hoSQLHelper
15719>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15720>>>>>>>>>>>
15720>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ApplySQLFilterStr String sFilter
15722>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoSQLHelper
15722>>>>>>>>>>>        Get phoSQLHelper to hoSQLHelper
15723>>>>>>>>>>>        Send ApplySQLFilterStr of hoSQLHelper sFilter
15724>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15725>>>>>>>>>>>
15725>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure ApplySQLFilter
15727>>>>>>>>>>>        String sNewFilter sOldFilter
15727>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bApplyGlobalSQLFilters bOldFilterActive
15727>>>>>>>>>>>        Get psSQLFilter to sNewFilter
15728>>>>>>>>>>>        // if we have am active  table filter we can either ignore it or and it to the where clause
15728>>>>>>>>>>>        // pbApplyGlobalSQLFilters determines what to do.
15728>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbApplyGlobalSQLFilters to bApplyGlobalSQLFilters
15729>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbOldFilterActive to bOldFilterActive
15730>>>>>>>>>>>        If (bApplyGlobalSQLFilters and bOldFilterActive) Begin
15732>>>>>>>>>>>            Get psOldFilter to sOldFilter
15733>>>>>>>>>>>            Get SQLStrAppend sOldFilter sNewFilter to sNewFilter
15734>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15734>>>>>>>>>>>>
15734>>>>>>>>>>>        Send ApplySQLFilterStr sNewFilter
15735>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15736>>>>>>>>>>>
15736>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Data_Set_PreFind
15738>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bUseDDSQLFilters
15738>>>>>>>>>>>        String sOldDDFilter
15738>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbUseDDSQLFilters to bUseDDSQLFilters
15739>>>>>>>>>>>        If bUseDDSQLFilters Begin
15741>>>>>>>>>>>
15741>>>>>>>>>>>            Send StoreDefaultSQLFilters
15742>>>>>>>>>>>
15742>>>>>>>>>>>            // this can get called during cascade deletes. In such a case we will
15742>>>>>>>>>>>            // never explicitly not apply an SQL filters because it could violate relational integrity
15742>>>>>>>>>>>            If (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_DELETING) Begin
15744>>>>>>>>>>>                Get psSQLFilter to sOldDDFilter
15745>>>>>>>>>>>                Set psSQLFilter to "" // make sure there is no filter applied
15746>>>>>>>>>>>            End
15746>>>>>>>>>>>>
15746>>>>>>>>>>>
15746>>>>>>>>>>>            Send ApplySQLFilter
15747>>>>>>>>>>>
15747>>>>>>>>>>>            If (OPERATION_MODE=MODE_DELETING) Begin
15749>>>>>>>>>>>                Set psSQLFilter to sOldDDFilter
15750>>>>>>>>>>>            End
15750>>>>>>>>>>>>
15750>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15750>>>>>>>>>>>>
15750>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15751>>>>>>>>>>>
15751>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Data_Set_PostFind
15753>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bUseDDSQLFilters
15753>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbUseDDSQLFilters to bUseDDSQLFilters
15754>>>>>>>>>>>        If bUseDDSQLFilters Begin
15756>>>>>>>>>>>            Send RestoreDefaultSQLFilters
15757>>>>>>>>>>>        End
15757>>>>>>>>>>>>
15757>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
15758>>>>>>>>>>>
15758>>>>>>>>>>>
15758>>>>>>>>>>>    // returns active constraints in atConstraintDef array.
15758>>>>>>>>>>>    // Should be called after constraints are built
15758>>>>>>>>>>>    // typically right after Rebuild_Constraints
15758>>>>>>>>>>>
15758>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DDOConstraints Returns tConstraintDef[]
15760>>>>>>>>>>>        tConstraintDef[] Constraints
15760>>>>>>>>>>>        tConstraintDef[] Constraints
15761>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer i iCount i1
15761>>>>>>>>>>>        Get DATA_SET_CONSTRAINT_COUNT to iCount
15762>>>>>>>>>>>        For i from 0 to (iCount-1)
15768>>>>>>>>>>>>
15768>>>>>>>>>>>            Get DATA_SET_CONSTRAINT_INFO i 0 to i1 // type / mode
15769>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Hi(i1)) to  Constraints[i].eType
15770>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Low(i1)) to  Constraints[i].eMode
15771>>>>>>>>>>>            Get DATA_SET_CONSTRAINT_INFO i 1 to i1 // file / field
15772>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Hi(i1)) to  Constraints[i].iFile
15773>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Low(i1)) to  Constraints[i].iField
15774>>>>>>>>>>>            Get DATA_SET_CONSTRAINT_INFO i 2 to i1 // other file /field
15775>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Hi(i1)) to  Constraints[i].iOtherFile
15776>>>>>>>>>>>            Move (Low(i1)) to  Constraints[i].iOtherField
15777>>>>>>>>>>>            Get DATA_SET_CONSTRAINT_INFO_Value i  to Constraints[i].sValue
15778>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
15779>>>>>>>>>>>>
15779>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return Constraints
15780>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15781>>>>>>>>>>>
15781>>>>>>>>>>>    // returns constraint finding information about the current find. This tells us what kinds
15781>>>>>>>>>>>    // of constraint find "expressions" are used. This will actually do a cosntrained find
15781>>>>>>>>>>>    // initialization much like Establish_Find_Direction, which means it can change the values in
15781>>>>>>>>>>>    // the file buffer to assist with a jump-in.
15781>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DDOConstraintFindMeta Integer eMode Integer iOrder Returns tDDOConstraintFindMeta
15783>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDOConstraintFindMeta FindMeta
15783>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDOConstraintFindMeta FindMeta
15783>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer i
15783>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Constraint_Exps eMode iOrder to i
15784>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (Hi(i)) to FindMeta.iJumpInSegments
15785>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (i iand CONST_EXP_JUMPOUT) to FindMeta.bJumpOut
15786>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (i iand CONST_EXP_PRE_RELATE) to FindMeta.bPreRelate
15787>>>>>>>>>>>        Move (i iand CONST_EXP_POST_RELATE) to FindMeta.bPostRelate
15788>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return FindMeta
15789>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15790>>>>>>>>>>>
15790>>>>>>>>>>>    // this tells you if the current find or read requires a relate to evaluate the DF constraint.
15790>>>>>>>>>>>    // If false you could use this to set no_relate_state to false for the find/read process and then
15790>>>>>>>>>>>    // restore it when complete. Be careful using this.
15790>>>>>>>>>>>    Function DDOConstraintNeedsRelate Integer iOrder Returns Boolean
15792>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDOConstraintFindMeta FindMeta
15792>>>>>>>>>>>        tDDOConstraintFindMeta FindMeta
15792>>>>>>>>>>>        Get DDOConstraintFindMeta (GE) iOrder to FindMeta
15793>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return FindMeta.bPostRelate
15794>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15795>>>>>>>>>>>
15795>>>>>>>>>>>    // returns true if this table supports SQL filter interface
15795>>>>>>>>>>>    Function SupportsSQLFilters Returns Boolean
15797>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bSupports
15797>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoSQLHelper
15797>>>>>>>>>>>        Get phoSQLHelper to hoSQLHelper
15798>>>>>>>>>>>        Get SupportsSQLFilters of hoSQLHelper to bSupports
15799>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return bSupports
15800>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15801>>>>>>>>>>>
15801>>>>>>>>>>>    // SQL Helper functions that return SQL Filters strings that can be used in a where clause
15801>>>>>>>>>>>
15801>>>>>>>>>>>    // Creates an SQL Like Filter for this field and search target
15801>>>>>>>>>>>    Function SQLStrLike Integer iField String sSearch Returns String
15803>>>>>>>>>>>        String sFilter
15803>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoSQLHelper
15803>>>>>>>>>>>        Get phoSQLHelper to hoSQLHelper
15804>>>>>>>>>>>        Get SQLStrLike of hoSQLHelper iField sSearch to sFilter
15805>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sFilter
15806>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
15807>>>>>>>>>>>
15807>>>>>>>>>>>    // Appends two Filters with an AND clause. Both or either can be empty
15807>>>>>>>>>>>    Function SQLStrAppend String sOrigFilter String sFilter Returns String
15809>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoSQLHelper
15809>>>>>>>>>>>        Get phoSQLHelper to hoSQLHelper
15810>>>>>>>>>>>        Get SQLStrAppend of hoSQLHelper sOrigFilter sFilter to sFilter
15811>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return sFilter
15812>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
