16568>>>>>>>    Procedure Initialize_Files
16570>>>>>>>        Integer iFile
16570>>>>>>>        String sname
16570>>>>>>>        Send Clear_File_Data
16571>>>>>>>        Move 0 to iFile
16572>>>>>>>        Repeat
16572>>>>>>>>
16572>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute Df_File_Next_Used of iFile to iFile
16575>>>>>>>            If (iFile = 0) ;                Break
16578>>>>>>>            Get_Attribute Df_File_Logical_Name of iFile to sName
16581>>>>>>>            Send Set_File_Data sName iFile
16582>>>>>>>        Loop
16583>>>>>>>>
16583>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
16584>>>>>>>    
16584>>>>>>>    // Search_Field_Name provides a way of getting the
16584>>>>>>>    // field Name without generating an error. We will use an error
16584>>>>>>>    // handle in this object to "swallow" the error.
16584>>>>>>>    Procedure Error_Report Integer iErrNum Integer iErrLine String sErrMsg
16586>>>>>>>        Move True to Err
16587>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
16588>>>>>>>    
16588>>>>>>>    Function Search_Field_Name Integer iFile String sFieldName Returns Integer
16590>>>>>>>        Handle hOldErr
16590>>>>>>>        Integer iField
16590>>>>>>>        If (iFile = 0) ;            Function_Return 0
16593>>>>>>>        Move Error_Object_id to hOldErr           // push error handler
16594>>>>>>>        Move Self to Error_Object_Id    // redirect here, it is silent!
16595>>>>>>>        Move False to Err
16596>>>>>>>        Field_Map iFile sFieldName to iField      // this could gen an error, we will trap it here
16598>>>>>>>        Move hOldErr to Error_object_id           // pop old error handler
16599>>>>>>>        Function_Return (If( (Err), -1, iField))
16600>>>>>>>    End_Function
16601>>>>>>>    
16601>>>>>>>End_Class
