19386>>>>>>>>>>>>>Class server_mixin is a mixin
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   Server is the object id of the database agent for this object.
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   Watched_Servers is a set of object ids for database agents whose state
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   must also be monitored by this object (but which never receive requests
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   directly from this object, unlike the Server).
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   Servers_Scanned determines if the items of this object have been
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   scanned to see if this object should be connected to other database
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   agents as 'just watching' (see Watched_Servers, above).
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   Auto_Fill_State determines if this object should always automatically
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   fill itself with data when it is activated.
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   Deferred_State determines if this object's browsing in database files
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   should be reflected immediately in this object's database agent (and
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   the agents' agents, etc.), or not.
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19387>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure define_server
19389>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer obj#
19389>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer private.Server           0
19390>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Watched_Servers          0
19391>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // used to send Set Changed_State to "foreign" servers, while Watched_Servers
19391>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // is used for sending messages from the DDO to DEOs (there are more of them)
19391>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer ChangedStateWatched_Servers     0
19392>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer private.Servers_Scanned  0
19393>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19393>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Auto_Fill_State False
19394>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Boolean pbAutoFillOnInit True      // Used to tell DDO's that we want autofill on initialization when DEO is attaching
19395>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19395>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Deferred_State  False
19396>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19396>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // added to support DEO request-delegation. This is set true
19396>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if the server is explicitly set in this DEO (normally via a
19396>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // USING parameter).
19396>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer explicit_server_state False
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Since this package's SET changed_state is using change_
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // disabled_state we might as well define it here. This gets changed
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // by Clear_mx to support setting of defaults without changing the
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // objects changed_state.
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // This stops changed_state from getting changed. It allows item_changed_
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // state to chagne without the object's changed_state getting changed.
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // This should be considered protected (i.e., likely to change). The new
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // messages Entry_Defaults and Set Default_Value are both public and use
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // this. Try to use these messages instead of this property.
19397>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Change_Disabled_State  False
19398>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19398>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // If true DEO will not disconnect from server when deactivating.
19398>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // If true View should handles attaching and detaching.
19398>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Register_Function Default_static_server_state Returns Integer
19398>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Static_Server_State  (Default_Static_Server_State(Self))
19399>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19399>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Properties to better support tables. If Refresh_dirty_state
19399>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // is true then the list object needs refreshing (because it was inactive
19399>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // and changes were made that were not updated). After add_focus is
19399>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // complete the add_focus_msg is sent (allows tables to initialize the
19399>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // list).
19399>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Refresh_dirty_state  True // when not active/dirty
19400>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Property Integer Add_focus_msg        0    // by dflt no message
19401>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19401>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // This will call a stub procedure which will be augmented (or replaced)
19401>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // by the xdeo mixins
19401>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Define_Extended_DEO_Mixin
19402>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19402>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19403>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19403>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19403>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure remove_deo_from_server
19405>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer obj# isclient wsrvr
19405>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to obj#
19406>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // as of 17.0, containers will be added as a DEO so it receives the Refresh message
19406>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (obj# <> 0) ;            Send remove_user_interface to obj# Self
19409>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to wsrvr
19410>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If wsrvr ;            Send remove_user_interface to wsrvr Self True // TRUE for watchers
19413>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Refresh_dirty_state to True
19414>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
