19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This function returns the object id of the database agent of this
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   object, or 0.
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   If this object's Server is 0, this object's parent's Server is
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   returned, if any.
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Notes
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This function is used to allow nested data-entry objects to use the
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   database agent defined by their parent object.
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19422>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Server Returns Integer
19424>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer obj#
19424>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private.Server to obj#
19425>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (obj# = 0 and Component_State(Self)) ;            Function_Return (Locate_Server(parent(Self)))
19428>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return obj#
19429>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
19430>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19430>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19430>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure sets the value of the Server property of this object,
19430>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   notifying child-objects of the change, and destroying and creating
19430>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   connections with database agents, as required.
19430>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19430>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   If the Server of this object is changed while this object is inactive,
19430>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   no notification of child-objects is required or performed.
19430>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Server Integer newVal
19432>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer oldVal
19432>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set explicit_server_state to (newVal <> 0)
19433>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to oldVal
19434>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (newVal <> 0) ;            Set private.Server to (object_id(newVal))
19437>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else ;            Set private.Server to newVal
19439>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (active_state(Self)) Begin
19441>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Broadcast Send server_changed oldVal newVal
19443>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (oldVal <> 0) ;                Send remove_deo_from_server  //detach from current server
19446>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newval <> 0) ;                Send attach_deo_to_server    //attach to new server
19449>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19449>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19449>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19450>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19450>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure servers as notification of a change in the connection
19450>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   of this object's parent to its database agent.  If this object uses
19450>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   its parent's database agent by default (see the Server and Find_Server
19450>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   functions, above), it must disconnect from the old agent and connect
19450>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   with the new agent.
19450>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure server_changed Integer oldVal Integer newVal
19452>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer oldSrvr
19452>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // as of 17.0, containers will be added as a DEO so it receives the Refresh message
19452>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private.Server to oldSrvr
19453>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (oldSrvr = 0) Begin  //assumes Server(self) = oldVal by deleg
19455>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (oldVal <> 0) ;                Send remove_user_interface to oldVal Self
19458>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newVal <> 0) ;                Send add_user_interface to newVal Self
19461>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19461>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19461>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19462>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19462>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19462>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure empties the Watched_Servers broadcaster, after
19462>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   detaching this object from all of the broadcaster's elements.
19462>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure is invoked by Find_Servers_to_Watch, in preparation
19462>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   for a scan. Deletes both sets of watched servers
19462>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19462>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure delete_watched_servers
19464>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer vis#
19464>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19464>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get watched_servers to vis#
19465>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If vis# Begin
19467>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to vis# Self True //detach from all, TRUE for watchers
19468>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to False
19469>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send delete_Data to vis#                    //empty it
19470>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to True
19471>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19471>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19471>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19471>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to vis#
19472>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If vis# Begin
19474>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to False
19475>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send delete_Data to vis#                    //empty it
19476>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to True
19477>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19477>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19477>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19478>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19478>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure adds the specified object id (obj#) to this object's
19478>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set of database agents who are merely 'watched', and establishes a
19478>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   connection between the database agent and this object.
19478>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure add_watched_server Integer obj#
19480>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer vis# ndx
19480>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get watched_servers to vis#
19481>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if w server does not exist, first create it
19481>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Vis# = 0) Begin
19483>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Create of Desktop U_Broadcaster to Vis#
19484>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Watched_Servers to Vis#
19485>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19485>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19485>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
19485>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set broadcast_state of vis# to False
19486>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get find_element of vis# obj# to ndx
19487>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (ndx < 0) ;            Send add_element to vis# obj#
19490>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set broadcast_state of vis# to True
19491>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (ndx lt 0 and active_State(Self)) ;            Send add_user_interface to obj# Self True // TRUE for watchers
19494>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19495>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19495>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure add_ChangedStateWatched_Servers Integer obj#
19497>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer vis# ndx
19497>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to vis#
19498>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Vis# = 0) Begin
19500>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Create of Desktop U_Broadcaster to Vis#
19501>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set ChangedStateWatched_Servers to Vis#
19502>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19502>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19502>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
19502>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set broadcast_state of vis# to False
19503>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get find_element of vis# obj# to ndx
19504>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (ndx < 0) ;            Send add_element to vis# obj#
19507>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set broadcast_state of vis# to True
19508>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19509>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19509>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19509>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure removes the specified object id (obj#) from this object's
19509>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set of database agents who are merely 'watched', and destroys the
19509>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   connection between the database agent and this object.
19509>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure remove_watched_server Integer obj#
19511>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer vis# ndx
19511>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get watched_servers to vis#
19512>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Only if w server exists
19512>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If vis# Begin
19514>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to False
19515>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get find_element of vis# obj# to ndx
19516>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (ndx >= 0) ;                Send remove_element to vis# obj#
19519>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of vis# to True
19520>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (ndx >= 0 and active_State(Self)) ;                Send remove_user_interface to obj# Self True // TRUE for watchers
19523>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19523>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19523>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19524>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19524>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure causes the scanning of this object's items' fields,
19524>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   and the production of a set of database agents who should be 'watched'.
19524>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure depends completely upon Find_Servers_To_Watch, below.
19524>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19524>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Scan_Servers
19526>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send find_servers_to_watch False
19527>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure scans the fields of this object's items to determine
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   what other database agents (data_sets) other than this object's Server
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   should be 'watched' (for data changes).
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure is invoked once per object, the first time the object
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   is activated.  If the data_file, data_field, and/or main_file of this
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   object are changed (don't change them while this object is active!),
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set Private.Servers_Scanned to FALSE to force this object to scan
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   again (when it is next activated).
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 17.0: The logic has been retooled to add more watched servers to the DDOs. This is done so
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // DD operations will send Refresh to these additional watched-servers. There are two changes:
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 1. Containers are now made watched servers for the Server and all parent servers
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 2. Non-file.field DEOs (e.g., expressions) are made watched servers for the server (which it
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    already did and for all parent servers. Without this, parent entry_item expressions were not
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    getting updated
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Here is how watched-servers works.
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Each DEO attaches and detaches from its Server by sending Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to the server DD. Once attached, the DD knows about this DEO and sends messages to it as needed (Refresh,
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Entry_Update, etc.). In addition, a DEO may need to attach a parent DDO so that changes in that parent DD
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // results in those messages being sent. This is needed if the binding table in entry_item refers to a parent
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // table. So we need to send Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface to that parent server as well. If a DEO
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // has multiple, there could be multiple parent servers. As of 17.0, we are also attaching to parent servers if
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // we are unsure about how the DEO is being used. If an expression is used, it might need to be updated when
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // a parent (or any ancestor) changes. Each DEO keeps track of servers that it attaches to and this is referred
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to as the watched_server list. This list is maintained so the DEO knows which DDOs to attach and detach to.
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19528>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure find_servers_to_watch Integer tableFlag
19530>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer i file# obj# maxitems count p srvr# self# srvrfile
19530>>>>>>>>>>>>>        String fileStr fStr
19530>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bContainer bDoAll
19530>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19530>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Client_Area_State to bContainer
19531>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set private.Servers_Scanned to True
19532>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19532>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to srvr#
19533>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19533>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (srvr#=0) Begin
19535>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
19536>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19536>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19536>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19536>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send delete_watched_servers  //empty Watched_Servers broadcaster first
19537>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19537>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get main_file of srvr# to srvrfile  // data-set's main-file
19538>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19538>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If bContainer Begin
19540>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // containers should get added to all parent DDOs
19540>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers srvr#
19541>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
19542>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19542>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19542>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19542>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (tableFlag <> 0) ;            Get Prototype_Object to self# // tables
19545>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else ;            Move Self to self# // forms and text windows
19547>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19547>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get item_count of self# to maxitems
19548>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Decrement maxitems
19549>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19549>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if no items do nothing
19549>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if one item do quick check
19549>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if multiple items do it the hard way
19549>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19549>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (maxitems<0) Begin
19551>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if no items, which is unusual, we don't know what this DEO is so we will treat it like a container
19551>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // and add it as a watched server for all DDOs
19551>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers srvr#
19552>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return  // no items
19553>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19553>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19553>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19553>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (maxitems=0) Begin // only 1 item - skip most of the nonsense
19555>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get data_file of self# 0 to file#
19556>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // we need watched server if file exists, it is not the main file
19556>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // and is not an updating file (as opposed to updating data-set).
19556>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (file#>0 and file#<>srvrfile) Begin
19558>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Get which_data_set of srvr# file# to obj#
19559>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (obj# <> 0 and obj# <> srvr#) Begin
19561>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Send add_Watched_server obj#
19562>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Send add_ChangedStateWatched_Servers obj#
19563>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19563>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19563>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19563>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19563>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Else If (file#=0) Begin
19566>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // if no file (e.g., expression) we don't know when it changes so we tell all servers
19566>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // that this is a watcher
19566>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send WatchAllParentServers srvr#
19567>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19567>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19567>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If File# ;                Send Copy_Item_Options Srvr# file# (Data_Field(Self#,0)) Self# 0
19570>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19570>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19570>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin  // multiple items - do what you must
19571>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Move -1 to count
19572>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Move "," to fileStr
19573>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If tableFlag Begin
19575>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Get main_file to file#
19576>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (file# <> srvrfile) Begin    // only do this if mainfile is not the srvr file
19578>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Append fileStr file# ","   //insert mainfile to be sure it's watched
19580>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Increment count
19581>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19581>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19581>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19581>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19581>>>>>>>>>>>>>            For i from 0 to maxitems
19587>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19587>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Get data_file of self# i to file#
19588>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (file#=0) Begin
19590>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    // as soon as we don't know what the item is used for we will have
19590>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    // to attach to all parent DDOs.
19590>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move True to bDoAll
19591>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19591>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19591>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (file# > 0 and file#<>srvrfile and ;                    not(fileStr contains (","+String(file#)+",")) ) Begin
19593>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move (fileStr+String(file#) + ",") to fileStr
19594>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Increment count
19595>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19595>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19595>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If File# ;                    Send Copy_Item_Options Srvr# file# (Data_Field(Self#,i)) Self# i
19598>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Loop
19599>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19599>>>>>>>>>>>>>            
19599>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if an item's binding table is unknown, we watch all parent DDOs.
19599>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If bDoAll Begin
19601>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send WatchAllParentServers srvr#
19602>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19602>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19602>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
19603>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (count >= 0) Begin // any watched items?
19605>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Move (Right(fileStr, length(fileStr) - 1))  to fileStr  //remove leading comma
19606>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    For i from 0 to count
19612>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19612>>>>>>>>>>>>>                        Move (Pos( "," ,fileStr)) to p
19613>>>>>>>>>>>>>                        If (p > 1) Begin
19615>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            Move (Left( fileStr , p-1)) to fStr
19616>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            Move (Right( fileStr, length(fileStr) - p)) to fileStr
19617>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            Move fStr to file#
19618>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            Get which_data_set of srvr# file# to obj#
19619>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            If (obj# <> 0 and obj# <> srvr#) Begin
19621>>>>>>>>>>>>>                                Send add_Watched_server obj#
19622>>>>>>>>>>>>>                                Send add_ChangedStateWatched_Servers obj#
19623>>>>>>>>>>>>>                            End
19623>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19623>>>>>>>>>>>>>                        End
19623>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19623>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Loop
19624>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19624>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19624>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19624>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19624>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19624>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19624>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19624>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19625>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19625>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This does nothing. Other sub-classes (or later mixins) should add
19625>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // logic to this.
19625>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Copy_Item_Options Integer iDSO Integer iFile Integer iField ;            Integer iDEO Integer iItem
19627>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19628>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19628>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This does little. Other sub-classes (or later mixins) should add
19628>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // logic to this.
19628>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Define_Extended_DEO_Mixin
19630>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19631>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19631>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19631>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // created for Nesting support
19631>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Mark_As_Component
19633>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer ser#
19633>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Component_State to True
19634>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Set Has_Components_State to True
19636>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private.Server to ser#
19637>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (ser# = 0) Begin
19639>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Delegate Get Locate_Server to ser#
19641>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (ser# <> 0) ;                Set private.Server to ser#
19644>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19644>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19644>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19645>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19645>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This only gets called when the developer is killing this object. During application
19645>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // shut-down, only destroy_object is called. This augmentation destroys the watched broadcaster
19645>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (which is sitting on the desktop). During program shut down we don't care if this is called
19645>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // because it is getting destroyed anyway. We are making the assumption that a developer controlled
19645>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // destroy will always be called with the watcher still existing.
19645>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19645>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Destroy
19647>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatched
19647>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Changed_State to False //   is this really needed anymore???
19648>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The watched server, must still exist.
19648>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatched
19649>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
19651>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
19652>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the bcaster
19653>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19653>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19653>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The bound watched server, must still exist.
19653>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatched
19654>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
19656>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
19657>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the bcaster
19658>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19658>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19658>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Destroy
19660>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19661>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19661>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19661>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Should_Save Returns Integer
19663>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer Obj# Chngd
19663>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to Obj#
19664>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Changed_state to Chngd
19665>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return ( Chngd or (obj# <> 0 and Should_Save(obj#)) )
19666>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
19667>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19667>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Added server scan logic here instead of add_focus.
19667>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Attach_Deo_To_Server
19669>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer obj# isclient srvscn wsrvr
19669>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to obj#
19670>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get client_area_state to isclient
19671>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (obj# <> 0) ;            Send add_user_interface to obj# Self
19674>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private.Servers_Scanned to srvscn
19675>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (srvscn = 0) ;            Send scan_servers
19678>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to wsrvr
19679>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If wsrvr Send add_user_interface ;            to wsrvr Self True // TRUE for watchers
19682>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (obj# <> 0 and isclient = 0) ;            Send update_dependent_items
19685>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19686>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19686>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Removed server scan logic and moved it to attach-deo_to_server
19686>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Add_Focus Handle hoParent Returns Integer
19688>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer srvscn retval msg
19688>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
19688>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // standard DEO behavior
19688>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
19688>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Get msg_Add_Focus hoParent to retval
19690>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If retval ;            Procedure_Return retval
19693>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19693>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (client_area_State(Self) = 0) ; //clients already broadcast            Broadcast NO_STOP Send add_focus Self
19698>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
19698>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // server augmentation
19698>>>>>>>>>>>>>        //
19698>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (focus_mode(Self) <> NO_ACTIVATE and Active_State(Self)) ;            Send attach_DEO_to_server
19701>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
19701>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // last thing to do is send custom message. With list deos
19701>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // msg is probably initialize_list. With non-list deos it
19701>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // is probably nothing
19701>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get add_focus_msg to msg
19702>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If msg ;            Send msg
19705>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19706>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19706>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Connect DEO to Server if Demanded (DoAllfg=t) or ;
19706>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // allowed  (static_server_State=t). Broadcast if children exist
19706>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Connect_DEOs_to_Servers Integer DoAllFg
19708>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (DoAllfg or Static_Server_State(Self)) ;            Send Attach_Deo_to_Server
19711>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Has_Components_State(Self)) ;            Broadcast Send Connect_DEOs_to_Servers DoAllfg
19715>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Disconnect DEOs from Servers according to rules. Broadcast
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to child components.
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Pass: DoAllMode
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    DETACH_NEVER        Never
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    DETACH_IF_NO_CHANGE Do if changed_state=F
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    DETACH_ALWAYS       Do it no matter what
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    DETACH_IF_ALLOWED   Do if changed_state=F and auto_attach
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //                        (I don't think this will be needed!)
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19716>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Disconnect_DEOs_from_Servers Integer DoAllMode
19718>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (DoAllMode <> DETACH_NEVER) Begin
19720>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If ( DoAllMode=DETACH_ALWAYS or ; // do all no matter what                ( (Changed_state(Self)=0) and ;                ( (DoAllMode=DETACH_IF_NO_CHANGE) or  ;                (Static_Server_State(Self)) ) ) ) ;                Send Remove_deo_from_server
19723>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (Has_Components_State(Self)) ;                Broadcast Send Disconnect_DEOs_from_Servers DoAllMode
19727>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19727>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19727>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19728>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19728>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Changed to not remove from server if static.
19728>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Remove_Object
19730>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send remove_object
19732>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // remove if not static and no changes
19732>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If ( Static_Server_State(Self)=0 and ;            Changed_State(Self)=0 ) ;  // only detach if unchanged!            Send remove_DEO_from_server
19735>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (JJT) Changed so that this respects Change_disabled_state. I don't
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //       like this here but its the best I can think of. Therefore, all
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //       objects using server.pkg must understand Change_disabled_state.
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (JJT) Checks deferred_state and if set do not change the
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // changed state of the server object. This had been in datalist and is
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // required to make deferred_state work right. Deferred_state was created
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to make selection-lists work correctly and as far as I am concerned it
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // should be the only supported use of this. Therefore, I would not *ever*
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // expect deferred_state to be set true in tables, entry_forms, or text_
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // windows. Since deferred-state is known to this mixin the change
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // belongs here - but I expect it to only ever change behaviors in
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // selection-lists.
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Changed to not remove from server if static.
19736>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Changed_State Integer newVal
19738>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer srvr# wsrvr
19738>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If not (Change_Disabled_State(Self)) Begin
19740>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Forward Set Changed_State to newVal
19742>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get server to srvr#
19743>>>>>>>>>>>>>            
19743>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if deferred keep the server out of it.
19743>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If not (deferred_State(Self)) Begin
19745>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If (newVal and srvr#) Begin
19747>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Set Changed_State of srvr# to True
19748>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    // We also set changed_state of all "foreign" servers. These
19748>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    // are the ones whose Data_File is a parent File
19748>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to wsrvr
19749>>>>>>>>>>>>>                    If wsrvr ;                        Set Changed_State of wSrvr to True
19752>>>>>>>>>>>>>                End
19752>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19752>>>>>>>>>>>>>                
19752>>>>>>>>>>>>>                // Remove is changed-state=false, not active and not static
19752>>>>>>>>>>>>>                If ( not(newVal) and not(Active_State(Self)) and ;                    not(Static_Server_State(Self)) ) ;                    Send remove_DEO_from_Server
19755>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
19755>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19755>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
19755>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19755>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
19756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // When an object is created this sets the default value for
19756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Static_Server_state. If a parent DEO exists it will use its
19756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // static_server_state property. An Entry_view_Client0 object sets
19756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // this - this way view based daf programs will use the new behavior
19756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (although it can be disabled)  but non-daf programs will work like
19756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // they always did.
19756>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Default_Static_Server_State Returns Integer
19758>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer rVal
19758>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // We delegate to get the actual (not default) static state
19758>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Note: Can't check with component_state - it not defined yet
19758>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Delegate Get Static_Server_State to rVal
19760>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return rVal
19761>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
19762>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
19762>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This adds every parent DDO for the passed DDO to the DEO's list of DDOs to watch.
19762>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // It adds the parents and then does this recursively up the DDO tree.
19762>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This means that this DEO will respond to any DD change for any server. This does not
19762>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure WatchAllParentServers Handle hoDDO
19764>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoSrvr
19764>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iServer iServers
19764>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_Set_Server_Count of hoDDO to iServers
19765>>>>>>>>>>>>>        For iServer from 0 to (iServers-1)
19771>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19771>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Data_Set_Server of hoDDO iServer to hoSrvr
19772>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Add_Watched_Server hoSrvr
19773>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers hoSrvr
19774>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Loop
19775>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
19775>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
