25679>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25679>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This only gets called when the developer is killing this object. During application
25679>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // shut-down, only destroy_object is called. This augmentation destroys the watched broadcaster
25679>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // (which is sitting on the desktop). During program shut down we don't care if this is called
25679>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // because it is getting destroyed anyway. We are making the assumption that a developer controlled
25679>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // destroy will always be called with the watcher still existing.
25679>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Destroy
25681>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatched
25681>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Changed_State to False //   is this really needed anymore???
25682>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The watched server, must still exist.
25682>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatched
25683>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
25685>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
25686>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the broadcaster
25687>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25687>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25687>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // if non 0, The bound watched server, must still exist.
25687>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get ChangedStateWatched_Servers to hoWatched
25688>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatched Begin
25690>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set Broadcast_State of hoWatched to False
25691>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Destroy of hoWatched     // destroy the broadcaster
25692>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25692>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25692>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Forward Send Destroy
25694>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
25695>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25695>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Required DD/DEO interface
25695>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // sent by DD before a find and save. We only care about DD finds which
25695>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // means DoAll is 1
25695>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Entry_Update Integer iFile Integer iDoAll
25697>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure scans the fields of this object's items to determine
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   what other database agents (data_sets) other than this object's Server
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   should be 'watched' (for data changes).
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   iTableFlag is a boolean determining whether this object relies on a
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   prototype row (TRUE) or an item list (FALSE).
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   [JVH] VDF 17.0 - Ignored in this class.
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This object must understand pbDataBindable, and have a private
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   boolean property named Private_pbServersScanned to note the event.
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Notes
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure is invoked once per object, the first time the object
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   is activated.  If the data_file, data_field, and/or main_file of this
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   object are changed (don't change them while this object is active!),
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set Private_pbServersScanned to FALSE to force this object to scan
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   again (when it is next activated).
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 17.0: The logic has been retooled to add more watched servers to the DDOs. This is done so
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // DD operations will send Refresh to these additional watched-servers. There are two changes:
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 1. Containers are now made watched servers for the Server and all parent servers
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // 2. Non-file.field DEOs (e.g., expressions) are made watched servers for the server (which it
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    already did and for all parent servers. Without this, parent entry_item expressions were not
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //    getting updated
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Here is how watched-servers works.
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Each DEO attaches and detaches from its Server by sending Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to the server DD. Once attached, the DD knows about this DEO and sends messages to it as needed (Refresh,
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // Entry_Update, etc.). In addition, a DEO may need to attach a parent DDO so that changes in that parent DD
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // results in those messages being sent. This is needed if the binding table in entry_item refers to a parent
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // table. So we need to send Add_User_interface and Remove_User_interface to that parent server as well. If a DEO
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // has multiple, there could be multiple parent servers. As of 17.0, we are also attaching to parent servers if
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // we are unsure about how the DEO is being used. If an expression is used, it might need to be updated when
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // a parent (or any ancestor) changes. Each DEO keeps track of servers that it attaches to and this is referred
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // to as the watched_server list. This list is maintained so the DEO knows which DDOs to attach and detach to.
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // [JVH] VDF 17.1 cWebAppDEOServer_mixin Notes:
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // - Modified to support only 1 item per control. Get Item_Count interface not supported.
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // - Modified to not support the Prototype_Object interface (old windows Table class).
25698>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Find_Servers_To_Watch Integer iTableFlag
25700>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iFileNum iServerFile
25700>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer hoDataSet
25700>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bDataBindable
25700>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25700>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get pbDataBindable to bDataBindable
25701>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Private_pbServersScanned to True
25702>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
25703>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25703>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer = 0) Begin
25705>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
25706>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25706>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25706>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25706>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Delete_Watched_Servers  // empty Watched_Servers broadcaster first
25707>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Main_File of hoServer to iServerFile  // data-set's main-file
25708>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25708>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (not(bDataBindable)) Begin
25710>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // containers should get added to all parent DDOs
25710>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers hoServer
25711>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Procedure_Return
25712>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25712>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25712>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25712>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Data_File to iFileNum
25713>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // we need watched server if file exists, it is not the main file
25713>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // and is not an updating file (as opposed to updating data-set).
25713>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (iFileNum > 0 and iFileNum <> iServerFile) Begin
25715>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Which_Data_Set of hoServer iFileNum to hoDataSet
25716>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (hoDataSet <> 0 and hoDataSet <> hoServer) Begin
25718>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Add_Watched_Server hoDataSet
25719>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Add_ChangedStateWatched_Server hoDataSet
25720>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
25720>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25720>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25720>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25720>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else If (iFileNum = 0) Begin
25723>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // if no file (e.g., expression) we don't know when it changes so we tell all servers
25723>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            // that this is a watcher
25723>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send WatchAllParentServers hoServer
25724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25724>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
25725>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25725>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function returns the object id of the database agent of this object,
25725>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // or 0.
25725>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Locate_Server Returns Integer
25727>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer
25727>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
25728>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoServer
25729>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
25730>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25730>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Refresh Integer eMode
25732>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
25733>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25733>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure discontinues the connection between this object and its
25733>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   database agent(s) (Server and Watched_Servers).
25733>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Remove_DEO_From_Server
25735>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoServer hoWatchedServers
25735>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25735>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
25736>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25736>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer <> 0) Begin
25738>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to hoServer Self
25739>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25739>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25739>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25739>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Only send if watched-server exists
25739>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
25740>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25740>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
25742>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Send Remove_User_Interface to hoWatchedServers Self True // TRUE for watchers
25743>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25743>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25743>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25743>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // when removed the deo is no longer up to date.
25743>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Refresh_Dirty_State to True
25744>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
25745>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25745>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure removes the specified object id (hoServer) from this object's
25745>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   set of database agents who are merely 'watched', and destroys the
25745>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   connection between the database agent and this object.
25745>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Remove_Watched_Server Integer hoServer
25747>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer iIndex
25747>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoWatchedServers
25747>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25747>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Watched_Servers to hoWatchedServers
25748>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        // Only if w server exists
25748>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If hoWatchedServers Begin
25750>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to False
25751>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get find_element of hoWatchedServers hoServer to iIndex
25752>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iIndex >= 0) Begin
25754>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send remove_element to hoWatchedServers hoServer
25755>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
25755>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25755>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set broadcast_state of hoWatchedServers to True
25756>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (iIndex >= 0 and Active_State(Self)) Begin
25758>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Remove_User_Interface to hoServer Self True // TRUE for watchers
25759>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
25759>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25759>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25759>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25759>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
25760>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25760>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function returns the object id of the database agent of this object, or 0.
25760>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // If this object's Server is 0, this object's parent's Server is returned, if any.
25760>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This function is used to allow nested data-entry objects to use the
25760>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // database agent defined by their parent object.
25760>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function Server Returns Integer
25762>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer hoServer
25762>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private_Server to hoServer
25763>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer = 0) Begin
25765>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Function_Return (Locate_Server(parent(Self)))
25766>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25766>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25766>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoServer
25767>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
25768>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25768>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // This procedure sets the value of the Server property of this object,
25768>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // notifying child-objects of the change, and destroying and creating
25768>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // connections with database agents, as required.
25768>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // If the Server of this object is changed while this object is inactive,
25768>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // no notification of child-objects is required or performed.
25768>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Set Server Integer newVal
25770>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer oldVal
25770>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25770>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Set Explicit_Server_State to (newVal <> 0)
25771>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to oldVal
25772>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25772>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (newVal <> 0) Begin
25774>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set private_Server to (object_id(newVal))
25775>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25775>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25775>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Else Begin
25776>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Set private_Server to newVal
25777>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25777>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25777>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25777>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (Active_State(Self)) Begin
25779>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Broadcast Send server_changed oldVal newVal
25781>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (oldVal <> 0) Begin
25783>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Remove_DEO_From_Server  // detach from current server
25784>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
25784>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25784>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newval <> 0) Begin
25786>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Send Attach_Deo_To_Server    // attach to new server
25787>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
25787>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25787>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25787>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25787>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
25788>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25788>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure servers as notification of a change in the connection
25788>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   of this object's parent to its database agent.  If this object uses
25788>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   its parent's database agent by default (see the Server and Find_Server
25788>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   functions, above), it must disconnect from the old agent and connect
25788>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   with the new agent.
25788>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Server_Changed Integer oldVal Integer newVal
25790>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Integer oldSrvr
25790>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        
25790>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get private_Server to oldSrvr
25791>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (oldSrvr = 0) Begin  //assumes Server(self) = oldVal by deleg
25793>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (oldVal <> 0) ;                Send remove_user_interface to oldVal Self
25796>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (newVal <> 0) ;                Send add_user_interface to newVal Self
25799>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25799>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25799>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
25800>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25800>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    // return the DEO that sets the server
25800>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Function ServerDEO Returns Handle
25802>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Handle hoServer hoServerDeo
25802>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Boolean bExplicitServer
25802>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Get Server to hoServer
25803>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        If (hoServer) Begin
25805>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Get Explicit_Server_State to bExplicitServer
25806>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            If (bExplicitServer) Begin
25808>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Move Self to hoServerDeo
25809>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
25809>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25809>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            Else Begin
25810>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>                Delegate Get ServerDEO to hoServerDeo
25812>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>            End
25812>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25812>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        End
25812>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
25812>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Function_Return hoServerDeo
25813>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Function
25814>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
25814>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   This procedure causes the scanning of this object's items' fields,
25814>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    //   and the production of a set of database agents who should be 'watched'.
25814>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    Procedure Scan_Servers
25816>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>        Send Find_Servers_To_Watch False
25817>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    End_Procedure
25818>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>    
