31330>>>>>// Models a data entry view panel. This is a container for...
31330>>>>>// - A DDO structure
31330>>>>>// - Panel layout
31330>>>>>// - Child DEO and non-DEO controls.
31330>>>>>//
31330>>>>>// Adds support for...
31330>>>>>// - DDO Container,
31330>>>>>// - DDO request interface
31330>>>>>Class cWebView is a cWebWindow
31331>>>>>    
31331>>>>>    Procedure Construct_Object
31333>>>>>        Integer eStyle 
31333>>>>>        String sName
31333>>>>>        
31333>>>>>        Forward Send Construct_Object
31335>>>>>        
31335>>>>>        
31335>>>>>        
31335>>>>>        // this determines if request_save should validate all items or stop at the first error. The default
31335>>>>>        // for web applicaitions is to validate all.
31335>>>>>        // For now this is private, as this may never be needed.  
31335>>>>>        Property Boolean pbRequesteValidateAll True
31336>>>>>
31336>>>>>        // This is set to true during SyncDDOs, specifically while trying to re-establish the DDO's Field_Defaults.
31336>>>>>        // Typically the flag is used to protect DEO's during this process so that the Field_Default is re-established
31336>>>>>        // only in the actual DDO (where it is needed) and not in the DEO (where the value may have changed already).        
31336>>>>>        Property Boolean pbSynchingFieldDefaults False
31337>>>>>        
31337>>>>>        Property Boolean pbFindKeys True
31338>>>>>        Property Boolean pbClearKeys True
31339>>>>>        Property Boolean pbDeleteKeys True
31340>>>>>        Property Boolean pbSaveKeys True
31341>>>>>        
31341>>>>>        // set true if constrain_file change in data dictionaries for each client instance
31341>>>>>        // This is only applied with drilldown style views
31341>>>>>        Property Boolean pbDrillDownDynamicConstraints True 
31342>>>>>        
31342>>>>>        
31342>>>>>        
31342>>>>>        // Published Properties
31342>>>>>        Property Boolean pbServerOnSubmit False    // Set to true to trigger server OnSubmit event
31345>>>>>        Property String psClientOnSubmit ""        // Name of client side OnSubmit event handler
31348>>>>>        
31348>>>>>        Property Boolean pbServerOnResizeWindow False
31351>>>>>        Property String psClientOnResizeWindow ""
31354>>>>>         
31354>>>>>        Property Boolean pbFillHeight False
31357>>>>>        
31357>>>>>        // this gets set during object construction by looking at the cWebApp's application type.  
31357>>>>>        Property Integer peWebViewStyle wvsDesktop
31358>>>>>
31358>>>>>        Property Integer peViewType vtUndefined   // General purpose of this view: i.e. vtZoom or vtSelect
31359>>>>>        
31359>>>>>        // if drillDown should Request_Save attempt to save a new unchanged record?
31359>>>>>        // with drill down this makes the most sense. With Desktop style this is ignored.
31359>>>>>        // Currently marked private. Might be exposed if it turns out to be needed
31359>>>>>        Property Boolean pbAlwaysSaveWhenNewDrillDown True
31360>>>>>
31360>>>>>        // what to do when closing a changed view. This is called by
31360>>>>>        // GetChangedViewExitAction, which can be augmented to handle more dynamic actions
31360>>>>>        Property Integer peChangedViewExitAction cveConfirmSaveClearCancel
31361>>>>>        
31361>>>>>        Property Handle Verify_SaveClearCancel_msg (RefProc(SaveClearCancelConfirmation))
31362>>>>>
31362>>>>>        Property String psNavigateDataCallbackObj ""   // Private: Used by NavigateClose_Callback. Stores the callback object to populate the navigate data when navigating back. This is usually the object that invoked NavigateBack
31365>>>>>        
31365>>>>>        Property tWebNavigateData pNavigateData
31368>>>>>
31368>>>>>        Property String psNavigateBackView
31371>>>>>
31371>>>>>        Property String psInvokingObject ""        
31374>>>>>        
31374>>>>>        Property String psInvokingStateHash ""          //  Used to store the state hash of the invoking view for drill-down
31377>>>>>        Property Boolean pbNavReinitError False         //  Used to communicate issues back to NavigateInitialize
31378>>>>>        Property Boolean pbNavigating False           //  True while inside navigation messages
31379>>>>>        Property Boolean pbInitForShow False         //  True while inside initforshow
31380>>>>>        
31380>>>>>        Property Boolean pbStateRestoreRecord True      //  If true record ids will be part of the state hash for desktop-style
31381>>>>>        Property Boolean pbStateReplace False           //  If true the current view will not add a new history item but replace the current item in history
31382>>>>>        Property Integer peStateMode vsmDefault         //  Configures how the state hash for this view built
31383>>>>>        Property String psStateNewRecordId ""           //  Configures how new records will be represented in the state hash
31384>>>>>
31384>>>>>        
31384>>>>>        /*        A view is preloaded using delayloadview, this basically puts the view 'in sync' but it         loads the view details later. This is an optimization added for history management where it         has to rebuild the entire view stack for drill down applications. It now only fully loads         the visible view and the others are loaded in the background using delayloadview, but it         does need to refind records so InitForShow is already executed and should not be executed         again. pbPreLoaded indicates that it should skip InitForShow.                */
31384>>>>>        Property Boolean pbPreLoaded False
31387>>>>>                
31387>>>>>        Get Object_Label to sName
31388>>>>>        Property String psStateViewName sName
31389>>>>>               
