32781>>>>>    // This is an event hook sent to a view during NavigateForward. 
32781>>>>>    // You can augment this event to modify the view based on the 
32781>>>>>    // navigation context that is passed in the NavigateData parameter.
32781>>>>>    //
32781>>>>>    // You would typically use this event when a view is re-used in 
32781>>>>>    // different contexts within your application and you would like 
32781>>>>>    // to modify the appearance and features of the view accordingly.
32781>>>>>    Procedure OnNavigateForward tWebNavigateData NavigateData Handle hoInvokingView Handle hoInvokingObject
32783>>>>>    End_Procedure
32784>>>>>    
32784>>>>>    // Callback handler for the Show function used when navigating into a desktop view with the 
32784>>>>>    // drilldown model. It adds the view to the stack, now that we know for sure that it is in sync.
32784>>>>>    Procedure Show_CallBack Handle hoView
32786>>>>>        Send PushView to (ViewStack(Self)) hoView nfUndefined
32787>>>>>    End_Procedure
32788>>>>>
32788>>>>>    // This is overridden to handle desktop and drill down views.
32788>>>>>    // 1. if this is a dialog or if there is no stack, it just does a normal show
32788>>>>>    // dfirst Clear the view stack down as far as the default
32788>>>>>    // view, then load this view.
32788>>>>>    //
32788>>>>>    // Note: Augmenting this here means two things:
32788>>>>>    // 1. The application already supports the View Stack (drill-down)
32788>>>>>    // 2. That the Show command in the superclass does -not- try to manipulate the view stack.  
32788>>>>>    Procedure Show
32790>>>>>        Handle hoDefaultView hoTopView
32790>>>>>        Integer eWebViewStyle
32790>>>>>        Boolean bOK bUnconditional
32790>>>>>        Get peWebViewStyle to eWebViewStyle
32791>>>>>        If ((ViewStack(Self))=0 or eWebViewStyle=wvsDialog) Begin
32793>>>>>            Forward Send Show
32795>>>>>        End
32795>>>>>>
32795>>>>>        Else If (eWebViewStyle = wvsDesktop) Begin
32798>>>>>            Get GetDefaultView to hoDefaultView
32799>>>>>            Get TopViewHandle of (ViewStack(Self)) to hoTopView
32800>>>>>            Move (hoTopView=0 or peWebViewStyle(hoTopView)=wvsDesktop) to bUnconditional
32801>>>>>            Get Reset of (ViewStack(Self)) True bUnconditional to bOK
32802>>>>>            If bOK Begin
32804>>>>>                // if a non-drilldown just show and add to view stack
32804>>>>>                Send SetInvokingObject 0
32805>>>>>                Send ShowView to (Host(Self)) Self (RefProc(Show_CallBack)) Self
32806>>>>>            End
32806>>>>>>
32806>>>>>        End
32806>>>>>>
32806>>>>>        // moving to a drill down view - same as NavigateBegin
32806>>>>>        Else Begin
32807>>>>>            Send NavigatePathBegin Self False
32808>>>>>        End
32808>>>>>>
32808>>>>>    End_Procedure
32809>>>>>
32809>>>>>
32809>>>>>    // Send this to update psInvokingView of this view to the name of the next view down
32809>>>>>    // in the view stack. Also, psInvokingView of this next view down is set to "".
32809>>>>>    // This ensures that Only to top view in the view stack and its invoking view are synchronized.
32809>>>>>    // The view that receives this message should be the top view in the view stack. 
32809>>>>>    Procedure UpdateInvokingViewDrillDownStyle
32811>>>>>        Handle hoInvokingView
32811>>>>>        String sInvokingView
32811>>>>>        
32811>>>>>        Get InvokingViewHandle of (ViewStack(Self)) to hoInvokingView
32812>>>>>        
32812>>>>>        If (hoInvokingView = 0) Begin
32814>>>>>            Move "" to sInvokingView
32815>>>>>        End
32815>>>>>>
32815>>>>>        Else Begin
32816>>>>>            Get WebObjectName of hoInvokingView to sInvokingView
32817>>>>>            WebSet psInvokingView of hoInvokingView to ""
32818>>>>>        End
32818>>>>>>
32818>>>>>        
32818>>>>>        WebSet psInvokingView to sInvokingView
32819>>>>>    End_Procedure
